                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-181/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"34\" data-end=\"37\">\r\n<p data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"91\">Walter paused for a moment and opened his eyes wide.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"93\" data-end=\"167\">He told me that the reinforcement work was finished, and that he was here.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"169\" data-end=\"200\">How could I accept those words?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"275\">\"…Are you trying to tell me that I can’t suppress Miss Harnette’s magic?\"</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"277\" data-end=\"415\">“I may be misunderstanding something, but I need to say this. Even if the president can withstand my magic, this building might collapse.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"417\" data-end=\"515\">“We completed the reinforcement work first. For Dalian, it only took a moment… Isn’t that enough?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"599\">“I’m not used to this power yet. I don’t want to cause problems, even by mistake.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"601\" data-end=\"667\">“You’re not saying this because you’re underestimating me, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"669\" data-end=\"794\">“If I underestimated the president, I wouldn’t have come here. The president of the society is the Cetinos Quasar, isn’t he?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"796\" data-end=\"906\">Harnette had personally witnessed Walter and the president using magic in the battle against the slime dragon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"908\" data-end=\"1041\">There were many spells mixed together and interfering with her vision, but among them, she could at least distinguish Walter’s magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1144\">Among all the spells, the concentration of magical power was extremely strong—powerful and ferocious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1146\" data-end=\"1191\">“You must have seen my magic clearly, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1193\" data-end=\"1264\">“Yes, I definitely saw it. I understand why he’s called the Blue Sage.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1266\" data-end=\"1329\">“Even so… do you really think the Magic Society will collapse?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1331\" data-end=\"1503\">“Even the president must have seen my magic. If the color of the flames has changed, that means its properties have changed. I don’t know how these properties will behave.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1594\">Of course, Harnette had a rough understanding of the power contained in the golden flame.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1596\" data-end=\"1670\">It purified evil enemies with heat, and caressed the innocent with warmth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1782\">That was why, even though the slime dragon was engulfed in flames, the fire didn’t spread to the surroundings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1784\" data-end=\"1832\">“That makes sense. Then you’d better hold back.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1834\" data-end=\"1898\">Walter put on a serious expression and released a chilling cold.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1900\" data-end=\"1992\">The cold air spread in an instant, reaching toward Zion and the scholars watching from afar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1994\" data-end=\"2062\">Yet Harnette waited until the magic settled without moving a muscle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2064\" data-end=\"2112\">‘I froze the training room with freezing magic.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2114\" data-end=\"2196\">The cold created by Walter seeped everywhere—across the ceiling, floor, and walls.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2198\" data-end=\"2286\">Eventually, a thin layer of ice formed, wrapping around the inside of the training room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2351\">The freezing spell was meant to weaken the power of fire magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2353\" data-end=\"2404\">“Hmm… It might be good to add one more layer here.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2406\" data-end=\"2452\">Walter quietly muttered and shifted his magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2454\" data-end=\"2540\">A gust of wind blew, and soon the pressure of the wind weakened and calmed completely.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2542\" data-end=\"2607\">Harnette made eye contact with Zion and her eyes conveyed relief.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2609\" data-end=\"2672\">“With this, the building won’t collapse. No one will get hurt.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2674\" data-end=\"2748\">Inside the training room, wind roared and circulated around the icy walls.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2750\" data-end=\"2850\">Even if magic clashed, the wind would block it first, and then the cold air would absorb the impact.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"2978\">Even if both were overcome and the force struck the walls, the reinforcement work would still hold—they wouldn’t be scratched.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2980\" data-end=\"3026\">“You’re amazing. I didn’t even think of that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3028\" data-end=\"3157\">“This might be because I handle all magical elements. Isn’t competing with Miss Harnette only possible with this kind of talent?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3159\" data-end=\"3220\">No mage other than Walter could wield all magical attributes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3222\" data-end=\"3284\">At most, two attributes were the limit, and most had only one.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3286\" data-end=\"3384\">On top of that, differences in magic levels and mana capacity ensured no one could surpass Walter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3386\" data-end=\"3468\">Yet for the first time, Walter felt fear—and excitement—that he might fall behind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3470\" data-end=\"3518\">‘…It feels like I’ve become a challenger again.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3520\" data-end=\"3597\">Since childhood, Walter had no interest in winning battles or killing demons.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3599\" data-end=\"3676\">He only wondered how high he could climb, and how many mages stood above him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3678\" data-end=\"3778\">In the end, within a few years, he became the strongest mage and earned the title of Cetinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3780\" data-end=\"3819\">“It's sad and joyful at the same time.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3821\" data-end=\"3918\">Walter diligently fulfilled his duties as Cetinos Quasar, yet he was always haunted by emptiness.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3920\" data-end=\"3992\">If it had taken longer or required suffering, he might have accepted it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3994\" data-end=\"4059\">But because he obtained it too easily, he felt it had no meaning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4061\" data-end=\"4122\">Maybe that was why he hoped for a mage who could surpass him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4124\" data-end=\"4154\">‘It’s not that I lack talent…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4156\" data-end=\"4224\">Walter never envied others’ talent, though he admired their efforts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4226\" data-end=\"4280\">As far as magical talent went, no one could match him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4282\" data-end=\"4332\">Yet before Harnette, even that seemed meaningless.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4334\" data-end=\"4385\">‘I may not have what she has… but I won’t give up.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4387\" data-end=\"4438\">Effort and time don’t always bring desired results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4440\" data-end=\"4504\">You may wander for years in failure, frustration, and confusion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4506\" data-end=\"4568\">But without going through that process, you can’t rise higher.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4570\" data-end=\"4622\">The higher you climb, the more challenges await you.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4624\" data-end=\"4660\">‘That is the heart of a challenger.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4662\" data-end=\"4726\">Walter respectfully controlled his magic and looked at Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4728\" data-end=\"4768\">Harnette still hadn’t released her mana.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4770\" data-end=\"4827\">Perhaps she worried about something besides the building.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4829\" data-end=\"4867\">“…Are you worried about the darkness?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4869\" data-end=\"4907\">Harnette flinched and looked confused.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4909\" data-end=\"4969\">Zion could now move fine, but his treatment wasn’t complete.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4971\" data-end=\"5064\">He had come with her, saying he could walk lightly, but this situation had come unexpectedly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5066\" data-end=\"5166\">“You said your recovery isn’t complete, right? Your power seems unstable. If you’re really worried…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5168\" data-end=\"5209\">“I’m fine. Sister, do whatever you want.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5211\" data-end=\"5269\">Zion gave a firm answer so she wouldn’t hold back anymore.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5271\" data-end=\"5367\">Walter carefully strengthened his magic, perfectly protecting the interior of the training room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5369\" data-end=\"5490\">Moreover, the method was designed to withstand intense fire magic—it should be able to block Brecht’s flames for a while.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5492\" data-end=\"5497\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5499\" data-end=\"5555\">Harnette, deep in thought, gradually increased her mana.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5557\" data-end=\"5603\">She didn’t intend to avoid confronting Walter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5605\" data-end=\"5647\">She was simply unsure of her own strength.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5649\" data-end=\"5680\">‘Will I be able to do it well?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5682\" data-end=\"5732\">Brecht’s response surfaced alongside her question.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5734\" data-end=\"5805\">It wasn’t human speech, and only Harnette could understand its meaning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5807\" data-end=\"5821\">‘…Is that so?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5823\" data-end=\"5921\">At some point, Harnette began suppressing the golden fire, letting it flow through her whole body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5923\" data-end=\"5986\">The ice on the floor melted, and the surrounding cold vanished.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5988\" data-end=\"6036\">Walter held back a smile and released more cold.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6038\" data-end=\"6066\">‘It shouldn’t reach others.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6068\" data-end=\"6136\">Of course, there would be no harm even if it touched a living being.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6138\" data-end=\"6193\">If it wasn’t an enemy, no wounds or burns would appear.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6195\" data-end=\"6286\">She simply lacked confidence in distinguishing properly for now, so she was being cautious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6288\" data-end=\"6295\">‘Zion…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6297\" data-end=\"6367\">Whenever something happened, Zion was the first to appear in her mind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6369\" data-end=\"6444\">After nearly dying twice, she could no longer tolerate his being in danger.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6446\" data-end=\"6518\">If it were Zion, he would risk his life a third, fourth, and fifth time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6520\" data-end=\"6573\">The golden fire grew stronger and its reach expanded.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6575\" data-end=\"6649\">Wherever it passed, ice melted instantly, and the cold could not approach.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6651\" data-end=\"6711\">Walter watched the flame closely, feeling something strange.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6713\" data-end=\"6728\">‘It’s not hot.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6730\" data-end=\"6796\">If it were typical fire magic, it would burn everything with heat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6798\" data-end=\"6877\">But this magic—the golden flame—radiated warmth and only repelled cold and ice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6879\" data-end=\"6959\">In other words, it only attacked elements considered “enemies” within its range.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6961\" data-end=\"7030\">‘I’m not the enemy, so why is the magic I used being treated as one?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7032\" data-end=\"7079\">Given the circumstances, it couldn’t be helped.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7081\" data-end=\"7149\">This wasn’t a life-or-death battle—it was a test of one’s abilities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7151\" data-end=\"7225\">That was why he was leaving the mage alone and simply adjusting his magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7227\" data-end=\"7293\">‘This magic is terrifying. I couldn’t imitate it even if I tried.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7295\" data-end=\"7362\">It wasn’t easy to distinguish each target within the spell’s range.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7364\" data-end=\"7463\">If he focused too much on that, the magic’s power would weaken, or the spell might cancel entirely.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7465\" data-end=\"7512\">Perhaps this too fell into the realm of talent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7514\" data-end=\"7565\">‘I think I’ve lost all my other magical strengths…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7567\" data-end=\"7599\">But even that didn’t matter now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7601\" data-end=\"7669\">Those characteristics made her magic perfectly optimized for combat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7671\" data-end=\"7761\">No matter where allies were or what they were doing, the flames would target enemies only.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7763\" data-end=\"7812\">She could execute countless strategies with this.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7814\" data-end=\"7878\">With deception, she could completely crush the enemy’s momentum.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7880\" data-end=\"7907\">‘I can’t ignore her power…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7909\" data-end=\"7968\">A single spark had made four great calamities howl in pain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7970\" data-end=\"8018\">And the flames didn’t spread to trees or bushes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8020\" data-end=\"8080\">It targeted only one enemy while protecting everything else.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8082\" data-end=\"8168\">Most of the ice on the floor had melted, and even the wind could not erase the flames.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8170\" data-end=\"8228\">Facing the golden fire with cold was barely delaying time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8230\" data-end=\"8319\">To defeat Harnette, he would have to use irregular elemental magic and find her weakness.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8321\" data-end=\"8351\">‘This is the limit of Dalian.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8353\" data-end=\"8404\">Walter gathered his magic and dispelled his spells.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8406\" data-end=\"8451\">It felt like standing before an immense wall.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8453\" data-end=\"8515\">Even if he devoted his entire life to surpassing it, could he?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8517\" data-end=\"8532\">“I’m defeated.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8534\" data-end=\"8582\">“Huh? Oh no, wasn’t one of you supposed to win?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8584\" data-end=\"8654\">Harnette couldn’t hide her embarrassment as she extinguished the fire.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8656\" data-end=\"8712\">It had been a great duel, and the outcome meant nothing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8714\" data-end=\"8769\">Yet Walter was the first to step back and admit defeat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8771\" data-end=\"8830\">“I didn’t know enough. It’s late, but I want to apologize.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8832\" data-end=\"8889\">“There’s no need to apologize. I wanted to try this too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8891\" data-end=\"8900\">“…I see.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8902\" data-end=\"8959\">Walter was satisfied with her answer and glanced at Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8961\" data-end=\"9016\">Zion stood quietly as though he knew this would happen.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9018\" data-end=\"9052\">As expected—but unexpectedly, too.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9054\" data-end=\"9076\">‘Black lacks nothing.’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9078\" data-end=\"9083\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9085\" data-end=\"9123\">The royal castle, the sleeping palace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9125\" data-end=\"9184\">Brandis was swirling his glass, admiring the dim moonlight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9186\" data-end=\"9292\">It had been a long time since he rested, and the bitter taste of the alcohol seemed to linger in his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9294\" data-end=\"9367\">But he always drank alone—there weren’t many he could comfortably invite.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9369\" data-end=\"9407\">‘I can’t recommend alcohol to Glonet.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9409\" data-end=\"9501\">He couldn’t tell someone holding the position of Royal Knight Commander to neglect his duty.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9503\" data-end=\"9575\">He always needed to guard the king and keep his mind sharp, sword ready.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9577\" data-end=\"9644\">Though they were like old friends, their roles prevented closeness.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9646\" data-end=\"9667\">‘Will he arrive now?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9669\" data-end=\"9703\">At that moment, one window opened.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9705\" data-end=\"9758\">Brandis calmly set down his glass and poured another.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9760\" data-end=\"9821\">“…Your Majesty, I have carried out your orders and returned.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9823\" data-end=\"9855\">“You worked hard. Want a drink?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9857\" data-end=\"9906\">Caden bowed respectfully and sat across from him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9908\" data-end=\"9960\">He removed his mask and politely accepted the drink.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9962\" data-end=\"9982\">“Did you reap many?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9984\" data-end=\"10102\">“Yes, Your Majesty. I mainly eliminated those obstructing the front lines, and I completed reconnaissance as ordered.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10104\" data-end=\"10163\">“I received reports from Jasaek. It was quite the rampage.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10165\" data-end=\"10201\">Brandis smiled and sipped his drink.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10203\" data-end=\"10269\">Caden bowed again, then lifted his glass and drained it in one go.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10271\" data-end=\"10322\">“I merely did my best to honor Miss Brandis’s day.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10324\" data-end=\"10371\">“Yes, that’s something I should be able to do.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10373\" data-end=\"10417\">Even the name of the lamb felt familiar now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10419\" data-end=\"10492\">Perhaps he had accepted the person named Caden Aslower without realizing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10494\" data-end=\"10539\">Was this too influenced by Zion and Harnette?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10541\" data-end=\"10580\">“…There’s something I want to ask you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10582\" data-end=\"10607\">“I will answer anything.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10609\" data-end=\"10696\">“I want to appoint Harnette Adelaira as a Cetinos Quasar… I want to hear your opinion.”</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"10698\" data-end=\"10701\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-182/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"34\" data-end=\"37\">\r\n<p data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"69\">Kaden couldn’t open his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"71\" data-end=\"133\">Zion had already become active as a member of Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"135\" data-end=\"246\">Besides that, with so many restrictions placed on Hannett, I wondered whether the officials would object first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"248\" data-end=\"330\">“…Hannette Adelaira is a fiancée with dark skin. Wouldn’t that cause controversy?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"332\" data-end=\"438\">“She’s also the daughter of Duke Adelaira. There will be voices saying, ‘Wouldn’t that empower the Duke?’”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"512\">Brandis looked toward the not-too-distant future and set down his glass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"600\">Originally, he had considered granting the title of Setinos Quasar to Hannett as well.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"602\" data-end=\"701\">However, since she was engaged to Zion, there would inevitably be overlapping issues in many ways.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"703\" data-end=\"759\">“Shouldn’t you choose the Black one over the other two?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"869\">“I chose Black to persuade them. If Hannette Adelaira were chosen, would the bureaucrats really stay quiet?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"931\">Each of the royal officials belonged to a different faction.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"1084\">Duke Adelaira, Duke Ternane—people who didn’t wish to be bound to either side—and those who wanted loyalty to the king or directly to the royal family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1203\">Originally, the scales didn’t tilt either way, but as Zion and Hannett grew stronger, the balance began to collapse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1205\" data-end=\"1263\">“I don’t know the whole situation, but I’m just guessing.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1265\" data-end=\"1281\">“Guessing what?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1283\" data-end=\"1408\">“The Adelaira ducal family will surely grow larger than before. Won’t the nobles try to align themselves with Duke Adelaira?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1453\">“…However, Duke Adelaira has indeed grown.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1455\" data-end=\"1515\">Not only Brandis—many nobles and officials hadn’t forgotten.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1594\">Long ago, a duke used their power to manipulate the succession to the throne.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1596\" data-end=\"1698\">If that duke hadn’t been expelled, Brandis would never have been born, much less inherited the throne.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1700\" data-end=\"1829\">“This must never happen again. If it does, things will end quickly… If twisted the wrong way, the Alain Kingdom could be shaken.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1831\" data-end=\"1873\">“Are you trying to cut off Duke Adelaira?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1875\" data-end=\"1926\">Kaden faced the reality and expressed deep concern.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1928\" data-end=\"2007\">Brandis needed to govern as king and protect the authority of the royal family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2009\" data-end=\"2119\">If someone threatened his own position and that of future generations, he would end it by any means necessary.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2121\" data-end=\"2210\">“Then let me ask you. What do you think would happen if I sever ties with Duke Adelaira?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2212\" data-end=\"2375\">“The power of several nobles would collapse, and Duke Ternane’s power would grow. Many are loyal to Your Majesty, but mixed with fear and dread. More importantly…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2377\" data-end=\"2411\">Kaden looked at Brandis seriously.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2413\" data-end=\"2494\">Brandis, sensing that atmosphere, was momentarily overwhelmed by strange tension.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2496\" data-end=\"2594\">“You would have to abandon Black and Harnett Adelaira. Your Majesty would suffer enormous damage.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2596\" data-end=\"2633\">Kaden’s voice carried heavy pressure.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2635\" data-end=\"2708\">And because he even used the term “Your Majesty,” it was clearly sincere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2710\" data-end=\"2743\">“Damage… Is that what you think?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2745\" data-end=\"2911\">“Your Majesty, Black and Harnett Adelaira have brought victory to this country. Abandoning them is no different from ignoring the efforts of other officials as well.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2913\" data-end=\"2917\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2919\" data-end=\"2966\">Brandis fell silent, tilting his glass quietly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2968\" data-end=\"3010\">It wasn’t that he was angry or displeased.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3012\" data-end=\"3059\">He simply wanted to see how far Kaden would go.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3061\" data-end=\"3314\">“Black nearly died fighting Narak. I thought it was already too late. But he survived, and he’s been fighting ever since. Harnette Adelaira marched onto the battlefield alongside Black. Considering what both have contributed, you must not abandon them.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3316\" data-end=\"3391\">It was both a protest to Brandis and a plea on behalf of Zion and Hannett.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3393\" data-end=\"3476\">Brandis needed knights like Zion and Harnett, and misfortune must not befall them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3478\" data-end=\"3513\">That is why his words were earnest.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3515\" data-end=\"3524\">“Hahaha!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3526\" data-end=\"3573\">Brandis laughed lightly and refilled his glass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3575\" data-end=\"3602\">Kaden silently accepted it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3604\" data-end=\"3712\">“How could I ever abandon them? If I intended to abandon them, I never would have sworn in the first place.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3714\" data-end=\"3885\">“If that is truly how you feel, then you must not give Hannette Adelaira the title of Setinos Quasar. Strengthening Duke Adelaira’s power only weakens Your Majesty’s own.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3887\" data-end=\"3939\">“…I’ve already finished talking with Duke Adelaira.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3941\" data-end=\"3991\">Kaden’s expression stiffened as he held his glass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3993\" data-end=\"4045\">One way or another, it meant negotiations were over.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4047\" data-end=\"4110\">Things might have gone smoothly—or they might have been forced.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4112\" data-end=\"4144\">“Do you think I threatened him?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4146\" data-end=\"4154\">“Well….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4156\" data-end=\"4244\">“Hahaha! I govern this country—how could I possibly threaten the head of a ducal house?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4246\" data-end=\"4331\">Duke Adelaira was a family that had greatly contributed to the reform of the dynasty.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4333\" data-end=\"4436\">Moreover, they had maintained their relationship with the royal family and prevented internal conflict.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4438\" data-end=\"4526\">That was how they secured a solid position while continuously expanding their influence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4528\" data-end=\"4733\">“Duke Adelaira said he wouldn’t give the position of head of household to Hannette Adelaira. I also offered support for the reconstruction of the Royal Palace and Sevenil Castle. But I issued no commands.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4735\" data-end=\"4775\">“I understand Your Majesty’s intention.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4777\" data-end=\"4892\">“My son-in-law is a Setinos Quasar. The daughter grows stronger, following her fiancé. How could you not see that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4894\" data-end=\"4921\">“…Isn’t that enough, then?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4923\" data-end=\"4979\">Brandis had been watching Duke Adelaira for a long time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4981\" data-end=\"5047\">If the Duke had seen through him, he too would have been prepared.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5049\" data-end=\"5149\">However, the head-of-household position and financial support alone did not dispel Brandis’s doubts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5151\" data-end=\"5216\">“I told him I would not interfere with succession to the throne.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5218\" data-end=\"5267\">“That must be connected to the three princesses.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5269\" data-end=\"5526\">“The three princesses are engaged to Barchen Regard. Black is Varhen Regiard’s younger brother. Ultimately this leads back to Hannette Adelaira as well… You said you would decide the end, whether by granting independence or sending her to Marquis Reggiard.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5528\" data-end=\"5559\">“Is that why you’re asking me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5561\" data-end=\"5642\">“Shouldn’t I hear your opinion? I already heard the answers from White and Blue.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5644\" data-end=\"5733\">Naturally, he needed to discuss this with the Purple Priest and the Black Knight as well.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5735\" data-end=\"5841\">He had sent a separate letter to the Purple Priest, and he wondered whether to meet the Black Knight last.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5843\" data-end=\"5976\">“Hannett Adelaira deserves it… But there are too many complications. If she becomes a Setinos Quasar, Your Majesty will be troubled.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5978\" data-end=\"5999\">“Are you against it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6001\" data-end=\"6049\">“Yes, I wish to oppose it for both their sakes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6051\" data-end=\"6148\">If Harnette were appointed a Setinos Quasar, both Duke Adelaira and Zion would become entangled.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6150\" data-end=\"6220\">Silence would intensify, and rumors and misunderstandings would surge.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6222\" data-end=\"6306\">Even if Brandis relinquished the throne, he would continue suspecting Duke Adelaira.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6308\" data-end=\"6340\">“Is everyone thinking the same?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6342\" data-end=\"6369\">“…You mean White and Blue?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6371\" data-end=\"6404\">“They said much the same as you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6406\" data-end=\"6448\">That made three of the six who opposed it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6450\" data-end=\"6536\">If more than half expressed disagreement, there was no longer any reason to pursue it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6538\" data-end=\"6639\">“Whatever you choose, there will be drawbacks. But… Can we afford to lose more than we already have?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6641\" data-end=\"6732\">If Harnette acted as a Setinos Quasar, she would certainly contribute to the Alain Kingdom.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6734\" data-end=\"6823\">But the fact that she was Zion’s fiancée and Duke Adelaira’s daughter was too dangerous.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6825\" data-end=\"6901\">In the worst case, it could lead to the purge of the entire Adelaira family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6903\" data-end=\"6970\">“…I don’t want to make enemies. Aren’t they a well-matched couple?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6972\" data-end=\"7030\">New desires may arise when something precious is involved.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7032\" data-end=\"7091\">Besides, the two still held hearts that had once been lost.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7093\" data-end=\"7158\">Maybe that’s why he grew impatient despite looking forward to it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7160\" data-end=\"7234\">“Even if you leave things as they are, you can still use both as knights.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7236\" data-end=\"7354\">“You’re right. If you become too greedy, you may even lose what you already have. Things must not turn out like that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7356\" data-end=\"7402\">Brandis emptied his mind along with his glass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7404\" data-end=\"7477\">Granting Hannette Adelaira the title of Setinos Quasar was unprecedented.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7479\" data-end=\"7548\">Perhaps the Purple Priest and the Black Knight would answer the same.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7550\" data-end=\"7596\">“…Shouldn’t we talk about something else now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7598\" data-end=\"7634\">“What would you like to talk about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7636\" data-end=\"7742\">“I need to fulfill the promise I made to you. I’ll give you a day of my time—tell me what you want to do.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7744\" data-end=\"7787\">Brandis laughed and reached for the bottle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7789\" data-end=\"7867\">Kaden thought for a moment, then took the bottle and refilled Brandis’s glass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7869\" data-end=\"7905\">“…I’d like to observe Lady Brandis.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7907\" data-end=\"7962\">“Observe me? Hmm… You mean you want to see how I work?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7964\" data-end=\"8025\">“Yes, I want to understand what Lady Brandis’s life is like.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8027\" data-end=\"8034\">“Haha!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8036\" data-end=\"8091\">Brandis was taken aback, but found it somewhat amusing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8093\" data-end=\"8197\">He offered him the most time to spend together, and yet the request he returned was simply to watch him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8199\" data-end=\"8244\">What was he thinking, to make such a request?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8246\" data-end=\"8307\"><em data-start=\"8246\" data-end=\"8307\">…Really… Are you not embarrassed? You do such funny things.</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"8309\" data-end=\"8314\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8316\" data-end=\"8365\">Duke Adelaira’s residence — indoor training hall.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8367\" data-end=\"8427\">Zion held a wooden sword and practiced light swordsmanship.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8429\" data-end=\"8515\">It had taken quite a while, but his physical condition had finally returned to normal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8517\" data-end=\"8638\">Enrite had left a warning that there might be issues with his magic power, but pure darkness had settled within his body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8640\" data-end=\"8677\"><em data-start=\"8640\" data-end=\"8677\">Beyond Lane there must be darkness.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8679\" data-end=\"8756\">This was both the strength and flaw of Exceed Rain, the divine demonic sword.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8758\" data-end=\"8865\">The Demon God and the Third Demon King, who possessed the essence of darkness, could be overwhelmed easily.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8867\" data-end=\"8950\">But because the slime dragon had only weak darkness, it was not so easily cut down.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8952\" data-end=\"8992\"><em data-start=\"8952\" data-end=\"8992\">All I need is Brecht or Dran Calgonis.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8994\" data-end=\"9093\">Yet Brecht, the thousand-day demonic sword, and Dran Calgonis, the dragon demonic sword, were gone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9095\" data-end=\"9183\">They were attacks that unconditionally erased immortality and inflicted unbearable pain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9185\" data-end=\"9260\">In truth, with just those two swords, any demon beast could be annihilated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9262\" data-end=\"9302\"><em data-start=\"9262\" data-end=\"9302\">I never imagined I’d become this weak…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9304\" data-end=\"9348\">“I’ll guess what you’re thinking right now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9350\" data-end=\"9394\">Hannette looked at Zion and suddenly spoke.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9396\" data-end=\"9450\">Zion immediately set aside his wooden sword, puzzled.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9452\" data-end=\"9473\">“How will you guess?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9475\" data-end=\"9511\">“It’s obvious what you’re thinking.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9513\" data-end=\"9549\">Hannette stood and approached Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9551\" data-end=\"9604\">Zion quietly watched and waited for her to continue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9606\" data-end=\"9637\">“You think you’re weak, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9639\" data-end=\"9643\">“…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9645\" data-end=\"9696\">Zion froze for a moment, but tried not to show it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9698\" data-end=\"9762\">But Hannette caught the subtle change in his expression at once.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9764\" data-end=\"9834\">“You’re not weak. I’m just getting stronger. Oh—does Lesia count too?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9836\" data-end=\"9854\">“Ah… not exactly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9856\" data-end=\"9963\">“No, what do you mean ‘not exactly’? If you leave everything to someone else, of course you feel insecure.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9965\" data-end=\"9969\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9971\" data-end=\"9998\">He couldn’t make an excuse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10000\" data-end=\"10026\">She knew him too well now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10028\" data-end=\"10071\">And if he lied, she’d see right through it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10073\" data-end=\"10143\">“You’ve worked so hard all this time. Will you continue to work hard?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10145\" data-end=\"10200\">“It’s not that I don’t trust you. I just want to help…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10202\" data-end=\"10282\">“Didn’t I tell you? I just want you to stay by my side. Is that really so hard?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10284\" data-end=\"10311\">Zion couldn’t accept that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10313\" data-end=\"10367\">Just staying by her side didn’t make him feel at ease.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10369\" data-end=\"10409\">Everything was good—so he needed a role.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10411\" data-end=\"10474\">“You’re not answering. Are you planning something weird again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10476\" data-end=\"10485\">“No, I….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10487\" data-end=\"10585\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">“I won’t allow it. Let’s get married right now. If we don’t, I won’t be able to keep hold of you.”</p></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-183/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"42\">\r\n<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"58\">“Uh… alright?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"117\">Zion, unable to find an answer, looked at her carefully.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"162\">Her golden eyes shone brighter than before.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"164\" data-end=\"191\">I couldn’t face those eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"193\" data-end=\"222\">“You think you can marry me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"266\">“I did say that… taking a bit more time….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"268\" data-end=\"325\">“Why are you so gloomy? Tell me why you can’t do it now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"344\">“There’s still….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"346\" data-end=\"380\">“Not counting the ones who drink.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"382\" data-end=\"386\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"431\">Zion fell silent and turned her eyes away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"433\" data-end=\"496\">Harnette casually met her gaze and waited for a further answer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"498\" data-end=\"547\">“Whoa… Sister, didn’t you say marriage is scary?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"549\" data-end=\"666\">“I’m more scared of what you do. Not once, not twice. If you’ve done it twice already, can’t you do it a third time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"695\">“Have I done anything yet?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"708\">“Just now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"710\" data-end=\"744\">“Can you see my future right now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"775\">“Because it’s my future too?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"835\">“Ah, so you’re going to tie me up so I can’t go anywhere?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"957\">“I don’t want to tie you up, I want to toss you somewhere. Are you saying that because you have so many lives to spare?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"959\" data-end=\"990\">“Well… should I laugh or cry…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1027\">Zion sighed and walked to a chair.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1063\">Harnette silently followed behind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1065\" data-end=\"1120\">“But I understand. I can’t even say it’s not my fault.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1122\" data-end=\"1169\">Zion sat down and began searching for a towel.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1227\">Harnette quickly grabbed a towel and handed it to Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1229\" data-end=\"1306\">“I only once… you twice. And I only got hit, but I didn’t rush out like you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1326\">“That’s true too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1359\">Zion didn’t bother denying it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1361\" data-end=\"1408\">After all, she had nearly thrown her life away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1468\">Both she and Harnette knew the meaning behind that action.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1723\">“Let me tell you what I’m thinking. The three great demon kings and the four great calamities might already be gone. Now there’s only that one drinker and other monsters left. It seems pretty much settled… so it wouldn’t be a problem if we married now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1725\" data-end=\"1768\">Zion wiped her sweat and continued calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1813\">Harnette sat right beside her and listened.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1815\" data-end=\"1845\">“But… I have a small concern.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1847\" data-end=\"1878\">“What are you concerned about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1880\" data-end=\"1979\">“I saw that artificial demon sword break, but… there were pieces left. Did you see it too, Sister?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1981\" data-end=\"2037\">“Yes, I saw it. So you’re trying to find the fragments.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2039\" data-end=\"2149\">Harnette had personally witnessed the artificial magic sword shatter while destroying the slime dragon’s core.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2151\" data-end=\"2244\">After that, the slime dragon’s body collapsed, red fluid pouring out and covering the ground.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2246\" data-end=\"2358\">She had kept an eye on the situation and tried to gather the broken fragments, but ultimately couldn’t find any.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2360\" data-end=\"2478\">“It might’ve disappeared while I couldn’t see for a moment. Maybe I’m mistaken. But… don’t you think it was too easy?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2480\" data-end=\"2486\">“Hmm…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2488\" data-end=\"2520\">Harnette pondered Zion’s words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2522\" data-end=\"2626\">Ever since the Demon God appeared in the capital, he used his superior speed and stealth to the fullest.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2628\" data-end=\"2717\">Even after being counterattacked by Lesia, he quickly escaped using those same abilities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2719\" data-end=\"2805\">How could a demon like that not react to the destruction of an artificial demon sword?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2807\" data-end=\"2825\">Was something off?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2827\" data-end=\"2906\">“I think something’s being hidden. Shouldn’t we keep watching a little longer?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2908\" data-end=\"2962\">“No harm in being cautious. Isn’t that thing strange?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2964\" data-end=\"3054\">The Demon God was the most unusual and troublesome demonic being she had ever encountered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3056\" data-end=\"3153\">He didn’t attack the Alain kingdom directly but secretly appeared and tried to advance his plans.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3155\" data-end=\"3213\">Above all, he had done strange things that made them wary.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3215\" data-end=\"3269\">“So it’s better to delay the wedding a little longer…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3271\" data-end=\"3336\">“If I delay, do I have to stay like this until I die of old age?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3338\" data-end=\"3371\">“Oh, of course—just a few years…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3373\" data-end=\"3405\">“Isn’t a few years a long time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3407\" data-end=\"3523\">“It’s been over a year since our engagement ceremony. Usually it takes 3 months, sometimes 6. Six months here, and…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3525\" data-end=\"3621\">“Speak accurately. It’s been one year, one month, and eight days since the engagement ceremony.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3623\" data-end=\"3627\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3629\" data-end=\"3668\">Zion slowly turned to her, speechless.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3670\" data-end=\"3742\">She hadn’t counted the days, but Harnette had tracked them meticulously.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3744\" data-end=\"3780\">Isn’t that just asking to be teased?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3782\" data-end=\"3867\">“Sigh… I can wait. Aren’t we both burdened by marriage? You should keep what I said.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3869\" data-end=\"3931\">“Weren’t you the one who asked to marry after a long journey?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3933\" data-end=\"4020\">“You’re not wrong. I can’t say it’s all over because something still feels suspicious.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4022\" data-end=\"4082\">As Zion said, maybe it was better to wait a few more years.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4084\" data-end=\"4151\">They were still very close, but there was no need to rush marriage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4153\" data-end=\"4233\">Most importantly, she didn’t want to ruin her only wedding because of one demon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4235\" data-end=\"4317\">“Earliest six months, latest two years. I think that’s plenty… what do you think?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4319\" data-end=\"4350\">“Not bad. Two years is enough.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4352\" data-end=\"4395\">“Didn’t you say you’d do it in six months?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4397\" data-end=\"4473\">“If you’re sure, you can do it today. How long do I have to stay like this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4475\" data-end=\"4543\">“You’re still young. It’s not like anything’s wrong with your body.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4545\" data-end=\"4635\">“Sister, you can have fun while you’re young. Isn’t it hard to have fun when you get old?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4637\" data-end=\"4651\">“…Is that so?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4653\" data-end=\"4703\">Harnette tilted her head, understanding her point.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4705\" data-end=\"4761\">Promises for the distant future don’t guarantee results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4763\" data-end=\"4825\">You could lose things, or end up full of regret and suffering.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4827\" data-end=\"4875\">That’s why you should live fully in the present.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4877\" data-end=\"4911\">“You should just get married now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4913\" data-end=\"4944\">“Are you even listening to me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4946\" data-end=\"4965\">“I just heard you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4967\" data-end=\"4991\">“You pretended to hear.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4993\" data-end=\"5119\">“There’s still a lot to do. We need a house, furniture. We need servants and soldiers. And… maybe something else will happen.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5121\" data-end=\"5133\">“What else?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5135\" data-end=\"5160\">“No idea. Just guessing.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5162\" data-end=\"5173\">“Ah, that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5175\" data-end=\"5235\">Human life is full of unpredictable and unreasonable things.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5237\" data-end=\"5312\">Preparation doesn’t always prevent them, and many things remain unresolved.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5314\" data-end=\"5391\">Perhaps Harnette was assuming based on everything she had experienced so far.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5393\" data-end=\"5549\">“I never imagined I’d live in a mansion or learn magic. That I’d follow you to remote areas? With you—kill demons, gain fame, revive myself, grow stronger…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5551\" data-end=\"5603\">Harnette looked back on her past and smiled faintly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5605\" data-end=\"5664\">If she had been alone, none of it would have been possible.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5666\" data-end=\"5725\">That’s why, relying on Zion, she tried to face everything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5727\" data-end=\"5823\">“My whole life has been you. How many more strange things will I go through if I stay with you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5825\" data-end=\"5872\">Harnette reached out and smoothed Zion’s hair.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5874\" data-end=\"5927\">Her sweat-soaked silver hair had a different texture.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5929\" data-end=\"6023\">Now, she couldn’t imagine being separated from Zion—and that feeling had only grown stronger.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6025\" data-end=\"6090\">“I thought I liked you as a friend… but I don’t think that’s it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6092\" data-end=\"6096\">“…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6098\" data-end=\"6144\">A strange atmosphere filled the training hall.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6146\" data-end=\"6213\">Zion got tangled in numerous thoughts, her tension rising sharply.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6215\" data-end=\"6263\">If she was right… Harnette was about to confess.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6291\">“I sincerely… so… I, you…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6293\" data-end=\"6338\">Harnette bit her lip, stumbling on her words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6340\" data-end=\"6421\">She had thought about this for a long time, yet couldn’t bring herself to say it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6423\" data-end=\"6454\">Why was she hesitating so much?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6465\">“Um… um…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6467\" data-end=\"6496\">“Are you saying you love me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6498\" data-end=\"6520\">“…Why did you say it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6522\" data-end=\"6550\">“Well… it looked difficult.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6552\" data-end=\"6578\">“Can’t you read the mood?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6580\" data-end=\"6633\">“You said this because you <em data-start=\"6607\" data-end=\"6613\">were</em> reading it, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6635\" data-end=\"6658\">“Hey! Are you joking!?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6660\" data-end=\"6698\">Harnette raised her voice, cheeks red.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6700\" data-end=\"6743\">It was something she wanted to say herself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6745\" data-end=\"6777\">But Zion had stolen the moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6779\" data-end=\"6821\">“Why did you say what I was about to say?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6823\" data-end=\"6830\">“Well…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6832\" data-end=\"6882\">“You could’ve listened quietly. Why’d you cut in?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6884\" data-end=\"6935\">“If you don’t talk, you’ll stay like this forever…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6937\" data-end=\"6973\">“You’re impatient? Is it that hard?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6975\" data-end=\"7001\">“It’s not that it’s hard…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7003\" data-end=\"7081\">“Do you know how I feel saying this? Does it look easy? Why don’t you get it…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7083\" data-end=\"7127\">“I love you too, can’t we leave it at that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7129\" data-end=\"7183\">“You have a problem with—wait, what did you just say?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7185\" data-end=\"7215\">Harnette frowned in confusion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7217\" data-end=\"7283\">Zion took a breath, calming her pounding heart, then spoke again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7285\" data-end=\"7305\">“I said I love you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7307\" data-end=\"7329\">“Uh… um… you love me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7331\" data-end=\"7383\">“I was going to say that too. You were just faster.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7385\" data-end=\"7416\">“How did you hear—really… ugh…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7418\" data-end=\"7459\">She worried Zion might think it strange.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7461\" data-end=\"7566\">Even though Zion had interrupted her confession, she wondered if at least it would ease her own anxiety.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7568\" data-end=\"7634\">If she didn’t say the same words back, she wouldn’t let Zion off.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7636\" data-end=\"7658\">“Are you alright now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7660\" data-end=\"7681\">“Nothing is alright.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7683\" data-end=\"7742\">“If we both confirmed it, what else are you unhappy about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7744\" data-end=\"7764\">“You… you stole it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7766\" data-end=\"7822\">“Then let’s pretend you didn’t hear it and start again—”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7824\" data-end=\"7864\">“How do you redo that!? Are you insane?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7866\" data-end=\"7872\">“Wow…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7874\" data-end=\"7910\">Zion scratched her head, flustered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7912\" data-end=\"7952\">She was upset over just one stolen line.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7954\" data-end=\"8024\">But since nothing else would calm her, Zion reluctantly stayed quiet.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8026\" data-end=\"8059\"><em data-start=\"8026\" data-end=\"8059\">Still… I have feelings for you.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8061\" data-end=\"8109\">Fear had stopped her from expressing them first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8111\" data-end=\"8180\">Maybe because she always felt like the only one who admired Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8182\" data-end=\"8267\">But since Harnette had spoken first, she finally gained a bit of courage—though late.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8269\" data-end=\"8306\"><em data-start=\"8269\" data-end=\"8306\">Is it okay for me to marry her now?</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"8308\" data-end=\"8311\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8313\" data-end=\"8357\">Duke Adelaira’s residence, the drawing room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8359\" data-end=\"8413\">Juter and Barchen visited Duke Adelaira to meet Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8415\" data-end=\"8532\">Of course, they had visited Zion when she was injured, but this time they came back because she had fully recovered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8534\" data-end=\"8625\">Zion greeted the two with Harnette, and they chatted, asking each other how they had been.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8627\" data-end=\"8662\">“I’m glad to hear nothing’s wrong.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8664\" data-end=\"8698\">“Yes, thank you for your concern.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8700\" data-end=\"8742\">“Lady Harnette must’ve been very worried.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8744\" data-end=\"8810\">“She’s recovered well, so I don’t think we need to worry anymore.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8812\" data-end=\"8901\">Harnette had heard from Enrithe that Zion had recovered, but that wasn’t enough for her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8903\" data-end=\"8998\">In the end, she checked Zion’s body and magic power one by one before she could finally relax.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9000\" data-end=\"9069\">“I need to consider side effects, so I can’t use my body recklessly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9071\" data-end=\"9130\">“Yes, I’ve been acting carefully because White advised me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9132\" data-end=\"9177\">“I see… Will the wedding be postponed again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9179\" data-end=\"9212\">“Ah, yes. It looks like it will.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9214\" data-end=\"9276\">“That’s a bit disappointing. You two should’ve married first.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9278\" data-end=\"9322\">Zion couldn’t help questioning those words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9324\" data-end=\"9342\">Why “marry first”?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9344\" data-end=\"9391\">Was someone else planning to marry before them?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9393\" data-end=\"9446\">“The order has changed. We’re getting married first.”</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9448\" data-end=\"9451\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-184/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"112\" data-end=\"115\">\r\n<p data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"127\"><strong data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"127\">“Yes?”</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"135\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"137\" data-end=\"197\">Zion and Hanette looked at Uter at the same time, surprised.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"199\" data-end=\"270\">Unlike them, Barhen only eavesdropped quietly while tilting his teacup.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"272\" data-end=\"391\">“His Majesty brought up the topic of marriage. We had no reason to waste time, so we simply followed the king’s order.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"393\" data-end=\"464\">“I know the engagement period was short, but… Are you already married?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"466\" data-end=\"543\">“Lady Harnett, it’s been five months since we got engaged. Isn’t that short?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"545\" data-end=\"557\">“That… yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"559\" data-end=\"590\">Harnette faltered for a moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"592\" data-end=\"683\">Normally, after an engagement, the wedding is held within 3 months, 6 months at the latest.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"685\" data-end=\"771\">But thinking only of herself and Zion, she decided that Uter’s marriage felt too soon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"773\" data-end=\"859\">“Since Lady Harnett set the length of your engagement, isn’t that why I felt lacking?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"861\" data-end=\"891\">“Yes, I suppose you’re right.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"998\">“Still, there must be a reason you postponed it… If you consider that, there’s nothing to apologize for.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1000\" data-end=\"1040\">“Oh no. It was something we decided on.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1042\" data-end=\"1076\">There was nothing wrong with that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1078\" data-end=\"1156\">She and Zion knew more than others and had relatively superior military power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1158\" data-end=\"1245\">No one knew the full situation, but it had to be done, so she and Zion bore the burden.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1247\" data-end=\"1325\">“Because you two worked hard, we were able to hold the wedding. I’m grateful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1370\">“If you think that way, then I’m thankful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1427\">If it was the king’s order, even Uter could not refuse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1494\">Besides, it was also the wedding of Zion’s older brother, Barhen.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1590\">Since he was now a member of the Lihines Knights, he should happily offer his congratulations.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1592\" data-end=\"1627\">“Does anyone else know besides us?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1715\">“There must be a letter from Marquis Regard. My brother or high officials might know.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1717\" data-end=\"1754\">“Have you chosen the date and place?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1756\" data-end=\"1841\">“I know you’re still choosing. Once everything is arranged, His Majesty will decide.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1891\">“Ah, then we still have time until the wedding.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1893\" data-end=\"1941\">“I don’t think much is left. We’re moving fast.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"1986\">“… You seem in a hurry. Is there a reason?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1988\" data-end=\"2063\">“It is difficult for me to say. I don’t know what His Majesty is thinking.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2128\">Brandis, along with Enrite, knew about the existence of demons.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2130\" data-end=\"2216\">But even so, was it necessary for Uter and Varchen’s wedding to suddenly move forward?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2218\" data-end=\"2291\">‘If you worry about drinking, you can’t do anything. Is that the reason?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2293\" data-end=\"2397\">It was good to stay alert for demon appearances, but if things continued this way, nothing would change.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2498\">Eventually, you get swept up by the atmosphere, mental fatigue builds up, and you become sensitive.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2500\" data-end=\"2572\">As time passes, things worsen, so perhaps he wanted to arrange it first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2574\" data-end=\"2613\">‘Maybe it’s better to act like a king.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2615\" data-end=\"2652\">Waiting isn't always the best choice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2654\" data-end=\"2738\">More importantly, he might have felt frustrated because Hannett was being held back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2740\" data-end=\"2799\">‘I understand his position, but… maybe I was too stubborn?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2801\" data-end=\"2868\">After constant hesitation, Hannette decided to accept the marriage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2870\" data-end=\"2936\">She worried about herself, but she also tried to express her love.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2938\" data-end=\"3032\">Even so, she only hoped Zion would notice it—and she was still thinking of fighting the enemy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3034\" data-end=\"3100\">‘Even if we prepare now, our schedules will overlap. That’s rude.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3102\" data-end=\"3191\">If you didn’t know Uter and Barhen were getting married, you could arrange it separately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3193\" data-end=\"3283\">But if you proceed knowingly, it would seem as if you were interfering with their wedding.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3394\">Moreover, Uter was direct royal family, and considering his siblings were involved, she had to quietly watch.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3396\" data-end=\"3433\">“I don’t think Hanette will like it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3435\" data-end=\"3481\">Zion quietly looked away and observed Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3483\" data-end=\"3553\">Outwardly, she seemed normal, but inside, things could be complicated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3555\" data-end=\"3630\">Following the natural order, she and Zion should have gotten married first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3632\" data-end=\"3687\">‘I already missed that, but if it turns out like this…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3689\" data-end=\"3869\">“Zion, take care of yourself. Even if you’re young, pushing yourself too hard will break your body. I want to tell you not to go to war… but one cannot say that to Setinos Quasar.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3871\" data-end=\"3920\">Barhen put down his teacup and broke the silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3922\" data-end=\"3986\">Wherever they were, he always gave Uter the first turn to speak.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3988\" data-end=\"4071\">Because he was direct royal family and her fiancé, Barhen waited for him to finish.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4073\" data-end=\"4099\">“Yes, I’ll do as you say.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4101\" data-end=\"4191\">“I feel I haven’t fulfilled my role as an older brother. I wish I could have done better…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4193\" data-end=\"4229\">“No. My brother is still wonderful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4231\" data-end=\"4302\">“I’m sorry, Lady Harnet. It seems I couldn’t keep my previous promise.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4304\" data-end=\"4376\">“You fought with us recently, didn’t you? For that alone, I’m grateful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4378\" data-end=\"4438\">Hannette never expected much from Barhen in the first place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4440\" data-end=\"4517\">As Zion’s older brother and a Royal Knight, all he needed to do was be there.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4519\" data-end=\"4577\">That way, Zion could feel at ease and focus on his duties.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4579\" data-end=\"4665\">“I feel the same as Barhen. I should have done something… I feel like I only watched.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4667\" data-end=\"4761\">In the battle with the slime dragon, Uter used his magical sword and poured out magical power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4763\" data-end=\"4878\">The slime dragon roared without hesitation, and Brandis and Walter did their best to sustain protection with magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4880\" data-end=\"4964\">With the president’s strength added, they managed to block all the dragon’s attacks.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4966\" data-end=\"5075\">“My brother and I were able to advance thanks to you both. Without you, we couldn’t have defeated the enemy.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5077\" data-end=\"5116\">Regardless of who contributed how much.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5118\" data-end=\"5172\">They all went to battle together, risking their lives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5174\" data-end=\"5274\">There were mistakes along the way, but in the end, they overcame them and defeated the slime dragon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5276\" data-end=\"5317\">No casualties—surely that was a blessing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5319\" data-end=\"5366\">“I am grateful for your words. Still, I tried.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5368\" data-end=\"5373\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5375\" data-end=\"5440\">Barhen swallowed his silence and looked between Zion and Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5442\" data-end=\"5516\">Though still speculation, the two had definitely been through an incident.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5518\" data-end=\"5626\">At that time, Zion couldn’t move, drenched in sweat, and Hanette stood before flames that had changed color.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5628\" data-end=\"5677\">But he couldn’t simply ask, so he kept it inside.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5679\" data-end=\"5693\">‘Zion… cried.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5695\" data-end=\"5748\">Even amid everything, Barhen noticed Zion’s feelings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5750\" data-end=\"5849\">He should have wiped away his tears from the beginning, but he couldn’t erase the traces of sorrow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5851\" data-end=\"5917\">If Zion shed tears in such a situation, there was only one reason.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5919\" data-end=\"5986\">‘Lady Harnett must have been gravely injured or died… and revived.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5988\" data-end=\"6037\">He wasn’t sure, but he didn’t think he was wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6039\" data-end=\"6119\">Because Hanette’s fire magic had changed, and even her atmosphere was different.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6121\" data-end=\"6209\">Perhaps it was because she had grown strong enough to repel the slime dragon by herself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6211\" data-end=\"6240\">‘Zion, that’s why I’m sorry.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6242\" data-end=\"6330\">When he first awakened his swordsmanship, he promised to go to Zion and Hanette to help.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6332\" data-end=\"6398\">When Zion became Setinos Quasar, he was asked to protect Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6400\" data-end=\"6473\">But he fulfilled none of those promises, and the battle was already over.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6475\" data-end=\"6506\">‘There’s nothing I can do now.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6508\" data-end=\"6545\">He could only promise for the future.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6547\" data-end=\"6605\">He would now marry Uter, but could no longer demand power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6607\" data-end=\"6681\">Only once Uter grew stronger could he offer something to Zion and Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6683\" data-end=\"6751\">‘Uter said he would become king. When he achieves his goal, for me…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6753\" data-end=\"6799\">Of course, he must not be greedy or stand out.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6801\" data-end=\"6872\">He must take only what was necessary, with proper reason and procedure.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6874\" data-end=\"6962\">Only then would he not hinder Uter, and the Marquis of Regiard could be fully protected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6964\" data-end=\"6989\">‘I will keep my promise.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6991\" data-end=\"7051\">Promises are not made only because of bloodline or siblings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7053\" data-end=\"7140\">Because these were words he said, a request he made as a knight—there must be a result.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7142\" data-end=\"7203\">If he couldn’t achieve that, he couldn’t be proud of himself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7205\" data-end=\"7252\">‘I won’t forget until then. Zion, Lady Harnet.’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"7254\" data-end=\"7259\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7261\" data-end=\"7322\">Near the Eldran supply base, where the slime dragon vanished.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7324\" data-end=\"7360\">Traces of the battle still remained.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7362\" data-end=\"7454\">After the trees were felled, they slowly rotted, and even weeds didn’t grow near the crater.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7456\" data-end=\"7566\">The animals left as carcasses became scattered pieces of flesh and bone—flies and ants wouldn’t even approach.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7568\" data-end=\"7631\">How many years would it take for this land to return to normal?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7633\" data-end=\"7644\">– …destroy…</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7646\" data-end=\"7691\">A strange, eerie voice echoed from somewhere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7693\" data-end=\"7780\">There was no mistaking it—it was the voice of a demon, but the atmosphere felt unusual.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7782\" data-end=\"7840\">As if it had just returned from being something unnatural.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7842\" data-end=\"7879\">– You need nothing. You must destroy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7881\" data-end=\"7936\">A dark aura seeped out as it crawled across the ground.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7938\" data-end=\"8000\">It resembled demonic energy, but its foundation was distorted.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8002\" data-end=\"8065\">White, gray, and green tangled together, producing a new color.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8067\" data-end=\"8145\">– This will not lead to the creation of a world. Only destruction will repeat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8147\" data-end=\"8175\">The demon had lost its body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8177\" data-end=\"8250\">Its mind had disappeared too, but its will remained—faint yet persistent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8252\" data-end=\"8326\">Following that will, mana gathered, and as a result, a new demon was born.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8328\" data-end=\"8404\">– Only destruction… indeed. When you reach destruction, you won’t feel pain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8406\" data-end=\"8442\">The black turned abruptly into gray.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8444\" data-end=\"8510\">A stream of gray air spread outward and began touching everything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8512\" data-end=\"8585\">Trees rotted faster, animal bones turned to dust, and the earth withered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8587\" data-end=\"8647\">Though formless, it drove everything around it toward death.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8649\" data-end=\"8774\">– Destroy. It ends with that. You need not go toward the future. You need not look back at the past. Life… is it not painful?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8776\" data-end=\"8877\">Because they live, they feel emotion, and constantly become tangled and influenced by those emotions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8879\" data-end=\"8914\">Some are happy, but become unhappy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8916\" data-end=\"8967\">Others enjoy pleasure, yet cannot escape suffering.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8969\" data-end=\"9015\">Why cling to life in such an irrational world?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9017\" data-end=\"9135\">– The answer is in destruction. Regret and remorse fade, and fear and anxiety vanish. After destruction, you may rest.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9137\" data-end=\"9187\">When touched by destruction—death—nothing is felt.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9189\" data-end=\"9253\">Life fades, thoughts scatter, and the body decays like a corpse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9255\" data-end=\"9320\">Living beings avoid death because they lose everything they have.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9322\" data-end=\"9398\">But after experiencing death, one no longer suffers, for emotion disappears.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9400\" data-end=\"9454\">– This world will fall. No one… can change the ending.</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-185/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"182\" data-end=\"185\">\r\n<p data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"228\"><strong data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"228\">Inside the carriage, near the palace.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"230\" data-end=\"305\">Zion and Hanette left the palace and headed back to Duke Adelaira’s estate.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"307\" data-end=\"406\">Juter and Barhen’s wedding was scheduled rather quickly, and many nobles had gathered just in time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"408\" data-end=\"545\">Since Zion was the royal family’s son-in-law and Hanette the daughter of a duke, they could sit at the high table and watch the ceremony.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"550\" data-end=\"561\">“… Sister.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"563\" data-end=\"593\">“Why are you calling me that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"595\" data-end=\"615\">“Are you not angry?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"617\" data-end=\"645\">“You’re always saying that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"660\">“Not always.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"734\">“It seems like I only say it when I <em data-start=\"698\" data-end=\"704\">feel</em> like I’m going to get angry.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"756\">“So, are you angry?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"758\" data-end=\"795\">“Ah, seriously! Why are <em data-start=\"782\" data-end=\"787\">you</em> angry?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"797\" data-end=\"835\">Hanette turned her head away, annoyed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"885\">Zion quietly stared at her and answered instead.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"887\" data-end=\"931\">“What? Why are you looking at me like that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"962\">“You said you weren’t angry.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"964\" data-end=\"984\">“You made me angry.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"986\" data-end=\"1032\">“You weren’t angry before I said that, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1034\" data-end=\"1068\">“Huh… Are you trying to fight me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1118\">“What good would it do to fight my future wife?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1194\">“Tch! Who knows if you’ll keep doing this to your future husband forever?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1196\" data-end=\"1242\">The two of them fell silent as their eyes met.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1304\">They stared for a moment, then both smiled at the same time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1306\" data-end=\"1363\">“That tone is kind of strange. You’re my future husband…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1365\" data-end=\"1406\">“You said <em data-start=\"1375\" data-end=\"1398\">you’re my future wife</em> first.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1408\" data-end=\"1437\">“Then… can I call you <em data-start=\"1430\" data-end=\"1435\">Mr.</em>?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1439\" data-end=\"1464\">“…We’re not married yet.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1516\">“Then can I call you that <em data-start=\"1492\" data-end=\"1499\">after</em> we get married?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1518\" data-end=\"1569\">“And I don’t want to hear ‘Mr.’ You sound too old.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1620\">“Then should I call you what you always call me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1622\" data-end=\"1704\">“Should I really be called ‘big brother’ just because you’re three years younger?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1706\" data-end=\"1760\">Hanette spoke bluntly, expressing her dissatisfaction.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1762\" data-end=\"1812\">Until now she could still hear him call her “sis.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1814\" data-end=\"1893\">But she didn’t want honorary titles being thrown around once they were married.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1895\" data-end=\"1964\">“Well… It seems a bit late now, but… should I call you ‘big sister’?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1966\" data-end=\"1994\">“Hmmm… try it, I’ll listen.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1996\" data-end=\"2059\">Hanette looked out the window calmly, though quietly expectant.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2061\" data-end=\"2119\">Zion hesitated for a moment, then slowly opened his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2121\" data-end=\"2166\">“Big sister… has your anger cooled down now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2168\" data-end=\"2197\">“Ugh… suddenly I feel angry.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2199\" data-end=\"2205\">“Why?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2207\" data-end=\"2243\">“It feels weird hearing you say it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2245\" data-end=\"2291\">“I see… You’re just being fickle, aren’t you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2293\" data-end=\"2343\">“I’m just saying what I feel, how is that fickle?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2345\" data-end=\"2397\">It felt completely different from what she expected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2524\">Hearing him call her “sis” was touching, but the moment it became “big sister,” a strange sense of rejection rose inside her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2526\" data-end=\"2602\">Maybe because it reminded her of an actual younger brother calling her that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2604\" data-end=\"2635\">Would she have preferred “sis”?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2637\" data-end=\"2665\">“No, I want something else.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2667\" data-end=\"2695\">“What do you want me to do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2697\" data-end=\"2728\">“Well… Fine. What should I do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2730\" data-end=\"2735\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2737\" data-end=\"2763\">Zion laughed, embarrassed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2765\" data-end=\"2845\">Fortunately, Hanette seemed uneasy about Juter and Barhen getting married first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2847\" data-end=\"2931\">She probably didn’t bring it up because she understood what mattered more right now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2933\" data-end=\"2997\">“Hanette… Oh? Is this the first time you’re calling me by name?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2999\" data-end=\"3005\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3007\" data-end=\"3046\">Hanette froze and opened her eyes wide.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3048\" data-end=\"3116\">She always felt she’d eventually hear her name spoken in that voice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3118\" data-end=\"3170\">But actually hearing it made her feel strangely shy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3172\" data-end=\"3214\">“Is that enough? You can say my name too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3216\" data-end=\"3243\">“T-that… th-that… is fine?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3245\" data-end=\"3322\">Hanette barely corrected her slip of the tongue, turning her head cautiously.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3324\" data-end=\"3374\">Just hearing her name made her whole body tremble.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3376\" data-end=\"3450\">Perhaps she had been waiting for this moment far longer than she realized.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3452\" data-end=\"3565\">“I was being polite since you’re three years older… but after we marry, we’ll be equals. You should drop it too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3567\" data-end=\"3601\">“Y-your tone… Did it get shorter?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3603\" data-end=\"3714\">“Because you’ll be my wife, not my senior. I can treat you politely if you want, but you hate that, don’t you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3716\" data-end=\"3724\">“U-ugh…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3726\" data-end=\"3759\">Hanette only stammered, blushing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3761\" data-end=\"3816\">Once he said her name, even his voice and tone changed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3818\" data-end=\"3888\">It felt awkward, but not to the point where she couldn’t listen to it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3890\" data-end=\"3968\">“Now that I think about it, I’ve been too stiff. You can call me by name too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3970\" data-end=\"4016\">“Then why didn’t you call me by name earlier?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4018\" data-end=\"4098\">“…I guess it just didn’t feel necessary. I always thought of you as my fiancée.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4100\" data-end=\"4126\">“Ah… I get what you mean.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4128\" data-end=\"4203\">If they hadn’t been engaged, they’d never have met, much less grown closer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4205\" data-end=\"4271\">Maybe he’d subconsciously kept distance because of the engagement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4273\" data-end=\"4370\">“So you’re confirming our feelings now? I love you too. Should I start worrying about etiquette?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4372\" data-end=\"4407\">Of course, nobles valued etiquette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4409\" data-end=\"4478\">Many married couples still used honorifics, rarely speaking casually.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4480\" data-end=\"4548\">But those were old traditions; they didn’t need to be bound by them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4550\" data-end=\"4619\">He just adjusted his tone to match Hanette’s preferred way of living.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4687\">“When did we ever care about etiquette? I only realized that now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4689\" data-end=\"4765\">“That’s true. I mean, we just did whatever we wanted… and only ever argued.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4767\" data-end=\"4796\">“You won’t see that anymore.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4798\" data-end=\"4835\">“Because there’s no reason to fight.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4837\" data-end=\"4857\">“That’s not a joke.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4859\" data-end=\"4898\">“It’s because we know each other well.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4900\" data-end=\"4919\">“Love is… not fun.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4921\" data-end=\"4951\">“It’s not supposed to be fun.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4953\" data-end=\"5009\">Hanette slowly reached out her hand, trying to take his.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5011\" data-end=\"5059\">Zion felt the touch and held her hand in return.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5061\" data-end=\"5101\">“It’s not fun… but it’s not bad either.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5103\" data-end=\"5147\">“Right. Fun fades quickly, love lasts long.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5149\" data-end=\"5250\">“You know what? They say love eventually cools. Married couples become partners joined by affection.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5252\" data-end=\"5290\">“I don’t know. Maybe ours won’t cool.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5292\" data-end=\"5381\">“Will I still love you when I’m old? My wrinkles will stretch out and make my face ugly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5383\" data-end=\"5453\">“Then I’ll be ugly too. Since we’ll be equals… may I love you anyway?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5455\" data-end=\"5493\">“Ugh… you’re annoyingly good at this.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5495\" data-end=\"5535\">“Better that than being terrible at it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5537\" data-end=\"5581\">“You could just say, ‘I’ll still love you.’”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5583\" data-end=\"5706\">“If I said that, you’d reply, ‘Don’t lie.’ Or you’d say something like, ‘Would you still like my ugly face?’ Wouldn’t you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5708\" data-end=\"5713\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5715\" data-end=\"5740\">Hanette closed her mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5742\" data-end=\"5797\">For some reason, she felt she <em data-start=\"5772\" data-end=\"5779\">would</em> say exactly that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5799\" data-end=\"5867\">He was describing her personality too accurately for her to deny it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5869\" data-end=\"5896\">“Was my guess too perfect?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5898\" data-end=\"5946\">“What do you think? I can’t even read the mood…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5948\" data-end=\"6048\">“Oh right, you confessed to me in the training hall. Should I try saying it again? Will you listen?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6050\" data-end=\"6076\">“You want to do it again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6078\" data-end=\"6157\">“I don’t want to redo what I’ve already done. So as an apology, I’ll go first.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6159\" data-end=\"6219\">Zion lightly cleared his throat and straightened his collar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6221\" data-end=\"6314\">Hanette tried to stop him, but couldn’t bring herself to—anticipation had already taken hold.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6316\" data-end=\"6361\">“I love you. That feeling will never change.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6363\" data-end=\"6392\">Zion spoke shyly, yet calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6394\" data-end=\"6460\">Hanette instinctively covered her mouth and snapped her head away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6462\" data-end=\"6497\">“Why? Did I say something strange?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6499\" data-end=\"6519\">“No… that’s not it…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6521\" data-end=\"6541\">Her face burned red.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6543\" data-end=\"6610\">The hand covering her mouth trembled, and even her eyes lost focus.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6612\" data-end=\"6674\">Her heart thumped wildly—she could clearly hear her own pulse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6676\" data-end=\"6734\">There was no way she could ignore such a powerful feeling.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6736\" data-end=\"6761\">“I only said I love you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6763\" data-end=\"6778\">“I heard it… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6780\" data-end=\"6803\">“Hm? What did you say?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6805\" data-end=\"6829\">“I didn’t say anything.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6831\" data-end=\"6872\">“Now it’s your turn. Isn’t it only fair?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6874\" data-end=\"6904\">“Ah… I can’t. Absolutely not.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6906\" data-end=\"6964\">Hanette waved her hands and retreated as far as she could.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6966\" data-end=\"7006\">She couldn’t even look Zion in the eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7008\" data-end=\"7067\">Did he know she’d react this strongly to just one sentence?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7069\" data-end=\"7133\">“I did it twice, but you won’t do it once? Isn’t that too much?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7135\" data-end=\"7174\">“Oh, whatever! This is all your fault!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7176\" data-end=\"7192\">“What did I do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7194\" data-end=\"7208\">“You’re so… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7210\" data-end=\"7254\">Hanette furrowed her brows, glaring at Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7256\" data-end=\"7345\">Her whole body trembled from embarrassment, but she couldn’t bring herself to explain it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7347\" data-end=\"7408\">If she said it out loud, everything would collapse instantly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7410\" data-end=\"7448\"><em data-start=\"7410\" data-end=\"7448\">Does he do that because he likes me?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7450\" data-end=\"7500\">If he didn’t, he would’ve frowned or snapped back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7502\" data-end=\"7558\">But she, unlike him, was blushing and avoiding his eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7560\" data-end=\"7626\">It was understandable she couldn’t say it—it was too embarrassing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7628\" data-end=\"7682\"><em data-start=\"7628\" data-end=\"7682\">If she didn’t love me, she wouldn’t react like this.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7684\" data-end=\"7720\">Zion leaned back with a quiet smile.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7722\" data-end=\"7807\">If things continued like this, he might get to enjoy the peaceful life he dreamed of.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7809\" data-end=\"7874\">But precisely because it was so peaceful, an uneasy feeling grew.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7876\" data-end=\"7931\"><em data-start=\"7876\" data-end=\"7931\">…She won’t give up, right? She might already be dead.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7933\" data-end=\"7966\">Which meant he had to be patient.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7968\" data-end=\"8017\">They couldn’t ignore the danger of the Demon God.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8019\" data-end=\"8075\">He couldn’t lower his guard until the demon disappeared.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8077\" data-end=\"8124\"><em data-start=\"8077\" data-end=\"8124\">If it appears again, I’ll have to destroy it.</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"8126\" data-end=\"8129\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8131\" data-end=\"8196\"><strong data-start=\"8131\" data-end=\"8196\">Eastern territory of the Allain Kingdom — Eldran Supply Base.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8198\" data-end=\"8262\">After the summons arrived, the Sillay Knights departed in haste.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8264\" data-end=\"8353\">Some knights and mages had tried to stop the incoming threat, but were forced to retreat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8355\" data-end=\"8492\">Most importantly, the grey airflow started from the point where the slime dragon vanished, so suspicion of the Demon God was unavoidable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8494\" data-end=\"8518\"><em data-start=\"8494\" data-end=\"8518\">Where are you hiding…?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8520\" data-end=\"8576\">Zion searched for the demon from atop the fortress wall.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8578\" data-end=\"8658\">The kingdom’s attack methods and the magic within the airflow weren’t the issue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8660\" data-end=\"8765\">He simply needed to pinpoint its location quickly—everything would end once the Demon God was eliminated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8767\" data-end=\"8828\"><em data-start=\"8767\" data-end=\"8828\">At this scale… it must be using an enormous amount of mana…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8830\" data-end=\"8883\">The grey airflow carried the Demon God’s magic power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8885\" data-end=\"8940\">It spread widely and crept toward Eldran’s supply base.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8942\" data-end=\"9051\">Wherever the grey air touched, rot spread instantly, and beasts decayed into nothing without leaving corpses.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9053\" data-end=\"9116\">It had clearly resolved to eradicate the entire Allain Kingdom.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9118\" data-end=\"9176\"><em data-start=\"9118\" data-end=\"9176\">There’s no point where mana is gathering. What happened?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9178\" data-end=\"9241\">Normally, when magic was used, mana gathered around the caster.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9243\" data-end=\"9352\">But the Demon God was nowhere to be found— instead, the grey airflow itself carried evenly distributed magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9354\" data-end=\"9426\"><em data-start=\"9354\" data-end=\"9426\">The mana of the Four Great Calamities is mixed in… What have you done?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9428\" data-end=\"9491\">The caster couldn’t be killed, so the magic couldn’t dissipate.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9493\" data-end=\"9601\">If the power were limited, it would naturally run out—but there was no way the Demon God wouldn’t know that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9603\" data-end=\"9660\">Did it erase its own body while emitting limitless magic?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9662\" data-end=\"9730\"><em data-start=\"9662\" data-end=\"9730\">If the demon’s life was added to the power of the Four Calamities…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9732\" data-end=\"9759\">“You can’t find it either?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9761\" data-end=\"9801\">“I don’t think it exists to begin with.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9803\" data-end=\"9853\">“Could it be using magic by sacrificing its life?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9855\" data-end=\"9911\">“Maybe because it fused with the Four Great Calamities.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9913\" data-end=\"9947\">“Can you erase it with acid rain?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9949\" data-end=\"9991\">“That’ll be difficult without dark magic.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9993\" data-end=\"10013\">“Then I’ll step in.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10015\" data-end=\"10078\">Hanette released her mana, enveloping herself in golden flames.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10080\" data-end=\"10120\">She didn’t need to defeat it personally.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10122\" data-end=\"10194\">As long as the Demon God was subdued, she would obtain what she desired.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10196\" data-end=\"10292\"><em data-start=\"10196\" data-end=\"10292\">Once this is over, we can have our wedding. Anyone who gets in the way… I won’t let them live.</em></p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-186/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"203\">\r\n<p data-start=\"205\" data-end=\"241\"><strong data-start=\"205\" data-end=\"241\">Still unable to find the caster.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"319\">The gray airflow continued expanding its territory, eating away at the land.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"321\" data-end=\"403\">If left unchecked, it would reach Eldran’s supply base—and eventually the capital.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"408\" data-end=\"434\"><em data-start=\"408\" data-end=\"434\">“Isn’t that the caster?”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"436\" data-end=\"522\">Hanette had studied the gray stream several times before reaching a simple conclusion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"624\">The gray airflow existed as a manifested magical product—but there was no person acting as its base.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"738\">In other words, the Demon God might have <em data-start=\"667\" data-end=\"675\">become</em> the gray airflow itself, turning its form into magic and mana.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"743\" data-end=\"804\"><em data-start=\"743\" data-end=\"804\">“If there’s no shortage of mana… it can sustain that form.”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"806\" data-end=\"901\">He must have gained a massive amount of magical power by sacrificing his own body as the price.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"903\" data-end=\"1027\">The mana continuously turned into magic, and the gray airflow would gradually spread, devouring the continent of Caronbelaz.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1089\">It might even attempt to swallow the seas beyond Caronbelaz.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1131\"><em data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1131\">“I have to wipe it out completely.”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1226\">The Demon God had left behind nothing but mana, and that mana functioned as the gray airflow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1328\">Meaning: only when the gray airflow was completely eliminated would the Demon God finally disappear.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1409\">But the gray flow was still spreading, and erasing it all at once was not easy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1453\"><em data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1453\">“…Should I try to counterbalance it?”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1455\" data-end=\"1521\">Mana could be diminished and destroyed using mana of equal nature.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1523\" data-end=\"1649\">Magic born from mana followed the same rule: magic with higher concentration and magical power would overwhelm the weaker one.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1651\" data-end=\"1779\">But something like the gray airflow—produced endlessly—could only be suppressed with <em data-start=\"1736\" data-end=\"1742\">vast</em> magic power if one hoped for an end.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1784\" data-end=\"1839\"><em data-start=\"1784\" data-end=\"1839\">“There must be some kind of hidden ability involved.”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1841\" data-end=\"1895\">Since the enemy was a demon, she kept digging further.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1897\" data-end=\"2024\">It had invaded the capital of Allain, fully used its strange abilities, and now wielded the power of the Four Great Calamities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2026\" data-end=\"2089\">As Zion drowned in thought, he searched for more possibilities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2094\" data-end=\"2101\">“Zion.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2103\" data-end=\"2111\">“…What?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2113\" data-end=\"2142\">“Don’t do anything reckless.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2144\" data-end=\"2178\">“I haven’t done anything, have I?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2180\" data-end=\"2281\">“I said I’d let you get away with it twice. Starting the third time, you’d better be ready. Alright?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2283\" data-end=\"2288\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2290\" data-end=\"2338\">Zion swallowed his words and met Hanette’s eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2340\" data-end=\"2385\">Her golden irises burned with strong resolve.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2387\" data-end=\"2431\">Was that the determination to protect <em data-start=\"2425\" data-end=\"2430\">him</em>?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2436\" data-end=\"2557\">“You’re the one who asked me to wait. You’re the one who said you loved me. I won’t let you be taken away from me again.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2559\" data-end=\"2570\">“…Alright.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2572\" data-end=\"2623\">For now, it was impossible to use <em data-start=\"2606\" data-end=\"2622\">that technique</em>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2625\" data-end=\"2693\">It needed a target to execute, but the target wasn’t showing itself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2695\" data-end=\"2763\">Most importantly—he couldn’t afford to die and leave Hanette behind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2768\" data-end=\"2788\"><em data-start=\"2768\" data-end=\"2788\">I planned to stop…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2790\" data-end=\"2860\">Hanette circulated mana inside her body, then released it explosively.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2862\" data-end=\"2943\">The golden flames split into dozens of branches, spreading outward from the city.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2945\" data-end=\"3036\">Where the flames touched the earth, long lines formed as they connected into a massive web.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3038\" data-end=\"3123\">Then at some point, a great wall of flame rose, covering the entire area around them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3128\" data-end=\"3155\"><em data-start=\"3128\" data-end=\"3155\">“Then I’ll push forward.”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3157\" data-end=\"3223\">In an instant, the gray airflow collided with the barrier of fire.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3225\" data-end=\"3291\">It tried to advance further—but the flames refused to let it pass.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3293\" data-end=\"3362\">The gray stream accumulated over time, its momentum growing stronger.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3367\" data-end=\"3407\"><em data-start=\"3367\" data-end=\"3407\">Just as I thought… This won’t be easy.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3409\" data-end=\"3467\">She wondered if the difference lay in sheer magical power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3469\" data-end=\"3571\">Her own magic was not weak—but her enemy was a demon saturated with the powers of the Four Calamities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3576\" data-end=\"3618\"><em data-start=\"3576\" data-end=\"3618\">Would it make a difference if I held on?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3620\" data-end=\"3703\">Even if many knights and mages worked together, they couldn’t overpower this force.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3705\" data-end=\"3730\">It would merely buy time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3732\" data-end=\"3834\">Even if all arcane sword wielders and Setinos Quasar users gathered… wouldn’t the same outcome repeat?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3839\" data-end=\"3869\"><em data-start=\"3839\" data-end=\"3869\">It would just waste my mana.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3871\" data-end=\"3909\">Block until her mana ran out, retreat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3911\" data-end=\"3962\">Recover mana, raise flames again, slow the advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3964\" data-end=\"4060\">Repeat that, and eventually exhaustion would set in—and they would fall back toward the capital.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4065\" data-end=\"4113\"><em data-start=\"4065\" data-end=\"4113\">Even awakening the arcane sword… isn’t enough?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4115\" data-end=\"4191\">The demon’s immortality was broken, Brecht’s flames burned hotter than ever.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4193\" data-end=\"4256\">But even with overwhelming strength, victory wasn’t guaranteed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4258\" data-end=\"4355\">The Demon God had transcended life and death. No one knew the source of its endless magical fuel.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4360\" data-end=\"4396\"><em data-start=\"4360\" data-end=\"4396\">If I don’t finish this… Zion will—</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4483\">“Don’t overdo it. If you can’t defeat it now, you need to conserve your strength.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4485\" data-end=\"4531\">“But if we kill it now, we reduce the damage—”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4533\" data-end=\"4543\">“Hanette.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4545\" data-end=\"4575\">A firm voice pierced her ears.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4577\" data-end=\"4621\">Hanette pushed aside her anxiety and turned.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4623\" data-end=\"4673\">Zion held her shoulders, his gaze calm and steady.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4678\" data-end=\"4765\">“I’m still alive. I’m not hurt, and I know better than to act stupid. So listen to me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4767\" data-end=\"4772\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4774\" data-end=\"4822\">She regained clarity and steadied her breathing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4824\" data-end=\"4887\">She and Zion were sent to Eldran’s supply base as the vanguard.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4889\" data-end=\"4974\">It would be fortunate if they could finish things here—but if not, retreat was wiser.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4976\" data-end=\"5071\">The other arcane sword users, Setinos Quasar warriors, and reinforcements weren’t gathered yet.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5076\" data-end=\"5125\">“Do you remember when the demon swords gathered?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5127\" data-end=\"5141\">“…I remember.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5143\" data-end=\"5191\">“It hasn’t happened yet. Now might be the time.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5193\" data-end=\"5274\">Considering the timing and the conditions, this might be the most fitting moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5276\" data-end=\"5350\">An unseen enemy. A world-devouring force. A fight impossible to win alone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5352\" data-end=\"5457\">The situation was so one-sided and disadvantageous that they were forced to prepare for the final resort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5462\" data-end=\"5490\">“You mean… we have to wait?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5492\" data-end=\"5618\">“Exactly. We wait until everyone gathers. If we waste our strength now, we won’t be able to fight when the true moment comes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"5649\">Brandis and Uter were absent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5651\" data-end=\"5717\">Among the Setinos Quasar present, only Zion and Enrite were there.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5719\" data-end=\"5781\">The demon’s attack had just begun—it likely wouldn’t end soon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5783\" data-end=\"5816\">Acting rashly now would be fatal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5821\" data-end=\"5829\">“…Haaa…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5831\" data-end=\"5888\">Hanette bit her lip as she stared at the towering flames.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5890\" data-end=\"5948\">The gray airflow had grown stronger, but still manageable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5950\" data-end=\"5997\">And Zion’s reasoning was too precise to ignore.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6002\" data-end=\"6111\">“You’re stronger than me. Maybe the strongest of all arcane sword wielders. You need to conserve your power.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6113\" data-end=\"6135\">“…I’ll do as you say.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6137\" data-end=\"6193\">Hanette extinguished her flames and suppressed her mana.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6195\" data-end=\"6268\">The accumulated gray airflow surged forward, spreading in all directions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6270\" data-end=\"6356\">It advanced rapidly toward Eldran’s supply base, terrifying the soldiers into retreat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6361\" data-end=\"6390\">“Enrite, we should withdraw.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6392\" data-end=\"6453\">“Yes. We need to discuss countermeasures back at the castle.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6455\" data-end=\"6504\">Enrite had discerned the nature of the gray flow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6506\" data-end=\"6537\">It was strange, alien, cunning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6539\" data-end=\"6597\">Why was the Demon God so obsessed with total annihilation?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6602\" data-end=\"6647\"><em data-start=\"6602\" data-end=\"6647\">You can’t kill it with magic or mana alone…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6649\" data-end=\"6674\">Only one answer remained.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6676\" data-end=\"6733\">Zion knew it too—hence his immediate command to withdraw.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6735\" data-end=\"6796\">And as arcane sword wielders, they had no choice but to obey.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6801\" data-end=\"6858\"><em data-start=\"6801\" data-end=\"6858\">The time has come—to create salvation and destroy evil.</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6860\" data-end=\"6863\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6865\" data-end=\"6917\"><strong data-start=\"6865\" data-end=\"6917\">Rear Region of the Allain Kingdom — Keod Castle.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6919\" data-end=\"6985\">The troops from Eldran’s supply base retreated to the rear castle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6987\" data-end=\"7047\">Border regions stayed alert, preparing to flee if necessary.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7049\" data-end=\"7182\">The gray airflow expanded outward from the point where the slime dragon vanished, sweeping Eldran’s base and several nearby villages.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7187\" data-end=\"7257\">“…It’s not a bad sight. There were losses, but not the worst outcome.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7259\" data-end=\"7318\">Receiving the reports, Brandis arrived late at Keod Castle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7320\" data-end=\"7403\">Juter and Barhen followed, and the Royal Knights and the capital’s forces gathered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7405\" data-end=\"7479\">Troops from around the world would soon reinforce each castle and outpost.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7484\" data-end=\"7649\">“Your Majesty, we are not yet directly affected, but the future is grim. Unfortunately, we cannot resolve this simply by gathering arcane swords and their wielders.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7651\" data-end=\"7696\">“You’re right. We need to find another path.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7698\" data-end=\"7762\">Enrite, Brandis, and the other arcane sword wielders understood.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7764\" data-end=\"7835\">The prophecy spoken by the seven demon swords only stated the <em data-start=\"7826\" data-end=\"7834\">result</em>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7837\" data-end=\"7903\">The <em data-start=\"7841\" data-end=\"7849\">method</em> or <em data-start=\"7853\" data-end=\"7862\">process</em> to reach that result was never detailed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7905\" data-end=\"7982\">Only the fact that seven demon swords and seven wielders existed was certain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7987\" data-end=\"8041\">“Isn’t it something we can figure out while fighting?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8043\" data-end=\"8094\">Hanette reached that conclusion after much thought.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8096\" data-end=\"8161\">If the answer wasn’t written, then they would find it themselves.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8163\" data-end=\"8227\">Even if they struggled, fell, or suffered—they had to persevere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8298\">Only then would enlightenment appear amidst frustration and hardship.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8303\" data-end=\"8410\">“Hahaha! That’s right! Sitting still won’t give you answers. You learn only by touching the fire yourself!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8412\" data-end=\"8442\">Brandis sat with satisfaction.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8444\" data-end=\"8502\">No amount of discussion or planning would change anything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8504\" data-end=\"8576\">They had to move, to fight, to pour everything into defeating the enemy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8578\" data-end=\"8627\">Time spent hesitating would only increase losses.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8632\" data-end=\"8677\">“I’ll trust you. And I want you to trust me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8679\" data-end=\"8712\">With that, Brandis took the lead.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8714\" data-end=\"8778\">The arcane sword wielders followed, stopping at the castle gate.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8783\" data-end=\"8977\">“I will organize the decisions made. Ban direct contact with the gray aura—fight while keeping distance. If it becomes untenable, abandon the castle and retreat. If anyone disagrees, speak now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8979\" data-end=\"9002\">Silence filled the air.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9004\" data-end=\"9071\">Soldiers watched from the walls, and the Royal Knights stood ready.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9073\" data-end=\"9133\">Meanwhile, Hanette stared at the open gate, deep in thought.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9138\" data-end=\"9159\"><em data-start=\"9138\" data-end=\"9159\">…Why am I fighting?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9161\" data-end=\"9234\">At first, she sought to defeat the demon for recognition from her family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9236\" data-end=\"9319\">She wasn’t a foolish young girl—she was a magician, capable of making her own name.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9321\" data-end=\"9380\">Even without political marriage, she could prove her worth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9382\" data-end=\"9475\">But somewhere along the way, that purpose changed—and after achieving it, she had no regrets.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9480\" data-end=\"9541\"><em data-start=\"9480\" data-end=\"9541\">I thought I’d only marry after I became stronger than Zion.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9543\" data-end=\"9601\">Hanette stepped outside the castle, staying close to Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9603\" data-end=\"9697\">Perhaps because this felt like the final battle, memories and emotions overflowed in her head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9699\" data-end=\"9756\">She should’ve been married by now, yet she kept delaying.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9758\" data-end=\"9790\">What had frightened her so much?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9795\" data-end=\"9841\"><em data-start=\"9795\" data-end=\"9841\">Even if I trust Zion… I didn’t trust myself.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9843\" data-end=\"9873\">Marriage itself terrified her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9875\" data-end=\"9964\">It was an unwanted engagement at first, and she couldn’t predict what would happen after.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9966\" data-end=\"10038\">Sharing a room with Zion. Having children. Spending a lifetime together.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10040\" data-end=\"10069\">What if she ended up unhappy?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10074\" data-end=\"10119\"><em data-start=\"10074\" data-end=\"10119\">Now… I think I understand why I must fight.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10121\" data-end=\"10195\">Hanette turned from the slowly approaching gray airflow and looked inward.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10197\" data-end=\"10251\">No matter what happened to the world—it didn’t matter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10253\" data-end=\"10317\">Even if family or friends died, some things were beyond control.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10319\" data-end=\"10348\">She only needed <em data-start=\"10335\" data-end=\"10340\">one</em> person.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10353\" data-end=\"10377\"><em data-start=\"10353\" data-end=\"10377\">Zion… I only need you.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10379\" data-end=\"10409\">She stood here for Zion alone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10411\" data-end=\"10472\">As long as she was by his side, despair would never take her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10474\" data-end=\"10526\">And through that hope—a new future could take shape.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10531\" data-end=\"10588\"><em data-start=\"10531\" data-end=\"10588\">I don’t care about this world. I’ll fight only for you.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10590\" data-end=\"10639\">Hanette recalled her resolve and summoned Brecht.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10641\" data-end=\"10694\">Flames surged violently, blazing in brilliant colors.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10699\" data-end=\"10787\">— <em data-start=\"10701\" data-end=\"10787\">A desire cannot be satisfied by a reason. A selfish heart causes desire to overflow.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10789\" data-end=\"10824\">A strange voice echoed in her mind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10826\" data-end=\"10858\">Hanette looked around, startled.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10863\" data-end=\"10983\">— <em data-start=\"10865\" data-end=\"10983\">But your desire… You think only of your own comfort and that of one person. Is that not both selfish and altruistic?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10985\" data-end=\"11023\">Brecht spread its wings and cried out.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11025\" data-end=\"11095\">Then the four other demon swords reacted—each radiating its own color.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11100\" data-end=\"11114\">“This… what…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11116\" data-end=\"11123\">“What?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11125\" data-end=\"11136\">“This is…!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11141\" data-end=\"11256\">— <em data-start=\"11143\" data-end=\"11256\">Your desire overflows, yet it endlessly sinks. You wish to fill it but cannot; you wish to empty it but cannot.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11258\" data-end=\"11391\">Ferundira, the ice demon sword.<br data-start=\"11289\" data-end=\"11292\">\r\nPaku, the lightning demon sword.<br data-start=\"11324\" data-end=\"11327\">\r\nTimer, the wind demon sword.<br data-start=\"11355\" data-end=\"11358\">\r\nGerganber, the earth demon sword.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11393\" data-end=\"11429\">Their colors gathered toward Brecht.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11431\" data-end=\"11457\">Enrite watched, murmuring:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11462\" data-end=\"11525\">“The one who inherits the five sources… will create salvation.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11530\" data-end=\"11633\">— <em data-start=\"11532\" data-end=\"11633\">How can you save others if you do not value yourself? There is no salvation without a life to save.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11635\" data-end=\"11680\">Enveloped by five lights, Brecht transformed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11682\" data-end=\"11740\">Hanette whispered the word <em data-start=\"11709\" data-end=\"11720\">salvation</em>, watching silently.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11745\" data-end=\"11827\">— <em data-start=\"11747\" data-end=\"11827\">Save yourself, and those you wish to protect. And by creating salvation… live.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11829\" data-end=\"11858\">Brecht became a single blade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11860\" data-end=\"11954\">Gold, sky-blue, yellow, pale green, and brown fused into one, radiating immense magical power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11956\" data-end=\"11988\">Hanette knew its name instantly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11993\" data-end=\"12026\">“The Sword of Salvation… Isruen…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12028\" data-end=\"12069\">She gripped the hilt and took her stance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12071\" data-end=\"12099\">It was not a weapon to kill.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12101\" data-end=\"12164\">It was a sword to guide the world to salvation and recreate it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12166\" data-end=\"12191\">She swung Isruen lightly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12193\" data-end=\"12261\">A beautiful five-colored light shot forth, piercing the gray stream.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12263\" data-end=\"12324\">Dry lands turned lush again, and rotting trees regained life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12329\" data-end=\"12334\">“Ah…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12336\" data-end=\"12359\">“It’s impressive, but…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12361\" data-end=\"12418\">The gray airflow persisted—then reversed the restoration.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12420\" data-end=\"12476\">The land decayed again, trees shriveled, colors drained.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12478\" data-end=\"12521\">Zion frowned and recalled another prophecy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12526\" data-end=\"12589\"><em data-start=\"12526\" data-end=\"12589\">“He who embraces both light and darkness shall destroy evil.”</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12591\" data-end=\"12638\">Salvation alone—Isruen alone—couldn’t end this.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12640\" data-end=\"12716\">No matter how many times she restored, the gray flow would corrupt it again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12718\" data-end=\"12789\">In the end, either he or Enrite had to inherit light and darkness both.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12794\" data-end=\"12816\"><em data-start=\"12794\" data-end=\"12816\">I must help Hanette.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12818\" data-end=\"12836\">Isruen had limits.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12838\" data-end=\"12923\">Even if she used it endlessly, even if she suppressed the gray flow—it wasn’t enough.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12925\" data-end=\"12966\">She would use Isruen until it killed her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"12971\" data-end=\"13017\"><em data-start=\"12971\" data-end=\"13017\">I didn’t come all this way to watch her die.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13019\" data-end=\"13089\">The first time he prepared to die, he learned what was truly precious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13091\" data-end=\"13151\">The second time he thought of death, he burned with revenge.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13153\" data-end=\"13215\">He would rather abandon the world than lose what he treasured.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13220\" data-end=\"13330\"><em data-start=\"13220\" data-end=\"13330\">I will protect my partner. If the world cannot be lived in by her, then the world does not deserve to exist.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13335\" data-end=\"13361\">— <em data-start=\"13337\" data-end=\"13361\">Is that your darkness?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13363\" data-end=\"13389\">A strange voice whispered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13391\" data-end=\"13441\">Zion gripped his hilt and searched for its source.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13446\" data-end=\"13550\">— <em data-start=\"13448\" data-end=\"13550\">There must be both light and darkness in the world. If only light existed, could it be called light?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13552\" data-end=\"13556\">“…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13561\" data-end=\"13708\">— <em data-start=\"13563\" data-end=\"13708\">Brightness alone is not goodness. Warmth does not guarantee life. Without darkness, light cannot be felt. One must overcome cold to reach life.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13710\" data-end=\"13715\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13717\" data-end=\"13763\">It was strange logic—yet strangely convincing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13765\" data-end=\"13787\">Still, he felt uneasy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13792\" data-end=\"13821\"><em data-start=\"13792\" data-end=\"13821\">What are you trying to say?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13826\" data-end=\"13886\">— <em data-start=\"13828\" data-end=\"13886\">Your darkness… contains light. Do you know why they mix?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13888\" data-end=\"13906\"><em data-start=\"13888\" data-end=\"13906\">Why ask me that?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"13911\" data-end=\"14087\">— <em data-start=\"13913\" data-end=\"14087\">You recognize evil clearly. You understand truth hidden in endless hatred. Those who have malice but pretend goodness are praised as saints. Fools cannot see hidden hatred.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14089\" data-end=\"14094\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14099\" data-end=\"14219\">— <em data-start=\"14101\" data-end=\"14219\">But you… show goodness as malice. You keep hatred for yourself, and goodwill for others. Is that not deeply selfish?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14221\" data-end=\"14323\"><em data-start=\"14221\" data-end=\"14323\">I’m not foolish enough to live for others. For myself, my partner, and my comrades—I’ll hold hatred.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14328\" data-end=\"14469\">— <em data-start=\"14330\" data-end=\"14469\">Then use that to destroy evil. Evil must be erased as evil. Fools try to erase evil with kindness. And… do you not have goodness as well?</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14471\" data-end=\"14517\">As the voice spoke, Acid Rain shone deep blue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14519\" data-end=\"14565\">At the same time, El Tesoicb shimmered silver.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14570\" data-end=\"14640\">— <em data-start=\"14572\" data-end=\"14640\">Destroy hatred with your hatred. And temper it with your goodwill.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14642\" data-end=\"14669\">“It’s time… to release it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14671\" data-end=\"14717\">Enrite released El Tesoicb without hesitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14719\" data-end=\"14788\">The blade shot forth, and Zion intuitively reached out and seized it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14793\" data-end=\"14831\"><em data-start=\"14793\" data-end=\"14831\">There is only one thing I must kill.</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14833\" data-end=\"14888\">Zion accepted his fate—Acid Rain and El Tesoicb merged.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14890\" data-end=\"14943\">Indigo and silver intertwined, forming something new.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14948\" data-end=\"14953\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14955\" data-end=\"14996\">Only a blue hilt remained in Zion’s hand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"14998\" data-end=\"15039\">There was no blade at all—only emptiness.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15041\" data-end=\"15096\">Still, Zion raised his arm, preparing a horizontal cut.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15101\" data-end=\"15142\"><em data-start=\"15101\" data-end=\"15142\">The Sword of Destruction… Lynn Neygarn…</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15144\" data-end=\"15190\">He swung it without channeling a drop of mana.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15192\" data-end=\"15229\">A colossal arc carved across reality.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15231\" data-end=\"15304\">It stretched across this land, the Allain Kingdom, and all of Caronbelaz.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15309\" data-end=\"15346\">“Even if you’re already dead… demon.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15348\" data-end=\"15428\">The enormous invisible blade passed through all things—and struck the gray flow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15430\" data-end=\"15492\">The Sword of Destruction, Lynn Neygarn, destroyed only <em data-start=\"15485\" data-end=\"15491\">evil</em>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15494\" data-end=\"15544\">Thus, anything not judged evil remained untouched.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15546\" data-end=\"15609\">Lynn Neygarn cleaved the gray flow, slicing to the far horizon.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15611\" data-end=\"15685\">The split gray stream vanished instantly—never returning, never reforming.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15687\" data-end=\"15741\">Because the flow itself was pure evil, it met its end.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15746\" data-end=\"15760\">“Th-that was…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15762\" data-end=\"15777\">“Unbelievable…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15779\" data-end=\"15820\">“To think I’d witness this before dying…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15822\" data-end=\"15845\">It lasted but a moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15847\" data-end=\"15923\">The gray airflow vanished completely—<br data-start=\"15884\" data-end=\"15887\">\r\nThe decaying world reverted to life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"15925\" data-end=\"16010\">Isruen reverted back into Brecht,<br data-start=\"15958\" data-end=\"15961\">\r\nLynn Neygarn separated into its two demon swords.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16015\" data-end=\"16022\">“…Wow…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16024\" data-end=\"16031\">“…Haa…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16033\" data-end=\"16099\">Zion and Hanette let out heavy breaths, meeting each other’s eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16101\" data-end=\"16133\">In the end, the demon was slain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16135\" data-end=\"16159\">Only one thing remained.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16164\" data-end=\"16196\">“How about… we get married now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16198\" data-end=\"16222\">“Then give me the ring.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16224\" data-end=\"16245\">“…I didn’t bring it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16247\" data-end=\"16276\">“Why didn’t you prepare it!?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16278\" data-end=\"16325\">“I came to fight—who carries a ring in battle?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16327\" data-end=\"16360\">“You really can’t read the mood.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16362\" data-end=\"16379\">“Don’t force me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16381\" data-end=\"16390\">“Hahaha!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16392\" data-end=\"16434\">Brandis laughed heartily as he approached.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16436\" data-end=\"16489\">Many had suffered—but these two were the true heroes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16491\" data-end=\"16557\">It was a royal wedding, and he wanted to see it with his own eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16562\" data-end=\"16649\">“By royal decree—I shall officiate the marriage of Zion Reggiard and Hanette Adelaira!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16651\" data-end=\"16657\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16659\" data-end=\"16665\">“Huh?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16667\" data-end=\"16729\">Zion, Hanette—and even the soldiers on the walls—were stunned.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16731\" data-end=\"16785\">Enrite laughed, Uter remained calm as if expecting it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16787\" data-end=\"16836\">Lecia watched the two with a small spark of envy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"16841\" data-end=\"16893\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><em data-start=\"16841\" data-end=\"16893\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Love… sounds wonderful. Maybe I should try it too?</em></p></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-187/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"87\" data-end=\"90\">\r\n<p data-start=\"92\" data-end=\"136\"><strong data-start=\"92\" data-end=\"136\">Duke Adelaira’s Residence, Banquet Hall.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"138\" data-end=\"236\">To prepare for the wedding, we continued discussing the venue, schedule, costs, and decorations.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"370\">Zion and Hanette didn’t say anything, but the heads and wives of the two families took the lead, trying to make all the decisions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"492\">Both could be satisfied simply by getting married, so they quietly observed the process until the wedding day arrived.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"494\" data-end=\"519\">“Ah… the day has come.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"576\">Hanette bit her lip as she sat at the dressing table.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"578\" data-end=\"654\">This time, instead of wearing a suit, she wore a pure white wedding dress.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"656\" data-end=\"743\">Only five maids were assigned to take care of things like makeup, hair, and clothing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"839\">She knew this day would come someday, but now she was overwhelmed with pressure and anxiety.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"882\">“If you said you wouldn’t do it now… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"941\">Hanette was flustered but still retained her composure.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"943\" data-end=\"986\">A flood of emotions clouded her judgment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1067\">However, because of her firm trust in Zion, she somehow managed to endure it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1069\" data-end=\"1085\">“How is Zion?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1087\" data-end=\"1155\">Perhaps he has arranged even the smallest details to suit himself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1157\" data-end=\"1243\">She wondered if she could even be aware of herself despite having the same thoughts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1312\">But until they met and spoke, she was uncertain about everything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1314\" data-end=\"1378\">“When will you arrive? Still, I think it ended sooner for me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1427\">She hadn’t seen Zion since entering the room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1511\">It took longer than usual to get ready, and there were many things to attend to.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1619\">She had visited Robens, Yenid, Dain, Enrithe, Lesia, Oz, and Uter, but she hadn’t even seen Zion’s face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1621\" data-end=\"1667\">“Well… maybe he’s busy entertaining guests.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1669\" data-end=\"1747\">Of course, only a few people could truly be considered close to him or Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1749\" data-end=\"1834\">At most, family, the Lihine knights, and Setinos Quasar would encompass everything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1836\" data-end=\"1957\">However, because connections formed by the families attended the wedding, Zion had no choice but to interact with them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1959\" data-end=\"2003\">“Better to only invite people you know… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2005\" data-end=\"2046\">She didn’t want an extravagant wedding.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2048\" data-end=\"2148\">She just wanted to complete it quietly and receive congratulations only from people she knew well.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2150\" data-end=\"2267\">However, as the daughter of Duke Setinos Quasar and a conqueror of demons, many people had no choice but to gather.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2269\" data-end=\"2315\">“How could you show me something like this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2317\" data-end=\"2361\">Light makeup and a suit always suited him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2446\">Originally, she even wanted to refuse the wedding dress, but she couldn’t resist.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2448\" data-end=\"2514\">Even if Zion understood, he couldn’t ruin this one-time wedding.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2516\" data-end=\"2576\">“After the wedding, I also have to spend the first night.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2578\" data-end=\"2625\">There was something scarier than the wedding.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2627\" data-end=\"2720\">Tonight would be spent in the same room as Zion, and the journey would only begin tomorrow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2722\" data-end=\"2811\">She had no choice but to go through it, though she wasn’t sure if she could do it well.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2813\" data-end=\"2842\">“Oh, I want to run away… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2889\">There was a knock on the door from outside.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2891\" data-end=\"2963\">Hanette waited for the door to open with an odd sense of anticipation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2965\" data-end=\"3014\">“Sorry, but could you step aside for a moment?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3079\">Hearing the familiar voice, the maids bowed and quickly left.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3081\" data-end=\"3157\">Hanette caught a glimpse of a shadow in the mirror and hurriedly crouched.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3159\" data-end=\"3183\">“Why did you do that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3185\" data-end=\"3203\">“…I don’t know.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3205\" data-end=\"3229\">“Are you embarrassed?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3231\" data-end=\"3256\">“Because I don’t know.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3258\" data-end=\"3290\">“Can you still show it to me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3292\" data-end=\"3311\">“You look awful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3313\" data-end=\"3348\">“Are you always beautiful to me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3350\" data-end=\"3359\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3419\">Hanette slowly turned and made eye contact with someone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3421\" data-end=\"3470\">Zion, wearing a black suit, was staring at her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3472\" data-end=\"3549\">It was a wedding dress, but she thought it looked beautiful in its own way.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3551\" data-end=\"3606\">“Are you embarrassed about your makeup or the dress?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3608\" data-end=\"3617\">“Both.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3619\" data-end=\"3655\">“Hmm… the dress looks fine to me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3657\" data-end=\"3689\">Zion smiled and looked closer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3691\" data-end=\"3755\">Her makeup was darker than usual, but it didn’t feel overdone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3757\" data-end=\"3833\">The wedding dress replaced the suit, yet looked elegant and sophisticated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3835\" data-end=\"3938\">Also, because she was embarrassed about her tied-up hair, she was reminded that the wedding was near.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3940\" data-end=\"3954\">“Don’t lie.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3956\" data-end=\"4052\">“Alright. Then I’ll be honest. It would be better to wear it as before, but now it’s not bad.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4054\" data-end=\"4071\">“You think so?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4073\" data-end=\"4199\">“The suit suits you. It would be better if you let your hair down too. But I think it’s fine because there’s a new feeling?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4201\" data-end=\"4220\">“If it’s fine… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4222\" data-end=\"4289\">At that moment, Hanette straightened her back and looked at Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4291\" data-end=\"4340\">Zion slowly bent down and held Hanette’s hands.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4342\" data-end=\"4392\">“Can’t you regret it? I have many shortcomings.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4394\" data-end=\"4457\">“That’s exactly what I want to say. Can you really marry me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4459\" data-end=\"4493\">“I can’t say I won’t do it now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4495\" data-end=\"4525\">“It seems like you hate me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4527\" data-end=\"4575\">Hanette replied briefly and narrowed her eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4577\" data-end=\"4619\">Zion laughed and touched Hanette’s hand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4714\">“Do you know why? If I didn’t marry you, I wouldn’t be able to bear it because I’d be sad.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4716\" data-end=\"4742\">“Below! You speak well.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4744\" data-end=\"4805\">“I won’t ask for anything. Just… stay by my side. Can you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4807\" data-end=\"4829\">“…So, you’re ready.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4831\" data-end=\"4890\">Hanette was satisfied with his answer and smiled quietly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4892\" data-end=\"4971\">She had been waiting for this day, and Zion had also considered her position.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4973\" data-end=\"5065\">Since she had been patient for a long time, shouldn’t she also listen to what Zion wanted?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5067\" data-end=\"5084\">“There… hey… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5086\" data-end=\"5116\">“Why? Do you have concerns?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5118\" data-end=\"5166\">“After the wedding… That… that… what… that… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5168\" data-end=\"5177\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5179\" data-end=\"5249\">Zion immediately understood her words and wore a serious expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5251\" data-end=\"5303\">He had already made promises to Hanette about her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5305\" data-end=\"5415\">Most importantly, she wanted to rest after the wedding, so she thought she would stay silent for the moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5417\" data-end=\"5511\">“Have we talked about this before? You asked me what I would do with Husa when I was drunk.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5513\" data-end=\"5534\">“Eh… eh, just now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5536\" data-end=\"5660\">“My thoughts are the same as then. I don’t want to have an heir if you don’t like it. Raising a child isn’t an easy task.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5662\" data-end=\"5678\">“That’s true.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5680\" data-end=\"5779\">“If… Alright… really, if you change your mind… Then I will reconsider. Could that be the answer?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5781\" data-end=\"5830\">Zion responded seriously and reassured Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5832\" data-end=\"6017\">Considering the purpose of the arranged marriage, they should have a child first, but both families wouldn’t interfere recklessly due to their established reputation and achievements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6019\" data-end=\"6149\">On the contrary, he wondered if he would care for himself and Hanette for a few years before carefully mentioning the successor.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6151\" data-end=\"6183\">“Have you ever had any ideas?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6185\" data-end=\"6282\">“Not really. I want to play while I’m young. Better if you have a beautiful wife by your side.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6284\" data-end=\"6321\">“Is there anything you want to do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6323\" data-end=\"6345\">“Anything with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6347\" data-end=\"6382\">“…Thank you. I should do better.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6384\" data-end=\"6445\">“You’re already doing well. What do you want to do better?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6447\" data-end=\"6506\">“I’m not doing good things. You’re the one who leads me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6508\" data-end=\"6562\">Hanette reached out and gently stroked Zion’s cheek.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6564\" data-end=\"6625\">Many people hailed him as a hero who achieved great things.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6627\" data-end=\"6684\">Yet, he didn’t act deliberately and only followed Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6686\" data-end=\"6760\">All these accomplishments were close to what Zion achieved, not herself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6762\" data-end=\"6808\">“Do you feel a little more comfortable now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6810\" data-end=\"6838\">“I think I can endure it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6840\" data-end=\"6874\">“Let’s finish quickly and rest.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6876\" data-end=\"6898\">“Yes, that’s right.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6900\" data-end=\"6950\">They fell silent, gazing at each other lovingly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6952\" data-end=\"6998\">All that remained was to enjoy a happy life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7000\" data-end=\"7065\">There would be much work ahead, but even that would be enjoyed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7067\" data-end=\"7128\">Because they would be together for the rest of their lives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7130\" data-end=\"7201\">“I must do everything I can before I grow old. I don’t want regrets.”</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"7203\" data-end=\"7206\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7208\" data-end=\"7252\"><strong data-start=\"7208\" data-end=\"7252\">Duke Adelaira’s Residence, Banquet Hall.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7254\" data-end=\"7297\">Zion and Hanette’s wedding went smoothly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7299\" data-end=\"7458\">The distinguished guests were full of connections from the Duke of Adelaira and Marquis of Reggiard, including the immediate royal family and Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7460\" data-end=\"7546\">Enrite presided over the wedding ceremony, and Brandis led it by the king’s command.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7548\" data-end=\"7716\">“…With this, the engagement of Zion Reggiard and Hanette Adelaira is officially concluded. As a sign of this engagement, please exchange these gifts with each other.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7718\" data-end=\"7791\">Brandis finished his speech and handed them a box containing the rings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7793\" data-end=\"7859\">Zion and Hanette politely received the box and opened it slowly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7861\" data-end=\"7944\">Zion placed the ring on Hanette first, and Hanette followed, giving him his ring.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7946\" data-end=\"8091\">“You have both witnessed the engagement certificate being ratified. Nothing can dissolve this engagement, and not even death can separate you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8093\" data-end=\"8144\">Brandis glanced at Enrite and gave a subtle wink.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8146\" data-end=\"8199\">Enrite immediately understood and opened his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8201\" data-end=\"8242\">“Next will be the inauguration speech.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8244\" data-end=\"8257\">“Hehehe… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8259\" data-end=\"8341\">Brandis cleared his throat and looked down at the ceremony door from the podium.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8343\" data-end=\"8373\">Not many words were written.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8375\" data-end=\"8447\">If it’s too long, it becomes boring; if too short, it loses authority.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8449\" data-end=\"8527\">That’s why he only said what was necessary and told them to proceed quickly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8529\" data-end=\"8737\">“Marriage is noble, but also something often seen. Can’t a man and woman promise marriage as long as they love each other? However, because you carry the lives of others, you must not make hasty decisions.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8739\" data-end=\"8803\">Brandis began reading the inauguration text in a serious tone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8805\" data-end=\"8870\">The distinguished guests listened intently, not even breathing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8872\" data-end=\"8961\">It was an inauguration ceremony by the king’s will, and it was not to be taken lightly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8963\" data-end=\"9167\">“These two dedicate themselves to the kingdom of Allain, and through that, the evil monsters have been subdued. I decided to officiate this ceremony myself to honor their sacrifice and accomplishments.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9169\" data-end=\"9236\">Brandis paused, glancing back and forth between Zion and Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9238\" data-end=\"9322\">The marriage of a high noble’s son and a beautiful noblewoman was nearly complete.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9324\" data-end=\"9420\">What the future held for them was unknown, but their feelings for each other would not change.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9422\" data-end=\"9644\">“I hope neither of them goes to the battlefield in the future. During that time, they’ve fought many battles, crossing limbs. It would be sad to die without marrying, but you can’t let someone die after marriage, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9646\" data-end=\"9712\">Of course, this wasn’t something Brandis could control entirely.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9714\" data-end=\"9830\">In emergencies, not only would Setinos Quasar, but also additional troops, have to be deployed to the front lines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9832\" data-end=\"9930\">Because Zion and Hanette were major powers, one wondered if they would be summoned in some form.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9932\" data-end=\"10107\">“…Unfortunately, I have no advice to give about marriage. My way isn’t necessarily right, and the obvious way isn’t helpful. Isn’t it nice to slowly get to know each other?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10109\" data-end=\"10170\">Brandis closed the ceremony doors, leaving the final words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10172\" data-end=\"10227\">Even without reading the text, the message was clear.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10229\" data-end=\"10268\">Everything he wanted to say was here.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10270\" data-end=\"10765\">“It’s not that there’s no personal desire. If something bothers you, try stepping away for a while, then meet again to talk. That will make things better. Don’t assume love has cooled just because your longing has weakened. It means you’ve become accustomed to each other and become true partners. Finally… make sure you have more than one child. The more, the better, but not zero. Isn’t this country and family only prosperous if there are many descendants carrying both of your bloodlines?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10767\" data-end=\"10785\">“Eh… alright… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10787\" data-end=\"10796\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10798\" data-end=\"10848\">Brandis slowly stepped back, leaving them shyly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10850\" data-end=\"10926\">His role was over, and now all that remained was to complete the marriage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10928\" data-end=\"11046\">Zion and Hanette would live together as husband and wife, and their descendants would continue to serve the country.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11048\" data-end=\"11130\">“Even fewer than two. Shouldn’t there be at least three more? No, about four… …”</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-188/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"105\" data-end=\"108\">\r\n<p data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"182\"><strong data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"182\">Cathedral of the Holy Kinesien Order, Office of the Second Cardinal.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"184\" data-end=\"275\">Right after the wedding ended, Enrite returned to the office together with Lesia and Seran.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"277\" data-end=\"410\">The demon beasts still remained outside the outskirts, but the 3 great demons and 4 great calamities had been completely annihilated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"412\" data-end=\"529\">The Demon God would no longer be able to rise again, and the frontline forces would be able to stop the Demon Beasts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"531\" data-end=\"571\">“Is a wedding supposed to be like this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"573\" data-end=\"631\">“Not all of them are the same… but the method is similar.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"633\" data-end=\"662\">“Were there too many humans?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"664\" data-end=\"780\">“The color was black, and there were reins, so yes, there were many. Didn’t you see another wedding a few days ago?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"782\" data-end=\"861\">“Ah. The ice magic sword? I didn’t understand it very well, so I just watched.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"863\" data-end=\"870\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"872\" data-end=\"906\">Enrite sighed and sat at the desk.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"908\" data-end=\"1029\">Given the scale of the wedding and the number of invited guests, Juter and Barchen’s wedding would be even more splendid.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1195\">Of course, Zion and Harnette’s wedding was not lacking in any meaningful way, but it still could not bridge the gap between a direct royal family and a ducal title.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1197\" data-end=\"1271\">“The king… His Majesty… No, does His Majesty often preside over weddings?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1273\" data-end=\"1333\">“… It doesn’t happen often. Usually bureaucrats prevent it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1361\">“Did you preside over it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1363\" data-end=\"1525\">“A hero who has achieved merits must be treated accordingly. His Majesty isn’t formally supposed to preside, but since it was black and white, I couldn’t refuse.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1527\" data-end=\"1566\">“Maybe you thought you <em data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1558\">should</em> do it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1568\" data-end=\"1677\">“There must be many bureaucrats supporting Duke Adelaira. Even the Duke of Ternane has shifted direction… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1679\" data-end=\"1756\">Because of Zion and Harnet, Duke Adelaira gained more power than ever before.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1758\" data-end=\"1900\">The Duke of Ternane followed the current through Oz, and was indirectly connected to the royal family with the Marquis of Reggierd in between.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1902\" data-end=\"2012\">Naturally, the king would keep an eye on this structure, and Duke Adelaira had no choice but to act carefully.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2014\" data-end=\"2113\">“Well… I think you’re right. The location is different, but the colors and atmosphere are similar.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2115\" data-end=\"2236\">“A wedding is also an event, so certain customs and policies must be followed. People choose what they’re familiar with.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2238\" data-end=\"2293\">“Aren’t you the same? You could make a few changes… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2491\">“All humans are different, but there are ideas that everyone commonly thinks and accepts. Without such shared ideas, humanity wouldn’t be able to align with each other. Weddings are part of that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2493\" data-end=\"2569\">“… Does that mean the Alain Kingdom is maintained because such ideas exist?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2571\" data-end=\"2631\">“I suppose I should explain further… but you don’t need to.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2633\" data-end=\"2667\">Enrite smiled and looked at Lesia.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2669\" data-end=\"2735\">He no longer doubted Lesia, but he still couldn’t leave her alone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2737\" data-end=\"2828\">There were still many things he didn’t know about her, and he questioned her very humanity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2830\" data-end=\"2915\">He had to follow her, teach her many things, and stop her before she caused problems.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2917\" data-end=\"2993\">“But I don’t think you’d have trouble living even if you reject such ideas.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2995\" data-end=\"3123\">“That’s one possibility. You could live quietly… or you would be pushed aside by other humans. Eventually, you’d be left alone.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3125\" data-end=\"3198\">“Do I have to follow the will of the majority, whether I like it or not?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3200\" data-end=\"3316\">“The majority’s will isn’t always correct. But fundamentally, it’s good to respond to it. Aren’t you human as well?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3318\" data-end=\"3391\">“Um… Depending on your mindset, you could become someone special, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3393\" data-end=\"3514\">“Then you would have to live alone. Without help, or if you’re unlucky, you might be ostracized. Can you withstand that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3516\" data-end=\"3574\">“If I’m with you, wouldn’t I be able to endure that much?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3576\" data-end=\"3582\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3584\" data-end=\"3637\">Enrite was startled and showed a confused expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3639\" data-end=\"3770\">Lesia still lacked many things, but now, even if she distanced herself from Enrite, she would likely adapt without much difficulty.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3772\" data-end=\"3887\">Meanwhile, he had built a material foundation by crafting spheres, so why was she suddenly showing such confidence?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3889\" data-end=\"4030\">“It sounds a bit exaggerated, but you have the ability to live without me. You can find the life you want as long as it doesn’t harm others.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4032\" data-end=\"4109\">“I tried to become human so I could meet you. You’re the reason for my life.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4111\" data-end=\"4187\">Saeran, who had been quietly listening, tensed up at the strange atmosphere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4189\" data-end=\"4251\">Enrite and Lesia had not gotten along from the very beginning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4253\" data-end=\"4316\">Enrite attacked without hesitation, and Lesia responded calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4318\" data-end=\"4401\">But at some point, they became close, and even expressed a desire to stay together.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4403\" data-end=\"4448\">“You mean you’ll stay with me until the end?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4450\" data-end=\"4471\">“I want to if I can.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4473\" data-end=\"4492\">“What if I refuse?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4494\" data-end=\"4589\">“Then wouldn’t it be fine if I prepare a house a bit farther away and think of something else?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4591\" data-end=\"4635\">“… You’re not trying to spy on me, are you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4637\" data-end=\"4661\">“How could I not watch?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4663\" data-end=\"4700\">“… Haah… Why do you think like that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4702\" data-end=\"4761\">“Why wouldn’t it happen? Can’t people do things like that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4763\" data-end=\"4804\">Enrite frowned, her feelings complicated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4806\" data-end=\"4902\">There were so many things Saeran wanted to say, but he thought he should endure a little longer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4904\" data-end=\"4989\">“Even if you and I are closer than most humans, that doesn’t mean you can spy on me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4991\" data-end=\"5012\">“You won’t watch me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5014\" data-end=\"5088\">“Think about the reverse. How would <em data-start=\"5050\" data-end=\"5055\">you</em> feel if I secretly watched you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5090\" data-end=\"5117\">“I think it would be nice.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5119\" data-end=\"5126\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5128\" data-end=\"5139\">“Hah… Hmm.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5141\" data-end=\"5201\">Saeran unconsciously sighed, then quickly covered his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5203\" data-end=\"5261\">If Enrite knew what was wrong, she wouldn’t even say that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5263\" data-end=\"5329\">Enrite also knew that, so she remained silent without getting mad.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5331\" data-end=\"5436\">“Lesia, approaching someone should be brief, not constant. This is also related to the idea I mentioned.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5438\" data-end=\"5505\">“Is that idea something that forms between one person and another?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5507\" data-end=\"5517\">“Exactly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5519\" data-end=\"5564\">“But we’re not ‘just others,’ so why bother?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5566\" data-end=\"5602\">“Because it makes me uncomfortable.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5604\" data-end=\"5652\">“Oh? You’ve been uncomfortable for a long time.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5654\" data-end=\"5701\">Enrite became flustered, but recovered quickly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5703\" data-end=\"5790\">She couldn’t demand too much from someone who was still learning humanity from scratch.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5792\" data-end=\"5869\">That was why she had to endure until Lesia built proper systems and concepts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5871\" data-end=\"5943\">“Then what should I do? You already told me not to follow you secretly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5945\" data-end=\"5975\">“… I never told you to leave.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5977\" data-end=\"6019\">“You say it as if one day I will have to.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6021\" data-end=\"6172\">“Whoa… You’ve experienced part of my life. It might change little by little in the future. It may not suit you, but do you still want to stay with me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6174\" data-end=\"6272\">“I can live just like this. Sometimes we eat something good, take walks… and I can talk with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6274\" data-end=\"6337\">Enrite realized her question was meaningless and laughed dryly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6339\" data-end=\"6416\">From the moment Lesia met her until now, Lesia had always endured everything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6418\" data-end=\"6504\">Of course, sometimes she expressed dissatisfaction, but always returned to daily life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6506\" data-end=\"6555\">Through perseverance, she gained trust in Enrite.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6557\" data-end=\"6620\">“I’ll ask you one last thing. Why do you want to stay with me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6622\" data-end=\"6655\">“Because you’re my only sibling.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6657\" data-end=\"6707\">At the unexpected answer, Enrite’s face stiffened.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6709\" data-end=\"6768\">Of course, to others, she and Lesia were known as siblings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6770\" data-end=\"6865\">But this was the first time Lesia had emphasized that they were siblings—not simply companions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6867\" data-end=\"6922\">“Being siblings doesn’t mean we have to stay together.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6924\" data-end=\"6977\">“I still want to be by your side. Do you dislike me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6979\" data-end=\"7024\">“It’s not that I dislike you. It’s just… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7026\" data-end=\"7063\">Enrite pondered, but couldn’t finish.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7065\" data-end=\"7108\">She and Lesia desired very different lives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7110\" data-end=\"7182\">Enrite wanted a calm, quiet life; Lesia wanted a passionate, lively one.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7184\" data-end=\"7266\">They were so different that staying together would only lead to constant conflict.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7268\" data-end=\"7346\">“Did I do something wrong? Or does it seem like I’m still hiding my identity?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7348\" data-end=\"7416\">“It’s not that. Rather, I think our personalities just don’t match.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7418\" data-end=\"7465\">“I’ve been fine so far, so what’s the problem?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7467\" data-end=\"7584\">“I can’t simply tell you to keep enduring. Whatever you do, it’ll become uncomfortable. It’s not good for you or me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7586\" data-end=\"7690\">“There’s nothing troublesome. Sometimes I get annoyed. But still, I like being with you… How about you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7692\" data-end=\"7751\">Enrite looked directly into Lesia’s eyes in the quiet room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7753\" data-end=\"7805\">Her purple eyes were dim, reflecting her own figure.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7807\" data-end=\"7877\">She wondered if Lesia’s reaction would change depending on her answer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7879\" data-end=\"8029\">“It didn’t start well. I always disliked you, and you probably had your own issues. It’s better now, but I don’t know what will happen in the future.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8031\" data-end=\"8038\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8040\" data-end=\"8094\">Lesia’s expression darkened, and she lowered her head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8096\" data-end=\"8194\">Enrite—her only brother, the one person she wanted to stay close with—was trying to push her away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8196\" data-end=\"8301\">She had expected it somewhat, but when faced with the truth, even the will to keep living seemed to fade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8303\" data-end=\"8389\">“But… If you want, you can stay by my side. I can’t just irresponsibly send you away.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8391\" data-end=\"8436\">“… Does that mean I can stay however I want?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8438\" data-end=\"8470\">“Yes, I’ll respect your choice.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8472\" data-end=\"8485\">“Haaahh… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8487\" data-end=\"8528\">Lesia leaned forward with a slight smile.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8530\" data-end=\"8580\">Enrite felt burdened, but reluctantly accepted it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8582\" data-end=\"8612\">“Then can we get married now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8614\" data-end=\"8621\">“What?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8623\" data-end=\"8631\">“… Huh?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8633\" data-end=\"8688\">Enrite and Seran exchanged shocked, suspicious glances.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8690\" data-end=\"8769\">Surely she said it because of her own thoughts, but it was a bizarre statement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8771\" data-end=\"8823\">What kind of thought process led to that conclusion?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8825\" data-end=\"8883\">“Why? Don’t people get married when they love each other?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8885\" data-end=\"8916\">“How did love come into this!?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8918\" data-end=\"8942\">“Well… Aren’t we close?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8944\" data-end=\"9084\">“Lesia, marriage isn’t a simple decision. You must distinguish between closeness and affection—and you can’t marry someone of the same sex.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9086\" data-end=\"9168\">“Ah, so you marry someone of the opposite sex? Why isn’t there a same-sex gender?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9170\" data-end=\"9180\">“Uhh… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9182\" data-end=\"9232\">Enrite stood up first and headed to the work desk.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9234\" data-end=\"9324\">Seriously worried now, she began to think Lesia was learning human concepts <em data-start=\"9310\" data-end=\"9323\">incorrectly</em>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9326\" data-end=\"9407\">No matter how much she had studied humans, to casually drop such dangerous ideas—</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9409\" data-end=\"9438\">“Uh… Is this also an ‘idea’?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9440\" data-end=\"9493\">“If it weren’t an idea, why would I need to explain?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9495\" data-end=\"9544\">“Do you intend to break free from your concepts?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9546\" data-end=\"9601\">“Lesia. Should I get angry, or will you give up first?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9603\" data-end=\"9624\">“I’ll give up first.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9626\" data-end=\"9681\">Lesia answered instinctively and avoided Enrite’s eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9683\" data-end=\"9726\">Enrite glared at her with sharp, cold eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9728\" data-end=\"9809\">It seemed her remark had triggered Enrite’s principles and common societal ideas.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9811\" data-end=\"9881\">“I must have let too much slide. I shouldn’t have been so lenient… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9883\" data-end=\"9914\">“Why… Why are you saying that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9916\" data-end=\"9988\">“You need to learn again from the beginning. Let me teach you properly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9990\" data-end=\"10022\">“You already know I don’t need—”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10024\" data-end=\"10075\">“Did you just think you could do well on your own?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10077\" data-end=\"10096\">“I don’t know… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10098\" data-end=\"10240\">“That’s why I want to teach you properly. I’ve seen you reading strange books somewhere… I’ll make sure you don’t think of such things again.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10242\" data-end=\"10249\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10251\" data-end=\"10305\">Lesia couldn’t even argue, breaking into a cold sweat.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10307\" data-end=\"10374\">It was just a short conversation, but it brought a strong reaction.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10376\" data-end=\"10429\">She wondered if she would have to suffer for a while.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10431\" data-end=\"10496\">‘Ahh… Will I have to listen to lectures for the rest of my life?’</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-189/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"186\" data-end=\"189\">\r\n<p data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"242\"><strong data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"242\">Residence and barracks of the Duke of Adelaira.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"331\">All of the Duke of Adelaira’s knights and soldiers lived and trained in these barracks.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"333\" data-end=\"440\">Formally, it was part of the mansion, but it was separated into a different location for aesthetic reasons.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"442\" data-end=\"556\">The knights of the Lihine Knights were in the same situation, but now the time had come for them to make a choice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"558\" data-end=\"581\">“Is everyone gathered?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"583\" data-end=\"589\">“Yes!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"591\" data-end=\"663\">In response to Enrite’s question, the knights answered at the same time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"749\">Lecia, Seran, and Oz were present, and Juter had been informed in advance by letter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"751\" data-end=\"916\">Since Zion and Hanette had gone on their honeymoon, Enrite had been entrusted with the position of leader of the knights and decided to organize them in their place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"1116\">“…Originally, after the Integrity Knight Commander returned from his honeymoon, he was supposed to tell you directly. But I decided there was no reason to delay, since this is an internal decision.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1181\">Enrite looked toward the knights and continued speaking calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1183\" data-end=\"1258\">Except for Zion, Hanette, and Oz, they were members of the Sillays Knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1260\" data-end=\"1422\">Originally, the Lihine Knights were operated by knights from two families—Zion’s and Hanette’s—so most of them naturally became involved with the Sillays Knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1424\" data-end=\"1475\">“Seran, what is the purpose of the Lihine Knights?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1477\" data-end=\"1575\">“To eradicate the three Great Demon Kings and the four Great Calamities, and to subjugate demons.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1647\">Enrite remained silent for a moment, giving the knights time to think.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1649\" data-end=\"1715\">Some already knew, and the rest would soon understand the meaning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1717\" data-end=\"2053\">“As everyone knows, the three Great Demon Kings and the four Great Calamities have been eradicated. The Purple Priest and the Silver Phantom Thief confirmed the facts, and His Majesty the King has also received the report. Subjugating demonic beasts is an important duty for knights, but total subjugation would take hundreds of years.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2055\" data-end=\"2132\">Subjugating demonic beasts was practically the duty of the Kingdom of Allain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2134\" data-end=\"2260\">It was nearly impossible to eliminate every demon, and most of the kingdom’s forces were invested simply in preserving Allain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2262\" data-end=\"2368\">His words made one wonder whether even after hundreds or thousands of years, magicians would still remain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2370\" data-end=\"2615\">“In any case… the Lihine Knights can be considered to have achieved the purpose of their existence. Other knight orders will find themselves in similar circumstances. Meanwhile, mercenaries have been permitted, but they will soon be sanctioned.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2617\" data-end=\"2675\">Seran reflected on those words and accepted them solemnly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2677\" data-end=\"2821\">Because of Zion and Harnette, they had achieved accomplishments beyond their limits, and recently even the demonic beast invasions had subsided.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2823\" data-end=\"2964\">The justification for acting as knights had disappeared, and since they had reached their limits, even their enthusiasm would naturally fade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2966\" data-end=\"3148\">“So… I will officially declare it here and now. The Knights of Lihines will soon be dissolved. After the Integrity Knight Commander returns, we will carry out the formal procedures.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3150\" data-end=\"3155\">“Ah…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3157\" data-end=\"3165\">“I see…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3167\" data-end=\"3229\">The knights felt bitter, but accepted the reality before them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3231\" data-end=\"3320\">If there were fewer battles with monsters, the value of knights would naturally diminish.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3322\" data-end=\"3460\">The Kingdom of Allain’s own strength was enough to defend the border region, and depending on the situation, it might even shrink in size.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3462\" data-end=\"3627\">“You have fought well up to this point. Even when the knight orders were merged and the leader changed, you adapted quickly. There were many difficulties back then.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3629\" data-end=\"3754\">Of course, only the magic sword users and Setino Quasar participated in important battles, and the rest simply held the rear.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3756\" data-end=\"3857\">However, the knights handled other tasks properly, never causing trouble, and did not disobey orders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3859\" data-end=\"3932\">The result was good because each of them faithfully fulfilled their role.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3934\" data-end=\"4113\">“The Commander of the Knights will distribute additional pay to you. It’s not a small amount, and you may consider it compensation for not being held responsible to the very end.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4115\" data-end=\"4120\">“Oh…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4174\">The knights brightened slightly and showed interest.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4176\" data-end=\"4195\">No one hated money.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4197\" data-end=\"4311\">Additionally, since Zion and Harnette had never acted arrogantly or mistreated them, there would be no complaints.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4313\" data-end=\"4398\">“You each must decide for yourselves what to do next. I, too, will find my own path.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4400\" data-end=\"4455\">“Can we not maintain the Knight Order among ourselves?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4457\" data-end=\"4502\">One of the knights raised his hand and asked.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4504\" data-end=\"4562\">Enrite thought for a moment, then slowly opened his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4564\" data-end=\"4804\">“…It’s not impossible. You simply have to start anew with a new order of knights. However, the Black Knights must never be mentioned anywhere, and the Duke of Adelaira must not be connected to the Marquess of Reggiard. Can you manage that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4806\" data-end=\"4835\">“I haven’t thought that far.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4837\" data-end=\"5057\">“I’ll warn you beforehand: think and act carefully. I will not sit idle if a Black Knight becomes involved while you run this knight order. Neither family will remain silent, and His Majesty the King may even intervene.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5059\" data-end=\"5089\">Enrite did not force his will.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5091\" data-end=\"5164\">He merely told them to give up if they could not manage the consequences.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5166\" data-end=\"5275\">Whether intentional or not, tarnishing the honor of Zion and Hanette was something that could not be allowed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5277\" data-end=\"5496\">“Do you want to know what I’m thinking? I do not recommend that you run a knight order among yourselves. There will surely be someone among you who commits a mistake. Can you imagine the impact of a single small error?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5498\" data-end=\"5501\">“…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5503\" data-end=\"5704\">“I can’t guarantee that even if I’m with you, no problems will arise. Do you think it will be different just because I’m Seran? Thank you very much, but no—it’s impossible to fully control all of you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5706\" data-end=\"5774\">After all, these knights came together because of Zion and Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5776\" data-end=\"5886\">Even if the Lihine Knights disappear, their legacy will remain, and it will have both major and minor effects.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5888\" data-end=\"5937\">Could the knights refrain from abusing that fact?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5939\" data-end=\"6077\">“It is best to retire like this, but… if you still have the heart to fight for this country, wouldn’t it be better to enlist as soldiers?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6079\" data-end=\"6123\">It was the cleanest and most effective path.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6125\" data-end=\"6181\">Even now, demonic beast invasions continued to decrease.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6183\" data-end=\"6340\">As a result, knights and mercenaries would be dissolved one after another as demand decreased, and the Kingdom of Allain’s power would naturally consolidate.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6342\" data-end=\"6448\">“I’m doing this for your sake. There is no place left for knights to go. Why not find your own lives now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6450\" data-end=\"6490\">None of the knights opened their mouths.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6492\" data-end=\"6561\">They each had their own thoughts, or had already set different goals.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6563\" data-end=\"6637\">Since Zion and Harnette had treated them well, there would be no backlash.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6639\" data-end=\"6825\">“There is still time before the Integrity Knight Commander returns. Just because I return doesn’t mean I’ll drive you out immediately. I hope you think carefully and make your decision.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6827\" data-end=\"6870\">Enrite hesitated briefly, then moved first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6872\" data-end=\"6934\">Lecia, Seran, and Oz quickly followed him out of the barracks.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6936\" data-end=\"6945\">“…Seran.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6947\" data-end=\"6953\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6955\" data-end=\"7087\">“I do not oppose you leading the knights again. But do not forget what I said. For now, it is best to dissolve the Templar Knights.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7089\" data-end=\"7129\">Seran couldn’t bring himself to say yes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7131\" data-end=\"7228\">Originally, the knights had been members of the Sillaz Knights, and he had acted as their leader.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7230\" data-end=\"7313\">If he led them again, they would surely follow—but he could not foresee the future.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7315\" data-end=\"7369\">‘Without effort, how could I maintain a knight order?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7371\" data-end=\"7425\">Holding a knight title had been a long-cherished goal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7427\" data-end=\"7539\">In the end, he achieved his dream at a young age, but naturally had to give it up as the number of knights grew.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7541\" data-end=\"7627\">He was too weak, and with only this many people, he could not defeat stronger enemies.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7629\" data-end=\"7677\">‘Until now… I haven’t been able to do anything.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7679\" data-end=\"7752\">The three Demon Kings and four Great Calamities had already been subdued.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7754\" data-end=\"7868\">There were no strong enemies left; thus, there was no reason for magic sword users or Setinos Quasar to intervene.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7870\" data-end=\"7964\">Most of all, he wondered whether it would be shameful to witness another’s overwhelming power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7966\" data-end=\"7987\">‘To become stronger…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7989\" data-end=\"8062\">He hadn’t made a decision yet, but he had already begun preparing for it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8064\" data-end=\"8138\">He had never had to kill anyone, but he did not want to give up like this.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8140\" data-end=\"8210\">Like them, he wanted to awaken a magic sword and reach a higher level.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8212\" data-end=\"8256\">“Oz-sama, are you thinking about something?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8258\" data-end=\"8312\">“Me… Me? I suppose I’ll have to think about it again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8314\" data-end=\"8356\">Oz looked half-heartedly at Enrite’s back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8358\" data-end=\"8429\">He was fortunate to have joined the Lihine Knights and achieved merits.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8431\" data-end=\"8504\">But it was hard to think ahead since he had no plans for what came after.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8506\" data-end=\"8561\">‘Why didn’t I think about this? It had to end someday…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8563\" data-end=\"8610\">Of course, he thought the timing was too early.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8612\" data-end=\"8647\">But looking back, this was natural.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8649\" data-end=\"8735\">All the magic sword users had gathered, and they had been supported by Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8737\" data-end=\"8796\">‘After the Lihine Knights disband… won’t my family meddle?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8798\" data-end=\"8889\">His father, the Duke of Ternane, had sent him to the Lihine Knights without any conditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8891\" data-end=\"8966\">At the time, everything went smoothly, but now something else might happen.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8968\" data-end=\"9038\">Before the Duke of Ternane made a move, he had to take action himself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9040\" data-end=\"9101\">‘I’ve saved quite a bit of money. Where should I run off to?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9103\" data-end=\"9154\">Oz had been paid as a member of the Lihine Knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9156\" data-end=\"9265\">Although he was a magic sword user, he had strength in his own way, so the amount must have been substantial.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9267\" data-end=\"9425\">Also, since the king, the three princesses, and the White Apostle were all magic sword users, they might ask for his help immediately if something went wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9427\" data-end=\"9450\">‘If that doesn’t work…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9452\" data-end=\"9480\">“Lecia, you… are… finished.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9482\" data-end=\"9519\">“Why are you stopping in the middle?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9521\" data-end=\"9561\">“Haven’t you already decided your goal?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9563\" data-end=\"9596\">“Can’t you just ask me directly?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9598\" data-end=\"9625\">“…You’re being ridiculous.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9627\" data-end=\"9678\">“Ah, I was just saying while asking Saeran and Oz.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9680\" data-end=\"9717\">Lecia sighed and looked disappointed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9719\" data-end=\"9771\">But Enrite ignored her and simply walked in silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9773\" data-end=\"9814\">“Um… White One. May I ask you something?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9816\" data-end=\"9827\">“Go ahead.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9829\" data-end=\"9874\">“How are the captain and vice-captain doing?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9876\" data-end=\"9926\">You mean after they returned from their honeymoon?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9928\" data-end=\"9934\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9936\" data-end=\"10020\">“They said they would rest for a while. If you have other plans, why not join them?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10022\" data-end=\"10082\">Enrite gave an ambiguous answer, recalling their invitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10084\" data-end=\"10110\">The two already had plans.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10112\" data-end=\"10233\">If conditions were good, they intended to buy a castle or a large house and become independent from the Duke of Adelaira.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10235\" data-end=\"10314\">Most importantly, he felt slightly hesitant because he was trying to step away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10316\" data-end=\"10340\">‘What are you thinking…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10342\" data-end=\"10393\">Zion knew he had lost the reason he wanted to live.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10395\" data-end=\"10490\">So once he built a new foundation, he proposed employing him as the family’s exclusive paladin.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10492\" data-end=\"10558\">Perhaps he assumed I would run away from the Holy Kinesian Church.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10560\" data-end=\"10598\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">‘Are you trying to give me a purpose?’</p></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-190/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"99\" data-end=\"102\">\r\n<p data-start=\"104\" data-end=\"170\">The rental house where Kelidos, Zion, and Harnette were staying.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"250\">The two of them spent their honeymoon traveling around the Kingdom of Alain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"370\">Of course, the location wasn’t too far from the capital, and the knight guards and servants followed them every day.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"487\">Now they had reached the last day, and while enjoying their honeymoon, they looked forward to their future plans.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"489\" data-end=\"513\">“I have to leave now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"515\" data-end=\"609\">“I have to depart tomorrow morning. There’s something I need to take care of when I arrive.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"611\" data-end=\"652\">“… Are you talking about the Templars?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"730\">Harnette remembered the things she had to do and spoke up unintentionally.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"815\">Since their objective had been achieved, there was no reason to keep the knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"817\" data-end=\"932\">In the future, she wouldn’t participate in battles as much as possible, so she had to organize things in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"982\">“Cardinal Selena should be able to handle it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1027\">“Still, shouldn’t it be you handling it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1098\">“No. You have to pay them, and you have to arrange meals for them.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1133\">“Won’t they feel dissatisfied?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1228\">“If you do it this far, there will be no other results. They rarely do this kind of thing.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1254\">“… Then it’s settled.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1256\" data-end=\"1303\">Harnette crossed her legs and sipped her tea.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1394\">As she took care of the tasks she had postponed one by one, it seemed to calm her mind.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1494\">It would be nice if she could afford a house like this, but she didn’t have that much money yet.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1559\">“Well… I don’t know if Cardinal Selena will accept my offer.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1561\" data-end=\"1627\">“Isn’t that a bit difficult? We’re not buying a house outright.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1733\">“Something might happen in the meantime. Even if you are formally employed, the salary won’t be easy.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1735\" data-end=\"1843\">“Hey, why worry about money if you have a gold vein? Isn’t it more important to mine it and sell quickly?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1845\" data-end=\"1938\">“That’s the problem. It shouldn’t be hard to mine, but you haven’t mined it yet, have you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1940\" data-end=\"1951\">“Um… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1953\" data-end=\"2095\">She had proven that there was a gold vein in the land granted by the king and had created a mining setup by borrowing money from her family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2097\" data-end=\"2170\">However, it took longer than expected, and the costs were considerable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2172\" data-end=\"2265\">First of all, she couldn’t get money to buy a house because she couldn’t mine the gold yet.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2267\" data-end=\"2390\">“If you rush too much, someone could get hurt. You’d better use your magic carefully. It might react with the gold vein.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2392\" data-end=\"2460\">“This isn’t going as well as I thought. I want to buy a house… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2462\" data-end=\"2514\">Harnette put down her tea cup, showing her regret.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2516\" data-end=\"2606\">She had definitely prepared thoroughly and had planned this even before getting married.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2608\" data-end=\"2673\">However, the timing wasn’t right, and it only made her anxious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2675\" data-end=\"2731\">“You don’t need to overthink. Do you still have time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2733\" data-end=\"2800\">“You’re doing that? You could still play well when you’re young.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2802\" data-end=\"2825\">“That’s what I said.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2827\" data-end=\"2890\">“Don’t you think you can only play well if you have a house?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2892\" data-end=\"2943\">“Are you still uncomfortable with Duke Adelaira?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2945\" data-end=\"3017\">“… It’s not that I’m uncomfortable. I just want to be alone with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3019\" data-end=\"3113\">Before the marriage, she could have cleared up some misunderstandings by talking to Robbins.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3115\" data-end=\"3220\">Of course, that didn’t mean the past would disappear, but she couldn’t take it with her until she died.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3222\" data-end=\"3312\">No matter how much she hated him, he was her father, and she couldn’t deny that lineage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3314\" data-end=\"3395\">“Even if you stay here, you won’t bother us. Can’t you hold it in for a while?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3397\" data-end=\"3465\">“You need to be patient. That’s better than going to your family.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3467\" data-end=\"3496\">“… Can I hear you grumble?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3498\" data-end=\"3587\">“I don’t know how you two will turn out. Can’t the situation get worse than it is now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3589\" data-end=\"3636\">Harnette rolled her eyes and tilted her head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3638\" data-end=\"3732\">Duke Adelaira was her residence until now, and he wouldn’t interfere continuously as before.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3734\" data-end=\"3864\">However, since the Marquis Regard family would treat her as a daughter-in-law, she had no choice but to show some consideration.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3866\" data-end=\"3972\">If a similar situation happened again, she wouldn’t tolerate it, and it could have serious consequences.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3974\" data-end=\"4041\">“Still, since she’s a duke’s daughter, are you trying to meddle?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4043\" data-end=\"4114\">“You could curse along too. You said you couldn’t protect your wife.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4116\" data-end=\"4163\">“If you say that, I think I’ll leave myself.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4165\" data-end=\"4189\">“… You can’t do that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4191\" data-end=\"4214\">“What else can I do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4216\" data-end=\"4259\">“If you want to do it, I’d better do it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4261\" data-end=\"4325\">“NO. In this case, Setinos Quasar has the right to intervene.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4327\" data-end=\"4348\">“Hah! What’s that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4350\" data-end=\"4397\">Harnette laughed heartily and waved her hand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4399\" data-end=\"4455\">Pleased with the reaction, Zion slowly raised his cup.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4457\" data-end=\"4539\">“It’s just a joke, but it will work. It seems no one can be the Cetinos Quasar.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4541\" data-end=\"4586\">“If you do that, won’t no one talk to you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4588\" data-end=\"4649\">“That will happen if I stare at them with a straight face.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4651\" data-end=\"4696\">“Did I hear you say my marriage was wrong?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4698\" data-end=\"4735\">“Do you want me to be the bad guy?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4737\" data-end=\"4823\">“If you’re bad, I’ll be the good and beautiful woman. How about sacrificing for me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4825\" data-end=\"4860\">“I’m fine, but sad to hear that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4862\" data-end=\"4925\">Zion looked back at their honeymoon with a smile on his face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4927\" data-end=\"5003\">It was more relaxed and comfortable than before, with nothing complicated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5005\" data-end=\"5050\">Just being together made the calmness fade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5052\" data-end=\"5097\">“Now I’ll ask. Marry me… do you regret it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5099\" data-end=\"5153\">“If I regretted it, I would have run away long ago.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5155\" data-end=\"5195\">“Can’t you settle it by running away?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5197\" data-end=\"5249\">“Wouldn’t I have to hide for the rest of my life?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5251\" data-end=\"5283\">“Isn’t it the king who leads?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5285\" data-end=\"5326\">“Ah… is it a death sentence if caught?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5328\" data-end=\"5385\">“Hee ha ha! Are you going to kill me for running away?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5387\" data-end=\"5487\">“That’s another thing I don’t know. I’m leading, but wouldn’t it be a little angry if I ran away?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5489\" data-end=\"5500\">“Um… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5502\" data-end=\"5566\">Harnette had doubts, but somehow it made sense, so she agreed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5568\" data-end=\"5627\">Zion looked at her casually, then slowly tilted his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5629\" data-end=\"5658\">“Can we not fight anymore?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5660\" data-end=\"5713\">“What do you mean? Haven’t you conquered them all?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5715\" data-end=\"5833\">“It’s true the conquests are over. The invasions have decreased, and now I can’t fight monsters well. I’m very… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5835\" data-end=\"5869\">Zion hesitated and said nothing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5871\" data-end=\"5924\">Harnette waited calmly, then belatedly spoke again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5926\" data-end=\"5972\">“You mean strong people might appear again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5974\" data-end=\"6042\">“I’m just guessing. Because there’s something that seems like it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6044\" data-end=\"6074\">She still didn’t believe it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6076\" data-end=\"6186\">The three great demon kings and the four great disasters were destroyed, and even the demons were wiped out.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6188\" data-end=\"6265\">It was such an ideal result that she couldn’t help but feel the difference.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6267\" data-end=\"6321\">“I’m worried about something that’s never happened.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6323\" data-end=\"6362\">“Right. I wonder why I did this too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6364\" data-end=\"6391\">“Aren’t there any signs?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6393\" data-end=\"6459\">“There’s nothing like that. It’s just speculation, no evidence.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6461\" data-end=\"6487\">“But why did you do it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6489\" data-end=\"6519\">“Well… I don’t know either.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6521\" data-end=\"6530\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6532\" data-end=\"6571\">Harnette looked at Zion in amazement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6573\" data-end=\"6624\">Zion slowly avoided her gaze and tilted his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6626\" data-end=\"6667\">“I’m here, what are you worried about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6669\" data-end=\"6716\">“Oh, well… you’re still stronger than me… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6718\" data-end=\"6808\">“Where’s the dog? If something happens, I’ll take care of it, so stay by my side. Okay?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6810\" data-end=\"6823\">“Eh… okay.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6825\" data-end=\"6876\">“And… don’t think like that. You think too much.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6878\" data-end=\"6914\">“Isn’t it better than not at all?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6916\" data-end=\"6959\">“Seeing you, you look better without it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6961\" data-end=\"6970\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6972\" data-end=\"7017\">Zion looked out the window, lost for words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7019\" data-end=\"7075\">As the sun slowly set, the orange light began to fade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7077\" data-end=\"7162\">Meanwhile, time passed quickly, and they didn’t even realize they were enjoying it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7164\" data-end=\"7203\">‘In my life now… twilight will come.’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"7205\" data-end=\"7208\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7210\" data-end=\"7262\">Mierne, western territory of the Kingdom of Alain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7264\" data-end=\"7357\">After Zion and Harnette returned to the Duke of Adelaira, they began dealing with problems.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7359\" data-end=\"7485\">The disbandment of the Lihines Knights, follow-ups on the knights, seven demon swords, Lesia’s artificial demon swords, etc.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7487\" data-end=\"7594\">Since it was impossible to resolve everything at once, they tried to tackle the easier issues one by one.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7596\" data-end=\"7708\">In the process, she inevitably had to get help from Enrite, eventually reaching the location of the gold vein.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7710\" data-end=\"7733\">“… Have you done it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7735\" data-end=\"7792\">“Because you need to mine it quickly to get the money.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7794\" data-end=\"7862\">Zion was examining the gold vein with Harnette, Enrite, and Lesia.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7864\" data-end=\"7945\">Many workers were mobilized, and there were two or three earth attribute mages.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7947\" data-end=\"8056\">The land was dug deep enough, and now they were making tunnels by erecting pillars throughout the basement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8058\" data-end=\"8083\">“Does Your Grace know?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8085\" data-end=\"8226\">“Yes, I reported it immediately after discovering it. Your Grace said there might be controversy, so he told us to keep it secret for now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8228\" data-end=\"8286\">“Everyone who should know now must already know, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8288\" data-end=\"8389\">“So I decided to donate part of the gold to the palace. That way, the bureaucrats won’t interfere.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8391\" data-end=\"8458\">“… That’s not a bad idea, since you’ll have to pay taxes anyway.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8460\" data-end=\"8535\">“Just a little more to give you reason. Your Grace will also be pleased.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8537\" data-end=\"8628\">Zion had taken prior steps to avoid the controversy that might arise over the gold layer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8630\" data-end=\"8724\">The king would certainly be on his side if he paid slightly more gold than the standard tax.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8726\" data-end=\"8875\">Moreover, since he was the current Setinos Quasar and the royal family’s in-law, it would probably be difficult to criticize him, let alone openly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8877\" data-end=\"8927\">“What will you do with the money you make here?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8929\" data-end=\"9079\">“I’ll buy a house. If I can build a building, I’ll build it and hire knights and servants. Wouldn’t it be nice if there’s something to write about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9081\" data-end=\"9143\">“So you’re saying you’ll hire me as your exclusive paladin?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9145\" data-end=\"9184\">“Yes, because I have a lot of money.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9186\" data-end=\"9195\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9197\" data-end=\"9262\">Enrite quietly chewed on those words and peeked into the shaft.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9264\" data-end=\"9354\">Sunlight only reached a little toward the entrance, but a bright yellow color reflected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9356\" data-end=\"9396\">There must be more gold hidden inside.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9398\" data-end=\"9473\">‘Even if you buy a castle, you still have it. Maybe I can buy more land.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9475\" data-end=\"9581\">Gold is extremely rare and has many uses, so its price would definitely be high under any circumstances.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9583\" data-end=\"9660\">Not only nobles and merchants, but even the royal family tried to buy gold.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9662\" data-end=\"9759\">Wouldn’t it be possible to live luxuriously for the rest of my life if I owned this gold layer?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9761\" data-end=\"9796\">“I’m not worried about anything.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9798\" data-end=\"9847\">Enrite had thought a lot about Zion’s proposal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9849\" data-end=\"9960\">Nobles are originally people who spend a lot of money, and no matter how much they have, they often waste it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9962\" data-end=\"10077\">Of course, the two of them wouldn’t waste money, but he decided he couldn’t employ them in the current situation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10079\" data-end=\"10149\">‘I don’t need to take money, but ordinary people won’t tolerate it.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10151\" data-end=\"10252\">The common folk would accept it unconditionally if they could hire someone without paying anything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10254\" data-end=\"10380\">However, Zion has the status of a noble, and since he had achieved much, he had no choice but to stand on his own authority.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10382\" data-end=\"10511\">Even if he offered to do the work for free, he wouldn’t allow it, even out of pride, because it was a job that didn’t pay Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10513\" data-end=\"10537\">‘If this happens… … .’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10539\" data-end=\"10600\">Enrite was still pondering but leaned in another direction.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10602\" data-end=\"10683\">Kinesien had no reason to stay with the Holy Church, and he had no other goals.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10685\" data-end=\"10764\">There’s no harm in enjoying leisure time in daily life, even if only briefly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10766\" data-end=\"10794\">‘Can I accept that offer?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10796\" data-end=\"10808\">Kidnapping</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-191/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"105\" data-end=\"108\">\r\n<p data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"138\"><strong data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"138\">1. Reality and Ideal (1)</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"140\" data-end=\"205\">Almost two years had passed since Zion and Hanette got married.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"207\" data-end=\"314\">As expected, the monsters hadn’t disappeared, but the kingdom of Alain was gradually becoming prosperous.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"316\" data-end=\"525\">From time to time, discussions at the palace revolved around expanding territories, or conversely, opinions arose that the number of troops should be reduced as the threat from the Beast Sorcerers decreased.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"527\" data-end=\"703\">However, even amid these debates, there was no talk of abolishing the Setinos Quasar system—perhaps a reminder of the days when three demon kings and four calamities existed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"705\" data-end=\"712\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"742\">Enrite got up immediately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"873\">It had been about nine months since he arrived at this mansion, and he had already adapted to the different living environment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"875\" data-end=\"1036\">Being employed as the family’s exclusive paladin, he was required to stay at the mansion at all times and was provided with a room along with a regular salary.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1075\"><em data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1073\">‘I thought it would take longer…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1138\">Enrite rose from bed and began searching for other clothes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1140\" data-end=\"1253\">Zion and Hanette had quickly finished the mining shafts, repeatedly mining and selling gold over the past year.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1397\">As a result, they had saved enough to buy a large house in the capital, and only after furnishing it and hiring staff did they call it home.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1413\"><em data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1411\">‘Wash up…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1415\" data-end=\"1471\">A servant entered the room after knocking on the door.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1473\" data-end=\"1546\">The servant gently bowed, placed a basin down, and quickly disappeared.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1582\">The basin contained clean water.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1632\"><em data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1630\">‘By now, darkness must have already spread.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1634\" data-end=\"1685\">Enrite washed his face and even trimmed his hair.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1687\" data-end=\"1764\">Finally, after changing his clothes, he could stand in front of the mirror.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1766\" data-end=\"1791\"><em data-start=\"1766\" data-end=\"1789\">‘Isn’t this strange?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1793\" data-end=\"1851\">Enrite observed his own appearance while wearing a suit.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1853\" data-end=\"1983\">When he became a cardinal of the Kinesian Church, he always wore robes, and when going to the battlefield, he always wore armor.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1985\" data-end=\"2082\">Though he held no noble title, he had been treated beyond that because he was a Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2084\" data-end=\"2179\">However, he had never touched this kind of outfit before, nor had he ever thought to wear it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2181\" data-end=\"2216\"><em data-start=\"2181\" data-end=\"2214\">‘… This is better than a robe.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2218\" data-end=\"2294\">Enrite usually reached a conclusion quickly and stepped into the corridor.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2296\" data-end=\"2429\">The servants and attendants appeared and disappeared from time to time, and a faint aroma of delicious food wafted through the air.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2431\" data-end=\"2535\">Sunlight streamed through the windows, and a warm atmosphere seemed to envelop the mansion’s interior.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2537\" data-end=\"2568\"><em data-start=\"2537\" data-end=\"2566\">‘Too big to live in alone.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2570\" data-end=\"2642\">It was something he had always thought since moving into this mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2644\" data-end=\"2783\">Its scale was smaller compared to the Duke of Adelaira or the Marquis of Reggiard, but it was still worthy of being called a large house.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2785\" data-end=\"2883\">That was why the servants managed the household, while knights and soldiers guarded the mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2885\" data-end=\"2918\"><em data-start=\"2885\" data-end=\"2916\">‘Still, Lesia and I coexist…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2920\" data-end=\"2969\">Enrite slowly stopped and glanced around again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2971\" data-end=\"3052\">Perhaps Lesia was still sleeping and would only wake up if the maid called her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3054\" data-end=\"3151\">Even though he was the family’s exclusive knight commander, was it really a problem to be lazy?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3153\" data-end=\"3182\"><em data-start=\"3153\" data-end=\"3180\">‘I’m glad I have skills.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3184\" data-end=\"3223\">Enrite exhaled and continued walking.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3225\" data-end=\"3335\">Though he was less active than other ordinary soldiers, he tried to act decisively once a decision was made.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3337\" data-end=\"3457\">When outsiders attacked, he would rise and go to war, clearly fulfilling his duties as the exclusive knight commander.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3459\" data-end=\"3499\"><em data-start=\"3459\" data-end=\"3497\">‘Serran will be on the front lines…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3501\" data-end=\"3588\">Serran enlisted in the military immediately after the Lihines Knights were disbanded.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3590\" data-end=\"3685\">Since he hadn’t told anyone, Brandis discovered it while passing through the training center.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3687\" data-end=\"3806\">Brandis invited Serran to join the Royal Knights, but he politely declined and requested to serve on the front lines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3846\"><em data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3844\">‘He must want to become stronger.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3848\" data-end=\"3937\">Among magic sword users, only Zion and Hanette had achieved remarkable accomplishments.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3939\" data-end=\"4078\">Not counting himself and Brandis, who worked together to some extent, the others seemed strongly influenced by the flow of circumstances.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4080\" data-end=\"4166\">Perhaps Serran had chosen the front lines to deny reality and aim for higher ground.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4168\" data-end=\"4208\"><em data-start=\"4168\" data-end=\"4206\">‘Oz… I am active as a Royal Knight.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4210\" data-end=\"4274\">Oz sought a way to survive while avoiding the Duke of Ternane.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4276\" data-end=\"4397\">All he had were his magic sword, sword skills, and the money he had saved, so he had to make the most of his situation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4399\" data-end=\"4542\">After various processes, he reached Brandis, and after a brief conversation with the Duke of Ternane, Brandis made Oz join the Royal Knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4544\" data-end=\"4627\"><em data-start=\"4544\" data-end=\"4625\">‘Not a bad move. If you are a Royal Knight, even your family cannot touch you.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4629\" data-end=\"4720\">Since a family member had joined the Royal Knights, the Duke of Ternane suffered no loss.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4722\" data-end=\"4865\">In some ways, it was better than an arranged marriage, and although delayed, it brought a great advantage to being part of the Royal Knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4867\" data-end=\"4975\">Most importantly, since Oz could leave the family on his own, it was clear he had achieved what he wanted.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4977\" data-end=\"5004\"><em data-start=\"4977\" data-end=\"5002\">‘The three princesses…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5006\" data-end=\"5064\">Enrite descended the stairs toward the first-floor hall.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5066\" data-end=\"5132\">This time, he could see not only the maids but also the knights.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5134\" data-end=\"5221\">The knights bowed quietly to Enrite as he passed by, and he nodded in acknowledgment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5223\" data-end=\"5287\"><em data-start=\"5223\" data-end=\"5285\">‘We expand our power. There’s no reason to think otherwise.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5289\" data-end=\"5348\">Juter had solidified his position since marrying Barchen.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5350\" data-end=\"5454\">The number of nobles connected to Uter gradually increased, and several royal families supported Uter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5456\" data-end=\"5531\">He must be trying to expand his power and influence to ascend the throne.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5533\" data-end=\"5620\"><em data-start=\"5533\" data-end=\"5618\">‘Even if I don’t want the black color, I have no choice but to be entangled in it.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5622\" data-end=\"5697\">Enrite stepped out of the mansion and began walking around the courtyard.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5699\" data-end=\"5790\">Zion was the royal family’s son-in-law and a direct knight of the king, a Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5792\" data-end=\"5884\">He would inevitably be caught up in that plot, placing him in a somewhat awkward position.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5886\" data-end=\"5940\">He might have to make a decision one way or another.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5942\" data-end=\"5996\"><em data-start=\"5942\" data-end=\"5994\">‘The Duke of Adelaira won’t be able to intervene.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5998\" data-end=\"6055\">Of course, it didn’t mean he couldn’t intervene at all.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6057\" data-end=\"6153\">However, there had been incidents involving the duchy, and the royal family was aware of them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6155\" data-end=\"6283\">Most importantly, he had no choice but to act cautiously because a single wrong step could turn the entire family upside down.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6285\" data-end=\"6334\"><em data-start=\"6285\" data-end=\"6332\">‘If the black moves, Hanette will agree too…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6336\" data-end=\"6406\">If he did not respond cleverly, he would suffer considerable losses.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6408\" data-end=\"6495\">He had to maintain his relationship with Juter without causing friction with Brandis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6497\" data-end=\"6615\">There was no harm in resenting the king, and it was highly likely that the three princesses would ascend the throne.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6617\" data-end=\"6648\"><em data-start=\"6617\" data-end=\"6646\">‘I might be entangled too.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6650\" data-end=\"6713\">Enrite tried to avoid the power struggle as much as possible.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6715\" data-end=\"6778\">Otherwise, he would be greedy and likely unable to handle it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6780\" data-end=\"6843\">He always remained neutral and simply observed the situation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6845\" data-end=\"6934\"><em data-start=\"6845\" data-end=\"6932\">‘All I need to eliminate is the Setinos Quasar title. There’s no reason for revenge.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6936\" data-end=\"7045\">He had little contact with nobles or bureaucrats, as he always tried to complete the tasks assigned to him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7047\" data-end=\"7097\">Opportunities were missed, but it wasn’t a loss.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7099\" data-end=\"7227\">Meanwhile, the salary he received as a Setinos Quasar and Cardinal was not small, so living alone should not be too difficult.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7229\" data-end=\"7266\"><em data-start=\"7229\" data-end=\"7264\">‘Perhaps I should talk to Black.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7268\" data-end=\"7313\">He could maintain his own level of comfort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7315\" data-end=\"7432\">However, he wondered if it would be challenging for Zion and Hanette given the unique conditions and circumstances.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7434\" data-end=\"7531\">Other Setinos Quasars would also be slightly entangled, so it was better to prepare in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7533\" data-end=\"7579\"><em data-start=\"7533\" data-end=\"7577\">‘… This everyday life must not be ruined.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7581\" data-end=\"7682\">Enrite faced his new life here and had fallen in love with the comfortable and peaceful atmosphere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7684\" data-end=\"7786\">It seemed like the same life repeated, but it was so stable and peaceful that it didn’t feel boring.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7788\" data-end=\"7907\">This was the point where he could feel that he no longer had to suffer due to battles with demons, missions, or work.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7909\" data-end=\"7961\"><em data-start=\"7909\" data-end=\"7959\">‘Both of them deserve to enjoy this daily life.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7963\" data-end=\"8021\">Enrite slowly turned his back and looked at the mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8023\" data-end=\"8102\">It was a home created by Zion and Hanette, and also the place where he lived.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8104\" data-end=\"8223\">Meanwhile, he had risked his life and worked hard, reaching the present after leaving behind remarkable achievements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8225\" data-end=\"8320\">However, if this were taken away, wouldn’t it be considered neglecting even the minimum duty?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8322\" data-end=\"8382\"><em data-start=\"8322\" data-end=\"8380\">‘If things get difficult, I’ll study the spells myself…’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8384\" data-end=\"8404\">“Are you with me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8406\" data-end=\"8449\">A man in a suit emerged from the mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8451\" data-end=\"8496\">Enrite cleared his mind and approached him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8498\" data-end=\"8567\">“Wouldn’t you look sincere if you wake up earlier than the master?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8569\" data-end=\"8630\">“You are always sincere, how much more sincere can you be?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8632\" data-end=\"8684\">“Because Lesia is not sincere, we balance it out.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8686\" data-end=\"8735\">“Lesia is fine. You don’t need to be burdened.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8737\" data-end=\"8849\">“Just because you do your job well doesn’t mean you can be lazy. If I can’t work, I’ll chase them out myself.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8851\" data-end=\"8891\">“Well… even if I gave you permission?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8893\" data-end=\"8944\">“If you have no shame, shouldn’t you realize it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8946\" data-end=\"8990\">“If you say that, I’ll just be a villain.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8992\" data-end=\"9066\">“Being too good isn’t good. Why not try being a tyrant once in a while?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9068\" data-end=\"9136\">“Isn’t that a bit difficult? I think my wife would stop me first.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9138\" data-end=\"9189\">Zion responded calmly, a faint smile on his face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9191\" data-end=\"9279\">At first, when they wanted to bring Enrite into the mansion, they also included Lesia.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9281\" data-end=\"9402\">She was the ego of the demon sword and Enrite’s brother, and had a crafted demon sword, so it needed to be kept nearby.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9404\" data-end=\"9478\">Even if they only tried to bring Enrite, wouldn’t Lesia come on her own?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9480\" data-end=\"9539\">“The master said so… I guess I should step back for now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9541\" data-end=\"9611\">“Lesia faithfully fulfills her duties. What more can you ask there?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9613\" data-end=\"9685\">Of course, those who tried to infiltrate this mansion were quite rare.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9687\" data-end=\"9811\">Knights and soldiers guarded near the main gate, and even if someone passed the barrier, it would be detected immediately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9813\" data-end=\"9925\">If it weren’t for talented individuals like the Silver Ghost thief, attempting a break-in would be impossible.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9927\" data-end=\"10015\">“That’s right. I was a little surprised because I’ve never missed an intruder before.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10017\" data-end=\"10148\">“When Hanette and I sense the presence, Lesia is always the first. I personally replaced dozens of knights, and there’s no loss.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10150\" data-end=\"10194\">It was not a lie to ease Enrite’s worries.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10196\" data-end=\"10257\">Zion only spoke what he felt, and Hanette thought the same.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10259\" data-end=\"10383\">It wasn’t meant specifically to reduce the cost of ordinary soldiers, it was simply the result of unintentional obedience.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10385\" data-end=\"10433\">“I can let it be as long as it’s not harmful.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10435\" data-end=\"10482\">Enrite knew these words were not pretentious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10484\" data-end=\"10567\">On the contrary, if it were Zion, he would clearly check the part that was wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10569\" data-end=\"10633\">If he tried to endure it, wouldn’t he step forward and fix it?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10635\" data-end=\"10647\">“… Black.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10649\" data-end=\"10657\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10659\" data-end=\"10726\">“The situation at the palace isn’t serious. What are your plans?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10728\" data-end=\"10798\">“I want to stay quiet, but… it’s not easy, so I have many concerns.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10800\" data-end=\"10862\">Zion answered without hesitation, staring at the rising sun.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10864\" data-end=\"10998\">If he pretended not to know, Barhen and his family would take notice, and if he intervened, Brandis and the bureaucrats would worry.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11000\" data-end=\"11090\">He had to make a wise decision here to continue his relationship with Brandis and Juter.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11092\" data-end=\"11128\">“Have you considered this method?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11130\" data-end=\"11168\">“What method are you talking about?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11170\" data-end=\"11231\">“Silver… no, how about talking to Her Majesty the Empress?”</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-192/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"101\" data-end=\"104\">\r\n<p data-start=\"106\" data-end=\"164\">Zion hesitated for a moment, but quickly became certain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"240\">The silver phantom thief had a special connection with the current king.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"242\" data-end=\"341\">In some ways, he knew more than the royal family and could understand the king’s heart in detail.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"343\" data-end=\"380\">“…Your Majesty will be suspicious.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"382\" data-end=\"496\">“Your husband often takes walks at night. It’s not hard to arrange meetings because he treats me like a friend.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"498\" data-end=\"572\">After two years had passed, there was no choice but to change gradually.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"574\" data-end=\"664\">The number of people in Setinos Quasar hadn’t changed, but they moved in their own ways.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"666\" data-end=\"742\">Of course, not everyone changed, and some maintained consistent attitudes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"916\">“Just a brief meeting with a friend, merely chatting with a colleague. This isn’t secret assistance and has nothing to do with crime. Do you think it could be a problem?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"1021\">“My husband and I are quasar Cetinos, but we’re not in the same situation. Arms tend to fold inward.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1023\" data-end=\"1101\">Zion tried to keep her distance from many people to avoid misunderstandings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1103\" data-end=\"1210\">In Enrite’s case, she maintained neutrality, so even if she was close to him, no controversy would arise.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1212\" data-end=\"1343\">However, since the silver phantom thief, Caden Aslower, was the current king’s husband, she hesitated to contact them separately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1470\">“Your husband can distinguish between public and private matters. If it’s just a request for advice, he’ll gladly respond.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1479\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1481\" data-end=\"1526\">Zion continued to worry, buried in silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1528\" data-end=\"1573\">It wasn’t that she doubted Enrite or Caden.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1575\" data-end=\"1645\">They were merely monitoring intertwined conditions and environments.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1647\" data-end=\"1691\">Once entangled, it wasn’t easy to get out.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1693\" data-end=\"1815\">“I understand what you’re worried about. There’s no point in making things more complicated here. Isn’t it worth a try?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1817\" data-end=\"1850\">“I’ll discuss it with my wife.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1852\" data-end=\"1874\">Enrite said no more.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1876\" data-end=\"1931\">You can give them a choice, but you can’t force them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1933\" data-end=\"1998\">Not everyone thinks alike, and the directions they take differ.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2024\">“…Breakfast is ready.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2026\" data-end=\"2091\">One of the maids stepped out of the mansion and spoke politely.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2093\" data-end=\"2156\">After exchanging glances with Zion, Enrite followed the maid.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2158\" data-end=\"2226\">‘It’s natural to be suspicious. I can’t trust the king’s husband.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2228\" data-end=\"2293\">If it were Cettinos Quasar, he could be considered a colleague.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2382\">But because he was married to the king, he was exempt from the concept of a coworker.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2384\" data-end=\"2524\">Especially in a court where the balance between the king and the three princesses was delicate, could she express her feelings recklessly?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2526\" data-end=\"2580\">‘If it’s silver, maybe you already know the answer.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2582\" data-end=\"2712\">Caden met Brandis because of the theft, was appointed as Setinos Quasar, and conducted reconnaissance and intelligence missions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2714\" data-end=\"2810\">In the end, he won Brandis’s heart, and after marriage, rose to the position of queen consort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2812\" data-end=\"2893\">With Caden’s insight, wasn’t it possible to understand what Brandis didn’t say?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2895\" data-end=\"2942\">‘But I can’t choose… I guess I have to wait.’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2944\" data-end=\"2947\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2949\" data-end=\"3011\">Regarding the family household, Zion’s and Harnette’s rooms.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3013\" data-end=\"3123\">Since the Marquis of Reggiard had not inherited the title, none of his children could use the Marquis title.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3125\" data-end=\"3228\">In this situation, when a child became independent, they were referred to as “family,” not “marquis.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3230\" data-end=\"3353\">If one inherited the title, the other would become a baron, and only then could they be called the head of the household.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3355\" data-end=\"3430\">“…In the meantime, rumors are spreading about approaching the concubine.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3432\" data-end=\"3485\">Zion and Harnette finished breakfast and drank tea.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3487\" data-end=\"3557\">Zion waited until they were alone and explained Enrite’s invitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3559\" data-end=\"3603\">Harnette listened quietly until she spoke.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3605\" data-end=\"3630\">“So, what did you say?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3632\" data-end=\"3671\">“I said I would discuss it with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3673\" data-end=\"3721\">“Will hearing my opinion give you the answer?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3723\" data-end=\"3748\">“Then… can I force it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3750\" data-end=\"3763\">“That… No.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3765\" data-end=\"3839\">“So I want to hear your opinion. It’s not something I can decide alone.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3841\" data-end=\"3895\">Zion raised her teacup late and quenched her thirst.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3897\" data-end=\"3933\">Her life was also Harnette’s life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3935\" data-end=\"4040\">Because they were married, became a couple, and had decided to be together for the rest of their lives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4042\" data-end=\"4148\">If one side collapsed, the other would stumble, and in the end, neither she nor Harnette would be happy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4150\" data-end=\"4177\">“What do you want to do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4179\" data-end=\"4328\">“The method isn’t bad. You must know a lot because you’re married to the king. You may already be familiar with the palace situation. But… hmm… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4330\" data-end=\"4394\">Zion couldn’t bring herself to say she would accept the offer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4396\" data-end=\"4435\">Because she would have to take risks.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4437\" data-end=\"4479\">Approaching Caden could provoke Brandis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4481\" data-end=\"4505\">“You don’t trust him?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4507\" data-end=\"4577\">“I would have trusted if it had happened before I married the king.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4579\" data-end=\"4638\">“I guess I wouldn’t have trusted even before we married.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4640\" data-end=\"4654\">“Eh… maybe.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4656\" data-end=\"4737\">Caden accepted the Setinos Quasar title for Brandis, not for the Alain kingdom.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4739\" data-end=\"4857\">In other words, he would be an ally against demons, but if trapped in the power structure, he could be an adversary.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4859\" data-end=\"4931\">Just because he was a king didn’t mean she could obey unconditionally.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4933\" data-end=\"5016\">“The king has given us something. But it’s just a concession to serve us better.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5018\" data-end=\"5065\">“The tone is a bit off, but… it’s not wrong.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5067\" data-end=\"5171\">“The reason I tried to get you into the Royal Knight back then was purely out of my own greed, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5173\" data-end=\"5240\">“I resigned because I was a marquess. I was even engaged to you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5242\" data-end=\"5357\">“In the end, I bet on turning you into a Setinos Quasar. I could have refused if it weren’t for the princess… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5359\" data-end=\"5409\">Harnette clenched her chin, showing disapproval.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5411\" data-end=\"5456\">Zion had committed to peace with foresight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5458\" data-end=\"5550\">Still, Brandis tried to gain more advantage, and now he embarrassed both himself and Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5552\" data-end=\"5602\">“Even so, there are still golden veins left… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5604\" data-end=\"5744\">“That was because of your good foresight. I’ve built many achievements, but I had to give them land. It doesn’t mean you don’t pay taxes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5746\" data-end=\"5788\">“You’re not wrong, but now the king… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5790\" data-end=\"5843\">“We’ve already done enough! What makes you greedy?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5845\" data-end=\"5852\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5854\" data-end=\"5904\">Zion understood the feelings but couldn’t argue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5906\" data-end=\"5988\">This situation arose because her and Harnette’s marriage was based on a premise.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5990\" data-end=\"6115\">Since she was the royal family’s daughter-in-law and Harnette a duke’s daughter, she was inevitably involved in succession.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6117\" data-end=\"6237\">Moreover, the king also watched Duke Adelaira, and the three princesses grew more confused as they wanted his support.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6239\" data-end=\"6358\">“Mr. Barchen is the same! What did we ask you to do? You could leave it, but you’re dragged by the three princesses!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6360\" data-end=\"6394\">“Uh… I’m sorry about that part.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6396\" data-end=\"6462\">“It’s useless for you to apologize. Your family is the problem.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6464\" data-end=\"6525\">If the Marquis of Reggiard intervened, it could have ended.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6527\" data-end=\"6586\">But he ignored the situation and demanded more from Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6588\" data-end=\"6666\">In the end, Zion drew the line, and Barchen’s delayed action left ambiguity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6668\" data-end=\"6781\">“Huh… I thought everything would settle after I married, but so many things keep happening. What have we done?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6783\" data-end=\"6809\">“I’ve done many things.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6811\" data-end=\"6917\">“We just wanted to live well among ourselves, but they won’t leave it be. What if we leave the capital?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6919\" data-end=\"6953\">“That would only make it worse.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6955\" data-end=\"7053\">“Oh, I don’t know. Let them handle themselves. Should we come if we come, or leave if we leave?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7055\" data-end=\"7172\">“Do you know, being in the capital is convenient. It’s easy to get things, and I can bring people whenever I need.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7174\" data-end=\"7219\">“I’m not saying that because I don’t know.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7221\" data-end=\"7242\">“Yes, that’s true.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7244\" data-end=\"7284\">Zion sighed and took a piece of candy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7286\" data-end=\"7331\">Actually, this situation wasn’t unexpected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7333\" data-end=\"7428\">But it tended to twist too much, and being caught in the middle was troublesome in many ways.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7430\" data-end=\"7548\">“Right now, the only ones who can help us are my sister, Lesia, and the staff. The rest… is just… below… But still.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7550\" data-end=\"7587\">“Still, my brother-in-law is fine.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7589\" data-end=\"7654\">“Oh yes. I forgot for a moment because you were so kind to me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7656\" data-end=\"7770\">Harnette’s younger brother, Dain Adelaira, became the next head of the family and received training accordingly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7772\" data-end=\"7876\">Among his siblings, he was the only one handling the reins, and Robbins adjusted him little by little.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7878\" data-end=\"7977\">Recently, they said they tried to persuade the Marquis of Reggiard, but no good news has arrived.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7979\" data-end=\"8018\">“Duke Adelaira is also working hard.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8020\" data-end=\"8027\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8029\" data-end=\"8086\">Harnette agreed with the idea but did not say it aloud.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8088\" data-end=\"8146\">As usual, she wanted to keep her words about her father.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8148\" data-end=\"8230\">Although she still harbored a bit of resentment, she was also somewhat grateful.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8232\" data-end=\"8327\">“There’s no way out now. You can stay quiet like this, but you’ll hate the three princesses.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8329\" data-end=\"8387\">“The three princesses just didn’t ascend to the throne.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8389\" data-end=\"8459\">“But in this atmosphere… I have no choice but to become a princess.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8461\" data-end=\"8517\">Now there was no need to discuss the original content.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8519\" data-end=\"8621\">Given the changing situation and circulating rumors, becoming heir to Juter’s throne was inevitable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8623\" data-end=\"8673\">Even she and Harnette couldn’t resist the trend.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8675\" data-end=\"8729\">“Anyway, wouldn’t it be better if we both ran away?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8731\" data-end=\"8779\">“I think I’ve heard something similar before.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8781\" data-end=\"8814\">“Is it the same now as before?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8816\" data-end=\"8859\">“Even so, the situation isn’t that good.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8861\" data-end=\"8889\">“…Did you miss that time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8891\" data-end=\"8956\">“I missed it, and it was difficult. Still… I’m happy with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8958\" data-end=\"9011\">Zion gave a refreshing smile and answered casually.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9013\" data-end=\"9082\">Harnette blushed briefly, then returned to her original expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9084\" data-end=\"9122\">“Are you saying you’re unhappy now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9124\" data-end=\"9167\">“I’m happier now. You made me your wife.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9169\" data-end=\"9239\">“I’m happy too… It would be better if this situation didn’t happen.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9241\" data-end=\"9295\">Harnette expressed regret but maintained her spirit.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9297\" data-end=\"9383\">If she faltered, Zion would hesitate, and in the end, even this mansion would shake.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9385\" data-end=\"9451\">Just by helping Zion stand firm, she could overcome this crisis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9453\" data-end=\"9521\">‘I need to think again. If you still haven’t gotten an answer… ….’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9523\" data-end=\"9526\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9528\" data-end=\"9575\">Regarding the family household, Lecia’s room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9577\" data-end=\"9618\">Lecia went to bed early today as usual.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9620\" data-end=\"9707\">Ate three meals a day, snacked occasionally, and patrolled in and around the mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9709\" data-end=\"9794\">From the outside, she seemed idle, but only at night could she show her true worth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9796\" data-end=\"9824\">‘…There’s something here.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9826\" data-end=\"9871\">Lecia stared out the window with wide eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9873\" data-end=\"9913\">The guards didn’t notice the movement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9915\" data-end=\"9968\">Subtle mana changes, silent steps, swift movements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9970\" data-end=\"10031\">Clearly an intruder had entered the mansion with a purpose.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10033\" data-end=\"10065\">‘Maybe she’s somewhat strong?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10067\" data-end=\"10122\">Lecia threw off her blanket and leapt out the window.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10124\" data-end=\"10205\">At the same time, she called Dran Calgonis and quickly approached the intruder.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10207\" data-end=\"10242\">“Five… Are you paying attention?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10244\" data-end=\"10287\">A clean white blade tore through the air.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10289\" data-end=\"10361\">Then, from the darkness, someone appeared, lightly flicking their leg.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10363\" data-end=\"10429\">Lecia glared at the intruder and thrust her sword tip into them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10431\" data-end=\"10463\">“If it moves, it will be cut.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10465\" data-end=\"10515\">“Someone said… Is that White’s younger brother?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10517\" data-end=\"10565\">The intruder laughed and studied Lecia’s face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10567\" data-end=\"10659\">Gray horns appeared from black hair, and scales covering the body reflected the moonlight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10661\" data-end=\"10738\">Even amid that, surprisingly, their appearance resembled the White Apostle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10740\" data-end=\"10805\">“I am a guest who came to see Black. I want you to move aside.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10807\" data-end=\"10844\">“Can a guest sneak in at midnight?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10846\" data-end=\"10892\">“That’s my character. Shall I show my face?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10894\" data-end=\"10947\">The intruder removed their mask without hesitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10949\" data-end=\"10992\">Curved gray hair and glowing purple eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10994\" data-end=\"11070\">The silver phantom thief, Caden Aslower, displayed an enticing appearance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11072\" data-end=\"11152\">“I don’t want to fight my friend’s brother. Why don’t you try black or white?”</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-193/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"188\" data-end=\"191\">\r\n<p data-start=\"193\" data-end=\"241\">Lecia was late in recalling that voice and mask.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"323\">I must have met them during the battle against the Great King and the Demon God.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"420\">Even though she hadn’t fought at the time, she clearly remembered that he was a powerful human.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"513\">“You are the king’s… Ah, I’m married to His Majesty’s… companion? husband? wealth… wealth…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"515\" data-end=\"536\">“That’s a bad habit.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"538\" data-end=\"549\">“Yes, sir.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"624\">“So… do you intend to keep pointing your sword at His Majesty’s consort?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"655\">“You shouldn’t sneak in… yo?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"657\" data-end=\"711\">Lecia responded firmly, keeping a consistent attitude.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"713\" data-end=\"794\">If he had a legitimate reason and goal, he would have visited the mansion openly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"796\" data-end=\"912\">But the fact that he casually slipped through the barrier only after sunset left her no choice but to be suspicious.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"914\" data-end=\"1014\">“I believe I just said it. I had no choice but to come like this because I am a guest of the night.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1016\" data-end=\"1176\">“Uh… what was I supposed to say at a time like this… Ah, right. I faithfully carry out my duties as the exclusive knight commander of House Reggiard… mm? What?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1231\">Lecia frowned while showing a half‑hearted formality.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1233\" data-end=\"1347\">Even though she had learned a lot from Enrite, it wasn’t easy to change the way she spoke depending on the person.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1480\">It would be easier to use the same tone all the time, but as she kept replaying her thoughts, she unconsciously tangled herself up.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1545\">“Puh! Unlike black, the white one has a funny sharpness to it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1547\" data-end=\"1591\">Kaden found it amusing, but wasn’t careless.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1657\">She seemed stronger than before, and her eyes were full of life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1659\" data-end=\"1732\">If they crossed swords, he could handle it—but he wasn’t sure of victory.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1734\" data-end=\"1755\">‘… Black is popular.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1816\">No one was unaware of the achievements of the Black Knight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1818\" data-end=\"1918\">Of course, his companions helped him, and the King and Setinos Quasar didn’t just sit around either.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1920\" data-end=\"2038\">Still, because he led the situation while standing at the center, his achievements and military merit were recognized.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2040\" data-end=\"2090\">‘Which is why the white one must be here as well.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2092\" data-end=\"2179\">The White Apostle, Enrite Selena, left the Holy Church of Kinesien about two years ago.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2181\" data-end=\"2269\">She stated that she was no longer needed after defeating 3 demon kings and 4 calamities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2271\" data-end=\"2420\">She hid for a while and periodically reported to the king, ultimately entrusting herself to the house where the Black Knight and his companion lived.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2422\" data-end=\"2487\">‘I also left the Setinos Quasar… Lady Brandis barely stopped me.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2489\" data-end=\"2566\">At that time, Enrite resigned as cardinal and immediately entered the palace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2568\" data-end=\"2667\">Then she confronted Brandis and recited a spell asking her to release her duties as Setinos Quasar.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2669\" data-end=\"2767\">Brandis, slightly startled, tried to persuade Enrite, who reluctantly bowed and silently withdrew.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2769\" data-end=\"2821\">‘I wonder if she wanted to settle everything first.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2823\" data-end=\"2899\">Enrite had already told Brandis about her intention to stay in this mansion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2901\" data-end=\"2973\">Brandis eventually understood Enrite’s intentions and said nothing else.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2975\" data-end=\"3064\">She tried to relinquish her status and honor so she would not be involved in controversy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3066\" data-end=\"3113\">‘So the white one might get dragged into this…’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3115\" data-end=\"3141\">“Lecia, lower your sword.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3143\" data-end=\"3195\">A woman wearing a coat appeared along with soldiers.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3197\" data-end=\"3233\">Kaden waved lightly and greeted her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3235\" data-end=\"3266\">“It’s been a while, hasn’t it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3268\" data-end=\"3309\">“… Greetings to Her Majesty the Consort.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3311\" data-end=\"3352\">Enrite set an example and replied calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3354\" data-end=\"3437\">Then the surrounding soldiers looked at each other and awkwardly bowed their heads.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3439\" data-end=\"3510\">“That feels wrong… I want you to call me the way you always called me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3512\" data-end=\"3550\">“You mustn’t be rude to your husband.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3552\" data-end=\"3631\">“It feels strange to hear formal speech from a friend. Don’t you think so too?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3633\" data-end=\"3640\">“Uh… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3642\" data-end=\"3712\">Lecia couldn’t bring herself to speak and only looked between the two.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3714\" data-end=\"3756\">Kaden smiled and stepped closer to Enrite.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3758\" data-end=\"3786\">“As for what my sister did…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3788\" data-end=\"3904\">“She did what she needed to do. I have no intention of punishing you for it. I don’t have the authority to do that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3906\" data-end=\"3911\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3913\" data-end=\"3962\">Enrite showed a thin smile and quickly erased it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3964\" data-end=\"4002\">Kaden hadn’t changed much from before.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4004\" data-end=\"4086\">He had simply married the person he loved and received the title of royal consort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4088\" data-end=\"4116\">“You seem to be doing well.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4118\" data-end=\"4145\">“Thank you for your words.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4147\" data-end=\"4202\">“It’s not flattery. Your expression has become softer.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4204\" data-end=\"4254\">Kaden became sure of it once he saw Enrite’s face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4256\" data-end=\"4312\">Unlike before, there was a calmness, as if washed clean.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4314\" data-end=\"4399\">Perhaps living in this mansion had relieved her sense of responsibility and pressure.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4477\">“Aren’t nobles annoying? I wouldn’t leave a beautiful woman like you alone.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4479\" data-end=\"4522\">“… I haven’t had any meetings with nobles.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4524\" data-end=\"4594\">“Oh, right. You don’t go out unless necessary. I forgot for a moment.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4596\" data-end=\"4646\">Kaden showed a relaxed attitude and slowly turned.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4648\" data-end=\"4712\">The people he wanted to see were running toward them in a hurry.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4714\" data-end=\"4753\">“Greetings to Her Majesty the Consort.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4755\" data-end=\"4800\">“Black, long time no see. Is your wife well?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4802\" data-end=\"4812\">“Ah, yes…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4814\" data-end=\"4854\">Hanette bowed her head shyly, uncertain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4856\" data-end=\"4915\">Would Zion or Enrite come here unless there was some issue?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4917\" data-end=\"5032\">He did tend to visit secretly at night, but after being caught by Lecia, he reluctantly revealed his true identity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5034\" data-end=\"5104\">“Everyone I wanted to meet has gathered. Could you spare me a moment?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5141\">“Yes, I will prepare the carriage.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5143\" data-end=\"5201\">“I didn’t come to drink tea… My, this is a lot of people.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5203\" data-end=\"5262\">Kaden looked around with a slightly embarrassed expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5264\" data-end=\"5320\">Zion, Hanette, Enrite, Lecia, even knights and soldiers.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5322\" data-end=\"5384\">Contrary to what he expected, he had gathered quite the crowd.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5386\" data-end=\"5443\">‘I did talk with Lady Brandis, but… is this really okay?’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5445\" data-end=\"5450\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5452\" data-end=\"5493\">Residence of House Reggiard, living room.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5495\" data-end=\"5529\">It was midnight, but not too late.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5531\" data-end=\"5607\">Zion and Hanette had just been about to lie down, and Enrite couldn’t sleep.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5609\" data-end=\"5704\">In fact, Lecia was the first to fall asleep, but Kaden entered the courtyard and acted quickly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5706\" data-end=\"5755\">“… You’re wondering why I came here, aren’t you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5757\" data-end=\"5806\">Kaden quietly drank his tea and opened his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5808\" data-end=\"5871\">Right now, only Zion, Hanette, Enrite, and Kaden were gathered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5873\" data-end=\"5919\">Lecia had left earlier because she was sleepy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5921\" data-end=\"6054\">“You always come to me like this, so I won’t say anything wrong. But does your visit as the king’s husband have to be done secretly?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6056\" data-end=\"6110\">Enrite asked swiftly, not even glancing at her teacup.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6112\" data-end=\"6221\">The fact that the king’s wife was the silver‑masked phantom thief was well‑known across the Kingdom of Alain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6223\" data-end=\"6340\">But with all the speculation and rumors created by visiting people secretly at night, it was impossible not to worry.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6342\" data-end=\"6399\">“I was going to do that. But… I thought this was better.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6401\" data-end=\"6428\">“It might raise suspicion.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6430\" data-end=\"6621\">“Even before marrying His Majesty, I went around like this. Everyone knows—the bureaucrats, the nobles. Wouldn’t it look more suspicious if I walked through the front door in broad daylight?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6623\" data-end=\"6628\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6630\" data-end=\"6698\">It made too much sense, leaving Enrite no choice but to fall silent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6700\" data-end=\"6754\">Meeting Kaden or Zion alone already stirred curiosity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6756\" data-end=\"6803\">In that case, it would be better to act normal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6805\" data-end=\"6839\">“Let’s get straight to it… Black.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6841\" data-end=\"6847\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6849\" data-end=\"6902\">“Are you in trouble because of the three princesses?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6904\" data-end=\"6909\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6911\" data-end=\"6958\">Zion did not respond and swallowed the silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6960\" data-end=\"7035\">The king’s consort was speaking about the issue of the throne’s succession.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7037\" data-end=\"7070\">What was he supposed to say here?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7072\" data-end=\"7133\">“Is it hard to speak openly? Because I’m the king’s consort?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7135\" data-end=\"7174\">“… Yes. You might consider us enemies.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7176\" data-end=\"7249\">Hearing Zion’s answer, Hanette and Enrite were startled at the same time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7251\" data-end=\"7318\">He had bluntly brought up the word <em data-start=\"7286\" data-end=\"7293\">enemy</em> right in front of Kaden.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7320\" data-end=\"7387\">It was a dangerous statement, and could easily be taken negatively.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7389\" data-end=\"7418\">“W‑wow! That was too direct.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7420\" data-end=\"7516\">“His Majesty is watching us. Depending on the choice made, we might become enemies. Am I wrong?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7518\" data-end=\"7570\">“It sounds quite sad, but… I think you’re mistaken.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7572\" data-end=\"7611\">Kaden fully understood Zion’s position.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7613\" data-end=\"7713\">His own brother was married to the 3rd princess, and his own wife belonged to Duke Adelaira’s house.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7715\" data-end=\"7795\">Caught in the middle, he had no choice but to be cautious as the king’s consort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7797\" data-end=\"7994\">“Let’s reconsider. You and your wife have devoted yourselves to this country. His Majesty hasn’t forgotten that. Even with such great rewards, it doesn’t erase the contributions you two have made.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7996\" data-end=\"8046\">“… Are you saying His Majesty won’t drive us out?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8048\" data-end=\"8100\">“Correct. He will never expel you unless you rebel.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8102\" data-end=\"8134\">“You’re not worried about that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8136\" data-end=\"8299\">“You need to see the bigger picture. They simply don’t want power to concentrate in Duke Adelaira’s hands. Shouldn’t we separate that from the incident back then?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8301\" data-end=\"8391\">“I can’t separate it. Aren’t you being cautious because it <em data-start=\"8360\" data-end=\"8364\">is</em> related to that incident?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8393\" data-end=\"8431\">Zion had no intention of backing down.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8433\" data-end=\"8534\">Naturally, because Kaden was the king’s wife, he shouldn’t say anything that could spark controversy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8536\" data-end=\"8602\">But he couldn’t just accept everything either—he had to push back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8604\" data-end=\"8723\">“Black. I’ll say this clearly—I did not come here to oppose you. I didn’t receive any special orders from His Majesty.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8725\" data-end=\"8777\">“His Majesty must know that your husband came here.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8779\" data-end=\"8847\">“I always tell him where I go. Fortunately… he didn’t say anything.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8849\" data-end=\"8854\">“… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8856\" data-end=\"8889\">Zion could not trust those words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8891\" data-end=\"8956\">Brandis could easily have ordered Kaden to secretly evaluate him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8958\" data-end=\"9032\">He might even already know that Zion considered himself a potential enemy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9034\" data-end=\"9076\">Still, he didn’t regret speaking honestly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9078\" data-end=\"9122\">“I’ve already said it—don’t you understand?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9124\" data-end=\"9201\">“You’re saying you came here on your own, without His Majesty’s involvement?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9203\" data-end=\"9267\">“His Majesty didn’t forbid me to come. What does that tell you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9269\" data-end=\"9312\">“Should I take that as something positive?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9314\" data-end=\"9363\">“Black… His Majesty said he would not expel you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9365\" data-end=\"9409\">“Can you still say that after I’m executed?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9411\" data-end=\"9419\">“Black!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9421\" data-end=\"9479\">Enrite instinctively raised her voice, then suppressed it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9481\" data-end=\"9531\">Zion reluctantly closed his mouth and turned away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9533\" data-end=\"9560\">“Boss, I should apologize…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9562\" data-end=\"9670\">“There’s nothing to apologize for. If I were the Black Knight, I would have thought the same at least once.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9672\" data-end=\"9708\">Kaden was not angry upon hearing it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9710\" data-end=\"9749\">He understood Zion’s anxiety very well.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9751\" data-end=\"9821\">Even a small misunderstanding could take everything he had worked for.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9823\" data-end=\"9892\">If Hanette were put in danger, Zion’s reaction would be unimaginable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9894\" data-end=\"10171\">“… I’ll say this one more time. I did not come under the king’s orders. I am not here as the king’s consort. I came here as a Quasar and as a colleague of Cettinos. I will not report anything we say here. Why? Because this is a private conversation between me and my comrades.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10173\" data-end=\"10238\">Kaden spoke with complete honesty, sinking into his own concerns.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10240\" data-end=\"10287\">Zion, the Black Knight, did not trust the king.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10289\" data-end=\"10363\">If pushed into an extreme situation, he would inevitably lose to the king.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10365\" data-end=\"10425\">Only by stepping in now could he put an end to this tension.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10427\" data-end=\"10512\">“Black, I want to propose a way out of this situation for you… Will you hear me out?”</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-194/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"174\" data-end=\"177\">\r\n<p data-start=\"179\" data-end=\"230\">Zion was looking in Kaden’s direction at one point.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"306\">It might just be a personal opinion, but it might also be the king’s will.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"394\">If the king was indirectly recommending him through Kaden, how could that be accepted?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"518\">“Unfortunately… I don’t know if my proposal will work. I respect His Majesty’s thoughts and give my answer in my own way.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"520\" data-end=\"576\">“…Does that mean it has nothing to do with His Majesty?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"578\" data-end=\"707\">“I can’t say it has nothing to do with him. Am I not His Majesty’s consort? I only want you to regard it as my personal opinion.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"762\">Kaden emptied his teacup and poured himself more tea.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"864\">Zion and Enrite walked along as well, but quietly raised their hands, signaling that they were fine.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"1079\">“Are you sure about that one thing? No one has stayed by your side as I have. His Majesty didn’t tell me everything, but you can feel the atmosphere, right? I’ve learned a bit about those things little by little.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1081\" data-end=\"1141\">“So that’s why you came all the way here to give us advice?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1143\" data-end=\"1300\">“Your wife is right. As the queen, I hope His Majesty doesn’t lose talented people. As Setinos Quasar, I want to keep my comrades from getting into trouble.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1302\" data-end=\"1358\">Kaden showed a bitter smile and lifted his teacup again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1430\">As the king and Brandis’s wife, she tried to help and protect Brandis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1549\">At the same time, she wanted to have a conversation like this because she didn’t want Zion and Hanette to be unhappy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1551\" data-end=\"1716\">“This situation has put His Majesty and Black at odds. As for the order… His Majesty must have initiated it first. Isn’t this country shaking because of that duchy?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1718\" data-end=\"1782\">Harnette was a little surprised at this, but she didn’t show it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1784\" data-end=\"1855\">She did not bring up the noble family to ridicule or criticize herself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1857\" data-end=\"1920\">It was simply to explain the position between Zion and Brandis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1922\" data-end=\"2122\">“Of course, Black and Madam don’t think that way. If he truly meant to do that, he would have exploded long before now. His Majesty knows that, but he worries about the future because he foresees it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2124\" data-end=\"2155\">No one had done anything wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2157\" data-end=\"2263\">Brandis was aware of the tragedies of the past, and Zion and Harnette had never even considered rebellion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2265\" data-end=\"2359\">But because the conditions were intertwined, they began sharpening their blades at each other.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2361\" data-end=\"2462\">“…Black, why don’t you listen to me and think again? I don’t want to lose either His Majesty or you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2464\" data-end=\"2504\">Kaden’s voice carried her sincere heart.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2506\" data-end=\"2553\">But Zion couldn’t say he would do as she asked.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2555\" data-end=\"2617\">Kaden Aslower, the silver ghost thief, was the king’s consort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2619\" data-end=\"2697\">“Can’t you trust me? Then you just need to trust White. You know what I mean?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2699\" data-end=\"2748\">“Are you really going to use White as a witness?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2750\" data-end=\"2817\">“A witness for you. Meaning, to prepare for the time I betray you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2819\" data-end=\"2865\">Zion met Kaden’s eyes with a stiff expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2916\">Kaden looked relaxed, but her eyes clearly shone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2918\" data-end=\"2989\">She must have foreseen this happening and brought Enrite to this place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2991\" data-end=\"3137\">“If you follow my instructions and something goes wrong, you may name White as your witness. I’m certain His Majesty won’t doubt what White says.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3139\" data-end=\"3194\">Kaden had glimpsed Brandis’s thoughts little by little.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3196\" data-end=\"3335\">Watching Zion and Hanette’s movements, knowing where they went yet not intervening, even knowing the conversations between her and the two.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3337\" data-end=\"3396\">Perhaps Brandis wanted this situation resolved in some way.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3398\" data-end=\"3427\">“…What do you want me to do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3429\" data-end=\"3477\">He had to listen first before making a decision.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3479\" data-end=\"3542\">After all, the king’s consort had personally come to his house.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3544\" data-end=\"3630\">Even if he rejected the proposal later, he still had to maintain the minimum courtesy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3632\" data-end=\"3789\">“If something happens with the three princesses in the future, you may go alone. If it’s an event or banquet, you’ll be able to state your thoughts clearly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3791\" data-end=\"3835\">Zion immediately understood what that meant.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3837\" data-end=\"3959\">The fact that Hanette would not appear before the three princesses also meant the Duchess of Adelaira would not interfere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3961\" data-end=\"4063\">Moreover, in a banquet attended by many nobles, such actions would be noticed and rumors would spread.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4065\" data-end=\"4199\">“Madam, why don’t you make a statement to His Majesty the King? You just need to clearly explain the part about the Duchess Adelaira.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4201\" data-end=\"4248\">“…Can that be done by removing my family name?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4250\" data-end=\"4305\">This time, Kaden panicked and straightened her posture.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4307\" data-end=\"4406\">Normally, when a man and woman married, the woman left her original family name and took the man’s.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4408\" data-end=\"4492\">However, if the woman held a higher status or title, her family name could continue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4494\" data-end=\"4575\">If Harnette decided it, it wouldn’t be hard to change it to the Reggierd surname.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4577\" data-end=\"4597\">“Harnette, you… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4599\" data-end=\"4668\">“It’s fine. It’s fine even if I’m no longer the Duchess of Adelaira.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4670\" data-end=\"4750\">“Lady Adelaira, His Majesty will not allow that. It would be an act of treason.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4752\" data-end=\"4825\">“I know. But if we at least do this much, wouldn’t His Majesty trust us?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4827\" data-end=\"4878\">Harnette was no longer bound by her family’s power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4880\" data-end=\"4963\">Of course it might help later, but she had to face the problem in front of her now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4965\" data-end=\"5066\">Most importantly, Zion was the only one she needed, so she was willing to throw away what she didn’t.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5068\" data-end=\"5223\">“All you need to do is go to the palace and declare that you will not interfere with the succession of the throne. His Majesty will understand your heart.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5225\" data-end=\"5298\">If it was Brandis, he would at least listen to Harnette’s words a little.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5300\" data-end=\"5423\">She had contributed greatly with the Black Knights, and at one point, the appointment of Setinos Quasar had been mentioned.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5425\" data-end=\"5505\">Since she was a hero who had achieved merit, it was impossible not to trust her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5507\" data-end=\"5652\">“…Say it one last time: His Majesty trusts you and your wife. No matter what happens, I will protect both of you and not treat you as criminals.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5654\" data-end=\"5739\">“Will you still trust us even after the three princesses become heirs to the throne?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5741\" data-end=\"5806\">“Black, how deep are your doubts that you can’t clear your mind?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5808\" data-end=\"5942\">“No one knows what will happen in the future. Do you think the princess won’t use the Marquis of Regiard and the Duchess of Adelaira?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5944\" data-end=\"5983\">Brandis and Kaden might be trustworthy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5985\" data-end=\"6062\">However, the future would continually change, and he couldn’t help but doubt.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6064\" data-end=\"6156\">People changed their minds over time, and if they had great power, they would use it easily.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6158\" data-end=\"6380\">“His Majesty must be thinking right now that choosing a princess would distress me and the Duchess Adelaira. But if he must choose between the first prince or the second, then the third princess would waste her qualities.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6382\" data-end=\"6389\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6391\" data-end=\"6550\">“If not for me and my wife, none of this would be happening. Otherwise, it would have been fine if the third princess and my older brother were not connected.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6552\" data-end=\"6619\">Zion spoke the words that had been in his heart without hesitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6621\" data-end=\"6681\">After all, Kaden must have come because she sensed a crisis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6683\" data-end=\"6786\">From his perspective, there was no room to retreat, so he was simply trying to negotiate one last time.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6788\" data-end=\"6891\">“This time, I’ll make an offer. I want you to take back the Setinos Quasar title that was given to me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6893\" data-end=\"6913\">“…What do you mean?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6915\" data-end=\"6983\">“It means I’ll put down everything that could threaten His Majesty.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6985\" data-end=\"7049\">Hanette and Enritte were bewildered, but they couldn’t stop him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7051\" data-end=\"7107\">Zion was about to discard what he had for his own peace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7109\" data-end=\"7188\">Of course, he couldn’t give up everything, but he could ease Brandis’s worries.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7190\" data-end=\"7301\">“At present, I am not cooperating with my family. You surely know why. And my wife is taking a similar stance.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7303\" data-end=\"7345\">“…Black, you said you weren’t suspicious.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7347\" data-end=\"7444\">“His Majesty and your husband may not doubt us. But don’t you have conditions that force you to?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7446\" data-end=\"7488\">Zion repeated his thoughts as he answered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7490\" data-end=\"7571\">If he used this situation well, he could throw off all the burdens placed on him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7573\" data-end=\"7654\">Brandis saw him and Harnette as talents he needed, but also as potential threats.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7656\" data-end=\"7706\">“Even if we leave Setinos Quasar, this won’t end.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7708\" data-end=\"7827\">“That is why His Majesty must issue a royal decree. Shouldn’t you pressure me so that the three princesses understand?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7829\" data-end=\"7836\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7838\" data-end=\"7879\">Kaden thought it was an excellent method.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7881\" data-end=\"7963\">If Zion’s position was elevated as a royal command, many people would take notice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7965\" data-end=\"8098\">Yuter, who was trying to borrow Zion’s power, would shrink back, and the royal family and nobles surrounding him would be frightened.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8100\" data-end=\"8291\">“If you punish me now, I can serve as an example. After that, you only need to guide them to be aware and silent. The nobles won’t approach me for fear of being seen as opposing His Majesty.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8293\" data-end=\"8381\">“I understand what you mean. But then… only you and your wife will be treated unfairly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8383\" data-end=\"8486\">“Someone must endure it. My wife will understand my choice. If I can help His Majesty, that is enough.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8488\" data-end=\"8543\">Zion tried to hide his true intent and answered calmly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8545\" data-end=\"8610\">Things like Setinos Quasar and the succession no longer mattered.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8612\" data-end=\"8664\">He only wanted to live a peaceful life with Hanette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8666\" data-end=\"8711\">“I don’t think His Majesty will like it… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8713\" data-end=\"8786\">“I know it’s impossible. I know His Majesty won’t punish me excessively.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8788\" data-end=\"8818\">“That may be true. But… sigh…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8820\" data-end=\"8875\">Kaden felt troubled, but she couldn’t reject the offer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8877\" data-end=\"8945\">If Zion sacrificed himself, Brandis could resolve everything easily.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8947\" data-end=\"9025\">However, remembering what Zion had achieved until now, her guilt grew heavier.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9027\" data-end=\"9141\">“This is the best I can do for you. If anything else happens later, I’ll have no choice but to leave the capital.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9143\" data-end=\"9200\">It was the choice he should have made from the beginning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9202\" data-end=\"9285\">After losing the Setinos Quasar title, all that remained was being a wealthy noble.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9287\" data-end=\"9397\">Of course, it would only be a symbolic punishment—there would be no seizure of assets or extreme imprisonment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9399\" data-end=\"9442\">He would simply be a hero bearing a stigma.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9444\" data-end=\"9527\">“I’ll have to tell His Majesty the truth. I don’t know if he’ll accept your offer.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9529\" data-end=\"9586\">Her mouth was dry, but she couldn’t reach for the teacup.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9588\" data-end=\"9634\">She didn’t want to ease this tension and pain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9636\" data-end=\"9695\">It felt like selling a comrade for the sake of a loved one.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9697\" data-end=\"9753\">‘How am I supposed to explain this to Lady Brandis… … .’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9755\" data-end=\"9760\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9762\" data-end=\"9804\">Royal palace, the royal sleeping quarters.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9806\" data-end=\"9845\">A woman with black hair lay on the bed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9847\" data-end=\"9918\">Now in her forties, her beauty seemed to grow deeper instead of fading.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9920\" data-end=\"9974\">She couldn’t sleep, waiting for her partner to return.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9976\" data-end=\"10054\">Before long, they met again, but only the strange proposal echoed in her ears.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10056\" data-end=\"10100\">“…Are you trying to make yourself a sinner?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10102\" data-end=\"10177\">“I said that if something like this happens again, I’ll leave the capital.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10179\" data-end=\"10186\">“Sigh…”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10188\" data-end=\"10219\">Brandis stood and began pacing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10221\" data-end=\"10289\">He had accomplished so much, yet now he wanted to throw it all away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10291\" data-end=\"10402\">He had lived peacefully after the kingdom found peace, but had inadvertently gotten caught in a political plot.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10404\" data-end=\"10481\">“It’s not that I don’t understand, but I can’t let everything fall on Black.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10483\" data-end=\"10630\">“Lady Brandis, you can’t only look at Black. The three princesses and the Duchess Adelaira are the same. If you don’t choose, nothing will change.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10632\" data-end=\"10682\">Kaden recited her spell with a serious expression.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10684\" data-end=\"10726\">There was no need to make Zion a criminal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10728\" data-end=\"10823\">They could restrain the Duchess Adelaira, and choose either the first or second prince as heir.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10825\" data-end=\"10879\">But she couldn’t decide because nothing satisfied her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10881\" data-end=\"10915\">“Boss, what do you want me to do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10917\" data-end=\"10952\">“I can’t say it with my own mouth.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10954\" data-end=\"10961\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10963\" data-end=\"10998\">Silence filled the sleeping palace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11000\" data-end=\"11084\">Kaden conveyed her intention with only one word, and Brandis understood immediately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11086\" data-end=\"11149\">The sacrifice of one innocent person would be the best outcome.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11151\" data-end=\"11179\">‘My greed has gone too far.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11181\" data-end=\"11251\">Brandis had tried to keep both Zion Regard and Barchen Reggiard close.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11253\" data-end=\"11400\">For the sake of Setinos Quasar, for the three princesses, to subdue the three demon kings and four calamities, for the future of the Alain Kingdom.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11402\" data-end=\"11502\">Some of these goals had been fulfilled, but in the end he had no choice but to send them away again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11504\" data-end=\"11566\">‘Reality is harsh, ideals are distant. How foolish I’ve been…’</p></div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-195/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"80\" data-end=\"83\">\r\n<p data-start=\"85\" data-end=\"120\">Maybe it’s better to leave it be.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"122\" data-end=\"167\">At least no innocent people will be harmed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"169\" data-end=\"231\">But since it’s already spilled, there’s no way to turn back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"233\" data-end=\"276\">“… Didn’t Black say something different?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"376\">“Those were words said when asking for a greeting. I made an offer first, but… I was persuaded.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"378\" data-end=\"445\">Caden deliberately refused to explain further what had been said.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"447\" data-end=\"530\">It was a private matter, so he wanted to respect both his own and their thoughts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"553\">“You must hate me.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"564\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"566\" data-end=\"627\">“I should have behaved better… Greed came before judgment.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"674\">Brandis slowly stopped and closed his eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"676\" data-end=\"748\">Just stripping him of the Setinos Quasar title was humiliating enough.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"871\">Moreover, the bureaucrats and nobles would doubt Zion even if they didn’t understand the reasoning behind the decision.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"873\" data-end=\"972\">Perhaps the Setinos Quasars and other clever nobles could grasp the meaning of Zion’s punishment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"974\" data-end=\"1035\">“I also said I would enter the palace as soon as possible.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1037\" data-end=\"1071\">“That will be our last meeting.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1146\">“Not like that. If Your Majesty calls, Black will always come running.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1148\" data-end=\"1280\">“That’s shameless. Ever since the punishment was given, darkness has been abandoned. How could I call back someone I left behind!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1282\" data-end=\"1335\">Brandis poured out his emotions without hesitation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1337\" data-end=\"1401\">Ever since Zion told him to punish him, I could see his heart.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1403\" data-end=\"1497\">He must be very disappointed in himself, and he must be fed up with his family and brothers.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1499\" data-end=\"1627\">As time passed, the situation worsened, leaving him with no choice but to reach the conclusion that he would cut himself down.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1681\">“Black is considering Lady Brandis’ feelings… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1683\" data-end=\"1795\">“So that’s wrong. A peerless black knight. Can you treat a hero who gave his life for this country like this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1797\" data-end=\"1921\">“Your Majesty, just because you desire it doesn’t mean you can have it. If Black is wasted, you could use another method.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1923\" data-end=\"1954\">Brandis also knew the answer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1956\" data-end=\"1982\">But he could not decide.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1984\" data-end=\"2059\">Because if he chose another way, he would have to give up more than that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2061\" data-end=\"2140\">“Even though you say you cannot speak, are you insisting on only one method?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2142\" data-end=\"2201\">“Because that method is in Your Majesty’s best interest.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2203\" data-end=\"2244\">“Isn’t Black your husband’s companion?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2246\" data-end=\"2353\">“… I decided to consider my spouse before my comrades. I want Your Majesty to make the decision as well.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2355\" data-end=\"2366\">“Sir… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2368\" data-end=\"2400\">Brandis looked at Caden sadly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2402\" data-end=\"2466\">Caden showed a sad expression, but his face remained the same.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2468\" data-end=\"2550\">Even if he turned away from that black knight, he would willingly blame himself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2552\" data-end=\"2715\">“His wrongdoing is fraud and dereliction of duty. As a result, the Setinos Quasar property and part of his assets are seized as punishment. May I conclude this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2717\" data-end=\"2765\">“Black also expected the seizure of property.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2767\" data-end=\"2820\">“I won’t take much. For example… just a little… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2822\" data-end=\"2844\">Brandis fell silent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2846\" data-end=\"2920\">For his own comfort and the country’s welfare, he tried to trap someone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2922\" data-end=\"3071\">Of course, because of this, the black knight would not be swept up in the power struggle, but he would not be able to clear his name until he died.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3073\" data-end=\"3081\">“Sir.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3083\" data-end=\"3091\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3093\" data-end=\"3127\">“It’s me… Do you still love me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3129\" data-end=\"3170\">“I know this is an unavoidable choice.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3172\" data-end=\"3206\">“Do you not regret marrying me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3208\" data-end=\"3285\">“Ever since I have served Your Majesty until now… I have always loved you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3287\" data-end=\"3296\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3298\" data-end=\"3340\">Brandis felt relieved just hearing that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3342\" data-end=\"3392\">The usual Caden would not ignore such an action.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3394\" data-end=\"3450\">He reluctantly agreed because it was connected to her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3452\" data-end=\"3490\">‘I don’t know what to say to Black.’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3492\" data-end=\"3499\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3501\" data-end=\"3552\">Outskirts of the Kingdom of Alein, Aliard Castle.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3554\" data-end=\"3678\">Compared to several years ago, monster invasions have decreased, yet the number of troops hasn’t been drastically reduced.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3680\" data-end=\"3790\">Even if the 3 Great Demon Kings and 4 Great Calamities have disappeared, the Witch Beasts themselves remain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3792\" data-end=\"3967\">The purple temple clearly revealed the facts before the king and officials, and as a result, the issue could be resolved by reducing only a few troops in the border regions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3969\" data-end=\"3997\">“… Did you hear the news?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3999\" data-end=\"4074\">The purple priest, Baltz Cabadrion, looked out from the castle and spoke.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4076\" data-end=\"4152\">The knight beside him was silent for a moment before reluctantly replying.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4154\" data-end=\"4162\">“Yes.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4164\" data-end=\"4196\">“I want to hear your opinion.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4198\" data-end=\"4248\">“You don’t seem right. Something must be wrong.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4250\" data-end=\"4289\">Seran gave a sharp look and asserted.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4291\" data-end=\"4404\">Meanwhile, he spent his time in remote areas, training his swordsmanship and fighting endlessly against demons.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4406\" data-end=\"4484\">He felt himself growing stronger, and his magical power gradually increased.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4486\" data-end=\"4582\">Even amidst his personal transformation, he could not accept the news coming from the capital.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4584\" data-end=\"4632\">“I think so too, but… there must be a reason.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4634\" data-end=\"4642\">“Why?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4644\" data-end=\"4730\">“Your Majesty made a choice you didn’t want, and Black was forced to make a choice.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4732\" data-end=\"4740\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4742\" data-end=\"4821\">Saeran pondered it several times but couldn’t grasp the meaning of his words.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4823\" data-end=\"4900\">Baltz maintained his posture for a while, but it was too late to turn back.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4902\" data-end=\"4927\">“Don’t you understand?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4929\" data-end=\"4967\">“I don’t know why it had to happen.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4969\" data-end=\"5083\">“You should know the details. This is a situation where the black knight had no choice but to be dragged along.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5085\" data-end=\"5122\">“Why did Black have to be dragged?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5124\" data-end=\"5316\">“That is the meaning of power. The more you have, the more you desire, and even if you want to stay quiet, you won’t be allowed. Black surely tried to get out, but he was inevitably caught.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5318\" data-end=\"5373\">“If that’s the case… Do you mean the noble families?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5375\" data-end=\"5444\">“Marquis of Reggiard and Duke of Adelaira. What else do you think?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5446\" data-end=\"5515\">“I understand that Black’s older brother married the 3rd daughter.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5517\" data-end=\"5531\">“What else?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5533\" data-end=\"5613\">“Black is connected to the rank of a Duke of Adelaira, and a duke’s rank… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5615\" data-end=\"5672\">Saeran stopped and recalled something he had forgotten.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5674\" data-end=\"5730\">There must have long been confusion because of a duke.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5732\" data-end=\"5803\">Could it be that the black knight was suspected just because of that?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5805\" data-end=\"5900\">“This doesn’t make sense. Are you trying to blame Black for something that already happened?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5902\" data-end=\"5983\">“Even when someone dies, power does not vanish. It just moves to someone else.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5985\" data-end=\"6013\">“Black would never rebel!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6015\" data-end=\"6050\">“Ssst, I have to cover my words.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6052\" data-end=\"6092\">Baltz calmed Saeran and looked around.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6094\" data-end=\"6201\">Even in the capital, this would cause an uproar, but he could not spread the rumor even in the outskirts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6203\" data-end=\"6302\">The soldiers’ morale must be prevented from falling, and the king’s authority must not be shaken.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6304\" data-end=\"6405\">“Black risked his life to protect the Kingdom of Alein! And Lady Adelaira? Are you still in doubt?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6407\" data-end=\"6524\">“… I understand. Black is a hero of this country. His comrades fought alongside him. I have no such doubts either.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6526\" data-end=\"6569\">Baltz answered calmly and shook his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6571\" data-end=\"6642\">Even if no one else knew, the king must not ignore that black knight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6644\" data-end=\"6752\">The same applies to the Setinos Quasar, and at least high-ranking officials must protect the black knight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6754\" data-end=\"6850\">However, he wondered if this had become difficult because politics and power were intertwined.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6852\" data-end=\"7006\">“Yet the situation occurred, so we have no choice but to act accordingly. Your Majesty must have thought deeply. Black must have known and accepted it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7008\" data-end=\"7085\">“You accepted it knowingly? I committed no sin, so why must I be punished?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7087\" data-end=\"7119\">“If not… many people may die.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7121\" data-end=\"7197\">“Isn’t there a reason why Black must be responsible for those people too?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7199\" data-end=\"7275\">“That is a word that encompasses Black. What if Lady Adelaira were there?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7277\" data-end=\"7330\">Saeran tried to say something but lowered his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7332\" data-end=\"7432\">Even if the black knight could give his own life, he would not tolerate the death of his comrades.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7434\" data-end=\"7546\">His comrade must have the same heart as the black knight, so he wondered if he chose the easier way to end it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7548\" data-end=\"7708\">“Your Majesty knows how it continues. You also expect the outcome. That’s why you chose Black. If only one black knight is sacrificed, no one else is harmed.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7710\" data-end=\"7756\">“Ha ha… So, can you try to use Black later?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7758\" data-end=\"7809\">“I can’t use him anymore. I’ve also been warned.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7811\" data-end=\"7830\">“Who warned you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7832\" data-end=\"7993\">“The three princesses and their close nobles, the Marquis of Reggiard, and the Duke of Adelaira. Everyone knows Black and White. Do you still understand this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7995\" data-end=\"8014\">“… I understand.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8016\" data-end=\"8075\">Saeran finally realized the position of the black knight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8077\" data-end=\"8146\">You don’t have to go out, but you never know what will happen next.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8148\" data-end=\"8225\">That’s why he became a sinner alone, trying to protect his wife and family.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8227\" data-end=\"8277\">“Still, it’s not just Black who suffers losses.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8279\" data-end=\"8358\">“Yes? I am punished and even lost my title, so why do I not suffer any loss?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8360\" data-end=\"8545\">“Haven’t I told you before? Now no one can approach Black. Your Majesty also made me a criminal to avoid touching the black knight. From now on, I will live comfortably with my wife.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8547\" data-end=\"8625\">“Even so… It’s unfair. There’s no reason Black should be treated like that!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8627\" data-end=\"8636\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8638\" data-end=\"8683\">Even Baltz could not refute that statement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8685\" data-end=\"8756\">Perhaps the king and black knight used this method after negotiation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8758\" data-end=\"8862\">It was clearly a rational result, but those who fought alongside the black knight would not accept it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8864\" data-end=\"8916\">No matter the reason, the method itself was wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8918\" data-end=\"8961\">“Why do you think you told me the truth?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8963\" data-end=\"8993\">“That… I’m not sure either.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8995\" data-end=\"9098\">“You are a comrade who fought alongside Black. If you are a colleague, shouldn’t you know the truth?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9100\" data-end=\"9151\">“Better not to know. What you can do is know… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9153\" data-end=\"9250\">“I’m not asking you to do anything for me. If you are truly Black’s comrade, what should I do?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9252\" data-end=\"9286\">Saeran recalled Zion’s memories.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9288\" data-end=\"9362\">Zion treated the knights under his command well but did not burden them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9364\" data-end=\"9485\">Instead, he tried to handle everything himself, and in the end, he gave me a generous salary and even words of comfort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9487\" data-end=\"9558\">Perhaps we should trust that Zion’s judgment is correct and faithful.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9560\" data-end=\"9596\">“… We must respect that decision.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9598\" data-end=\"9668\">“Yes, that’s enough. If you do that, even Black will appreciate it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9670\" data-end=\"9724\">That was something Zion did with firm determination.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9726\" data-end=\"9808\">However, if you go out alone and discard it for Zion, everything would collapse.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9810\" data-end=\"9889\">A true comrade should not destroy that resolve even if they know it is wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9891\" data-end=\"9917\">“It’s very unfortunate.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9919\" data-end=\"9957\">Baltz looked at himself skeptically.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9959\" data-end=\"10013\">Knowing and pretending not to know is a heavy trial.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10015\" data-end=\"10055\">If you didn’t know, you wouldn’t care.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10057\" data-end=\"10118\">‘The Setinos Quasar title is gone… The popularity remains.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10120\" data-end=\"10164\">Of course, not many people knew the truth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10166\" data-end=\"10256\">At most, it would be limited to Setinos Quasar, high-ranking officials, and some nobles.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10258\" data-end=\"10407\">However, the achievements Zion and Hanette accomplished will last a long time, and the good deeds accumulated during that time will return someday.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10409\" data-end=\"10470\">‘This is the bitter truth. Black cannot be perfect either.’</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-196/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"91\" data-end=\"94\">\r\n<p data-start=\"96\" data-end=\"161\"><strong data-start=\"96\" data-end=\"159\">Royal Palace, the gymnasium dedicated to the Royal Knights.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"163\" data-end=\"230\">As soon as Oz joined the Royal Knights, his skill was recognized.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"330\">Of course, he didn’t use the Demon Sword, relying solely on swordsmanship and his magical power.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"332\" data-end=\"436\">Now, sword skills could be executed without the Demon Sword, and his level continued to rise even now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"438\" data-end=\"468\">“What are you doing! Focus!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"470\" data-end=\"530\">A heavy wooden sword came crashing down with a loud shout.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"601\">Oz hesitated for a moment but reacted quickly, blocking the strike.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"669\">However, the wooden sword he held twisted awkwardly in his grip.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"671\" data-end=\"736\">“Are you going to fight like this even in front of the enemy?!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"819\">The Royal Knights’ commander, Gloone Eilike, raised his voice and stared at Oz.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"903\">The tip of the wooden sword was right in front of his eyes, but Oz felt no fear.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"973\">He kept repeating the news he had just heard and lowered his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"975\" data-end=\"1041\">“Is there still life left? Life, once lost, cannot be regained!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1080\">“…Captain, why do I have to fight?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1126\">Glonet frowned in surprise at that moment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1128\" data-end=\"1192\">It was impossible for the Oz he knew to say something so weak.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1194\" data-end=\"1277\">On the contrary, even if criticism came, he should endure it and wield his sword.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1413\">“You are a member of the Royal Knights. If you are a knight of His Majesty, you must carry out your mission until your last breath.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1415\" data-end=\"1470\">“Will anyone remember me after I fight to the death?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1551\">“His Majesty the King will not forget. Many knights will remember your name.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1553\" data-end=\"1602\">“Then… why must the Black Knight be like that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1604\" data-end=\"1613\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1615\" data-end=\"1688\">Glonet had suspected it, but hearing it himself left him quite shocked.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1690\" data-end=\"1784\">Brandis hadn’t said anything about the Black Knight, but the hidden truth could be inferred.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"1897\">Perhaps Brandis had removed the Black Knight and was indirectly trying to convey that meaning to some people.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1899\" data-end=\"1988\">“If you have sinned… you deserve punishment. Even the Quasar Cettinos is no exception.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1990\" data-end=\"2100\">“The Black Knight gave his life for this country. Lady Adelaira followed that will. By the way… but why… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2102\" data-end=\"2178\">Glonet gritted his teeth and grasped his sword hilt with all his strength.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2180\" data-end=\"2226\">He understood how Oz felt when he said that.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2228\" data-end=\"2309\">He hadn’t committed a heinous crime and could have received a light punishment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2402\">Yet Brandis didn’t even revoke the title of Setinos Quasar, and even seized his property.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2404\" data-end=\"2472\">“If you are a citizen of this country, you must abide by the law.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2474\" data-end=\"2562\">“Captain… you know. The punishment is too harsh for that crime. Can I really do this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2564\" data-end=\"2661\">“It is not for you to decide. His Majesty has his own reasoning, so he punished you like that.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2663\" data-end=\"2724\">Glonet protected Brandis while hiding his own speculations.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2726\" data-end=\"2793\">He couldn’t judge whether the king’s decision was right or wrong.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2795\" data-end=\"2890\">As the leader of the Royal Knights, he only escorted the king and followed the king’s orders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2892\" data-end=\"3120\">“I am grateful for the kindness His Majesty has shown me. You accepted me as a member of the Royal Knights when I had no place to go. Now, as a member of the Royal Knights, I have pride, and I do my best to improve my skills.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3122\" data-end=\"3131\">“… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3133\" data-end=\"3389\">“I respect you, Your Majesty. Aren’t you the one who went to the battlefield on behalf of the soldiers? You fought alongside me and won. Your Majesty knows what kind of person the Black Knight is. You can understand more… did you really have to do that?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3391\" data-end=\"3471\">Initially, he should have been reprimanded for insulting His Majesty the King.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3473\" data-end=\"3528\">But Glonet couldn’t speak, and just listened quietly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3530\" data-end=\"3584\">Because he himself had doubts, he implicitly agreed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3586\" data-end=\"3737\">“…I’m not necessarily right. The Black Knight made a great mistake, but His Majesty may have covered for him. Perhaps the Black Knight was deceived.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3739\" data-end=\"3786\">Oz muttered endlessly with slumped shoulders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3788\" data-end=\"3862\">He should train his sword skills as usual, but his body wouldn’t follow.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3864\" data-end=\"3970\">He shouldn’t have said this in front of the Royal Knights’ Commander, but he couldn’t hold back anymore.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3972\" data-end=\"4092\">“Now I don’t know. There must be a reason, but… is this right? I saw the Black Knight fight. I know how you fight… ….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4094\" data-end=\"4143\">Oz pursed his lips, unable to speak any longer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4145\" data-end=\"4217\">Even though it wasn’t happening to him personally, he felt frustrated.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4219\" data-end=\"4283\">His eyes trembled, but he couldn’t stop the lump from forming.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4285\" data-end=\"4312\">“Sorry. I’m leaving now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4314\" data-end=\"4357\">Oz quickly turned and left the gymnasium.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4399\">Glonet only stared silently after him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4422\">‘Your Majesty… … .’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4424\" data-end=\"4474\">If it weren’t for Oz, he wouldn’t have listened.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4476\" data-end=\"4532\">Oz had fought many battles following the Black Knight.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4534\" data-end=\"4619\">That was why he couldn’t hide his tears, even though he was upset by the treatment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4663\">‘Why did you abandon that Black Knight?’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4665\" data-end=\"4719\">It wasn’t that he didn’t understand Brandis’ choice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4721\" data-end=\"4825\">There was no other option but to do that, and the Black Knight would surely understand to some degree.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4827\" data-end=\"4903\">But did a hero who had achieved so much need to be brought down like that?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4905\" data-end=\"4937\">‘What would others think… … .’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4939\" data-end=\"5035\">The majority of nobles and citizens would believe that the Black Knight had committed a crime.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5037\" data-end=\"5132\">Unlike him, dukes, marquesses, and high-ranking officials would try to understand the reason.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5134\" data-end=\"5186\">Perhaps the Quasar Cetinos already knew the truth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5188\" data-end=\"5252\">‘I should have stayed silent at least for Quasar Cetinos… … .’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5254\" data-end=\"5257\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5259\" data-end=\"5310\"><strong data-start=\"5259\" data-end=\"5308\">Reggieard Family Residence, garden courtyard.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5373\">Zion was walking leisurely while looking around the garden.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5375\" data-end=\"5462\">Since the mansion was small, the space for the garden was limited but easy to manage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5464\" data-end=\"5588\">Usually, a gardener would be hired to maintain the garden, but sometimes Zion and Harnette would plant flowers themselves.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5590\" data-end=\"5615\">“…What about Harnette?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5672\">Enrite walked alongside Zion, cautiously speaking up.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5674\" data-end=\"5801\">The king had accepted Zion’s petition and restored the title of Setinos Quasar by requesting the acknowledgment of the crime.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5803\" data-end=\"5906\">Additionally, a fine was imposed, but it was a token punishment and no excessive amount was demanded.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5908\" data-end=\"5975\">He only reluctantly humbled himself as if he were being punished.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5977\" data-end=\"6048\">“I can’t see it as a good thing. I’m not satisfied with my decision.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6050\" data-end=\"6099\">“Wasn’t that a decision made after discussion?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6101\" data-end=\"6224\">“I’m not saying my method was bad. You could see it this way. I can understand it, but that means I have to be involved.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6226\" data-end=\"6238\">“Hmm… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6240\" data-end=\"6304\">Enrite didn’t even look at the flowers, repeating her worries.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6306\" data-end=\"6390\">No matter how much Zion wanted to console her, there was nothing more he could do.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6392\" data-end=\"6480\">It was a wise choice from Zion’s perspective, but Harnette only saw the negative side.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6482\" data-end=\"6640\">“That’s a good approach. Your Majesty has removed your anxiety, and the three princesses can no longer wear black. In the future, the nobles will not come.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6642\" data-end=\"6758\">“You’re right. That’s good for me. It’s just a little bothersome that I was punished for a crime I didn’t commit.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6760\" data-end=\"6827\">Zion had been concerned about this even before marrying Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6829\" data-end=\"6880\">Because he and Harnette had many matters at hand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6882\" data-end=\"6956\">Some wanted to borrow that power, others would look for possible abuses.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6958\" data-end=\"7048\">Zion didn’t want to be caught in the middle, so he chose a way to resolve it peacefully.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7050\" data-end=\"7189\">“Harnette doesn’t like making people in black the villains. You have lived a righteous life, so there’s no reason to be a sinner, right?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7191\" data-end=\"7366\">“…That’s extreme. All I needed was a safety rope and some decent money. Being twisted like this because of the Setinos Quasar title and the achievements I’ve earned so far.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7368\" data-end=\"7488\">“That’s why Your Majesty also accepted Black’s petition. Even if you remove it now, won’t it get tangled again later?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7490\" data-end=\"7558\">Enrite had been monitoring the palace situation for several years.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7560\" data-end=\"7670\">The behavior of the three princesses was unusual, and the Marquis Regard family also agreed with this trend.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7672\" data-end=\"7772\">In this situation, even if Zion compromised with the king, the problem would resurface eventually.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7774\" data-end=\"7816\">Zion knew this and ended it immediately.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7818\" data-end=\"7873\">“The fine isn’t much. You only pretended to take it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7875\" data-end=\"7951\">“If you really wanted to punish, it wouldn’t have ended with just a fine.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7953\" data-end=\"8111\">“There are many ways. Golden veins, a large house, and properties can all be confiscated. You could imprison me, or send me into distant exile. Or not… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8113\" data-end=\"8184\">Zion hesitated at the end of his words, but quickly closed his mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8186\" data-end=\"8226\">Enrite already knew what would happen.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8228\" data-end=\"8326\">It was the worst punishment a person could receive, and once executed, it would never be undone.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8328\" data-end=\"8398\">“There’s nothing good about that. I’m glad it’s all over like this.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8400\" data-end=\"8417\">“Yes, but… … .”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8419\" data-end=\"8463\">Zion frowned as he recalled recent events.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8465\" data-end=\"8560\">Saeran sent a letter inquiring about his condition, and Oz shed tears while hugging Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8562\" data-end=\"8696\">His father announced that he would no longer intervene, and the Duke Adelaira fully understood the situation while offering comfort.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8698\" data-end=\"8805\">The Blue Sage came directly to the mansion, speaking as if he knew everything, and showed strong resolve.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8807\" data-end=\"8900\">“There are many who want to help Black. Haven’t you built a good reputation all this time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8902\" data-end=\"8946\">“I’m just grateful that I have no doubts.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8948\" data-end=\"8988\">“Blue won’t spoil a word once spoken.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8990\" data-end=\"9046\">“…If you behave like that, there will be controversy.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9048\" data-end=\"9214\">“There will be controversy, but it’s not wrong. If you request the release of your title with a valid reason, His Majesty the King has no choice but to reconsider.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9216\" data-end=\"9311\">The Blue Sage said that if this happened again, he would relinquish the Setinos Quasar title.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9313\" data-end=\"9403\">It was a move to show that this was unfair treatment, and other magicians could join in.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9405\" data-end=\"9506\">If the situation spread to other regions, it wouldn’t be easy to suppress with just a king’s order.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9508\" data-end=\"9619\">“Purple also knows the details of this incident. There will be no one among Quasar Cetinos who doesn’t know.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9621\" data-end=\"9681\">“Thank you for your concern, but… this will be permanent.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9683\" data-end=\"9756\">It was something he and Brandis had understood first and then acted on.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9758\" data-end=\"9850\">There was no point in delaying, and it eliminated problems that would arise in the future.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9852\" data-end=\"9937\">Now he and Harnette were truly free, and nothing would interfere with this routine.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9939\" data-end=\"9967\">‘I can’t have everything.’</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9969\" data-end=\"10051\">The reality was harsh, and it was even difficult to envision an ideal situation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10053\" data-end=\"10148\">Even the king who ruled this country couldn’t be perfect, so he sacrificed himself for peace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10150\" data-end=\"10205\">He also gave up part of what he had to achieve peace.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10207\" data-end=\"10284\">If he hadn’t come into this world, what kind of future would have unfolded?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10286\" data-end=\"10382\">‘Would this world have collapsed? Or perhaps I would have won at the cost of many sacrifices.’</p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-197/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<p data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"345\">The western region of the Kingdom of Alain, retreating roads.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"430\">Demonic beasts had occupied the capital, and the royal palace lay in complete ruin.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"522\">Zion Regiard looked back on his own life, clutching loosely at the bitter path behind him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"586\">It had been so dull, so ordinary, without any lofty ambitions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"588\" data-end=\"667\">He only wanted to maintain a comfortable life by following his family’s wishes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"669\" data-end=\"696\"><em data-start=\"669\" data-end=\"696\">‘…Where did it go wrong?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"698\" data-end=\"750\">He had the question, but he already knew the answer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"752\" data-end=\"803\">He tried to stand tall no matter what he was given.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"805\" data-end=\"871\">He never tried to do anything; he only tried to hide his thoughts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"873\" data-end=\"922\">That was why his fiancée had surely run from him.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"924\" data-end=\"956\"><em data-start=\"924\" data-end=\"956\">‘Should I have worked harder?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1056\">If he had reached the battlefield a little sooner, maybe things would have turned out differently.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1138\">If he’d had a bit more courage, perhaps he could have protected the front lines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1140\" data-end=\"1248\">But because he was lazy and cowardly, he couldn’t do anything before the demonic beasts invaded the capital.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1250\" data-end=\"1285\"><em data-start=\"1250\" data-end=\"1285\">‘Only two Setino Quasars remain.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1287\" data-end=\"1320\">The White Apostle, the Blue Sage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1358\">Only two of the five still survived.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1457\">The Purple Temple fell at the front lines, and the Silver Phantom Thief died protecting the king.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1459\" data-end=\"1572\">The Golden Swordsman, enraged at the sight, threw himself forward; his body was torn apart battling the monsters.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1574\" data-end=\"1612\"><em data-start=\"1574\" data-end=\"1612\">‘Three demon-sword wielders remain.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1663\">Himself, the White Apostle, and Hanette Adelaira.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1665\" data-end=\"1820\">The Earth Demon Sword, Gerganber, was sealed by the Demon God, and the Wind Demon Sword, Timer, vanished when the Shadow Dragon fled into the shadow realm.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"1972\">At the very least, people searched for the Lightning Magic Sword <em data-start=\"1887\" data-end=\"1896\">Nailing</em> and the Ice Magic Sword <em data-start=\"1921\" data-end=\"1929\">Ferndy</em>, but they couldn’t even find their bodies.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1974\" data-end=\"2006\"><em data-start=\"1974\" data-end=\"2006\">‘I won’t last long like this.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2092\">Zion became convinced that the Kingdom of Alain would inevitably fall to the demons.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2094\" data-end=\"2251\">Demonic beasts swarmed within and around the capital, and the Demon God, having absorbed the power of the third Demon King, was fighting the fourth calamity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2253\" data-end=\"2403\">They could barely hold back the magical monsters as it was; if the demons or the Four Great Calamities approached, they would be swept away instantly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2405\" data-end=\"2467\"><em data-start=\"2405\" data-end=\"2467\">‘Trying to counterattack while retreating… It’s impossible.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2469\" data-end=\"2540\">There were too many magical beasts, and only a handful could use magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2542\" data-end=\"2683\">Most importantly, the Demon God and the Four Calamities were using their overwhelming power freely, and no one could erase their immortality.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2685\" data-end=\"2761\">Even if they fled and planned for the future, they could never destroy them.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2763\" data-end=\"2801\"><em data-start=\"2763\" data-end=\"2801\">‘It might be better to flee by sea.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2803\" data-end=\"2835\">Of course, that too wasn’t safe.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2837\" data-end=\"2938\">Currents were unpredictable and fierce, and dozens of storms surrounded the continent of Karon Belaz.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2940\" data-end=\"3065\">Even if the ship’s surface was reinforced with magical power, no one knew whether it could withstand the currents and storms.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3067\" data-end=\"3139\"><em data-start=\"3067\" data-end=\"3139\">‘I finally met my fiancée again after so long… Will it end like this?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3141\" data-end=\"3217\">It hadn’t been a warm reunion; they couldn’t even properly greet each other.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3219\" data-end=\"3291\">She reluctantly accepted the engagement, and then she secretly ran away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3293\" data-end=\"3391\">Even so, they met again in the capital and now fought side by side as fellow magic-sword wielders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3393\" data-end=\"3457\"><em data-start=\"3393\" data-end=\"3457\">‘At the very least… I should try talking to her before I die.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3459\" data-end=\"3502\">Zion dragged his weary body toward a woman.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3504\" data-end=\"3569\">By coincidence, she also sensed his presence and turned her head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3571\" data-end=\"3664\">Her orange hair and pale skin were stained with sweat and dust, but her beauty was unchanged.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3666\" data-end=\"3698\">“Are you not going to greet me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3700\" data-end=\"3722\">“… You don’t have to.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3724\" data-end=\"3761\">“I feel like I should, at least now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3763\" data-end=\"3811\">Hanette Adelaira looked at Zion with sharp eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3813\" data-end=\"3898\">Their engagement had been forced by their families, nothing more than an arrangement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3900\" data-end=\"3974\">Her partner couldn’t even say a single word and always seemed indifferent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3976\" data-end=\"4060\">In the end, to avoid marriage, she’d left Duke Adelaira and fled to a remote region.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4062\" data-end=\"4126\">“…Sorry. I don’t know why… I just felt like I should apologize.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4128\" data-end=\"4196\">“There’s nothing for you to apologize for. I acted the way I chose.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4198\" data-end=\"4262\">“I acted the way I chose too. I hoped we could get along, but….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4264\" data-end=\"4310\">Zion glanced around and swallowed the silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4312\" data-end=\"4356\">The defeated soldiers walked without spirit.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4358\" data-end=\"4435\">Everyone had lost family and comrades, and there weren’t even bodies to bury.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4437\" data-end=\"4507\">Monsters would keep coming; humans would slowly die off until the end.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4509\" data-end=\"4555\">“It’s all in the past. You can do better now.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4557\" data-end=\"4608\">“I don’t think ‘doing better’ will solve anything.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4610\" data-end=\"4636\">“Then wait until you die.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4638\" data-end=\"4671\">“…You’re going to keep fighting?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4673\" data-end=\"4734\">“I’m not stupid like you. Even if I die, I’ll die in battle.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4736\" data-end=\"4776\">Zion laughed softly and turned his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4778\" data-end=\"4809\">Hanette glared at him, annoyed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4811\" data-end=\"4826\">“What’s funny?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4828\" data-end=\"4907\">“Oh—sorry. I didn’t mean to mock you. I just… wished I could be like that too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4909\" data-end=\"4913\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4915\" data-end=\"4945\">Hanette fell silent, confused.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4947\" data-end=\"4983\">Why was he acting like a friend now?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4985\" data-end=\"5049\">Like before, he should just look at her quietly and say nothing.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5051\" data-end=\"5119\">Even if they grew closer, they could only remain wary of each other.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5121\" data-end=\"5249\">“As you can see, I’m weak. My magic is weaker than yours, and I got my demon sword too late. I can’t do anything alone anymore.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5251\" data-end=\"5283\">“Stop whining. It’s irritating.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5285\" data-end=\"5394\">“Since I don’t know when I’ll die, I wanted to have one last conversation. You <em data-start=\"5364\" data-end=\"5369\">are</em> my fiancée, aren’t you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5396\" data-end=\"5449\">“What does that matter? It wasn’t a good engagement.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5451\" data-end=\"5521\">“You’re right, but… it doesn’t change the fact that we <em data-start=\"5506\" data-end=\"5511\">are</em> engaged.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5523\" data-end=\"5557\">Zion steadied his trembling voice.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5559\" data-end=\"5628\">After this moment, would he ever get the chance to see Hanette again?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5630\" data-end=\"5686\">One of them might die first, or they might die together.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5688\" data-end=\"5752\">So if there was anything he wanted to say, he had to say it now.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5754\" data-end=\"5859\">“If I could be born again… you should meet someone cooler than me. There must be someone better for you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5861\" data-end=\"5895\">“Hah… Are you leaving a will now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5897\" data-end=\"5968\">“No one is left for me. My family is gone. So… you’re all I have left.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5970\" data-end=\"5974\">“….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5976\" data-end=\"6082\">“You’ve gone through so much. I want to break off the engagement, but right now… it’s a little difficult.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6084\" data-end=\"6106\">“You can do it later.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6108\" data-end=\"6159\">Hanette snapped at him and grabbed Zion’s shoulder.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6161\" data-end=\"6202\">She didn’t want to hear weakness forever.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6204\" data-end=\"6258\">Without hope, one wouldn’t have the strength to go on.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6260\" data-end=\"6299\">“Say it again. Then maybe I’ll listen.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6301\" data-end=\"6348\">“I’ll try. It’d be unfair if I died like this.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6350\" data-end=\"6411\">“Why are you talking nonsense when you’re perfectly capable?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6413\" data-end=\"6462\">Hanette let go of Zion’s shoulder and walked off.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6464\" data-end=\"6542\">To her, Zion was an outsider; she had no intention of binding him to anything.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6544\" data-end=\"6625\">But right now, survival came first, so she could at least treat him as a comrade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6627\" data-end=\"6687\"><em data-start=\"6627\" data-end=\"6687\">‘Kids like him are the first to die. It makes me anxious.’</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6689\" data-end=\"6694\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6696\" data-end=\"6723\">“Why did you go out alone!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6725\" data-end=\"6799\">Hanette’s voice trembled as she searched frantically to stop the bleeding.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6801\" data-end=\"6842\">The attack was one she should have taken.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6844\" data-end=\"6939\">But the man had blocked it for her, and the demon sword had pierced and broken inside his body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6941\" data-end=\"7003\">Meanwhile, the man protecting her had not been injured at all.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7005\" data-end=\"7053\">“S-someone… cooler than me… meet… someone cool!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7055\" data-end=\"7104\">Zion coughed bright red blood and shook his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7106\" data-end=\"7143\">Hot liquid seeped from his left side.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7145\" data-end=\"7193\">The pain was intense—yet somehow, slowly fading.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7195\" data-end=\"7227\">“Why are you worrying about me!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7229\" data-end=\"7258\">“B-Because I’m your fiancé….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7260\" data-end=\"7273\">“Ah… I see….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7275\" data-end=\"7324\">Hanette hurriedly wrapped cloth around the wound.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7326\" data-end=\"7394\">But the bleeding wouldn’t stop. Even the cloth was soaked instantly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7396\" data-end=\"7471\">The word “death” repeatedly flashed through her mind, filling her thoughts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7473\" data-end=\"7519\">“I’m sorry… If I hadn’t been engaged to you….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7521\" data-end=\"7562\">“How is that your fault! Why would you…!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7564\" data-end=\"7606\">Zion was in the same situation as she was.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7608\" data-end=\"7662\">Yet Zion didn’t leave, while <em data-start=\"7637\" data-end=\"7642\">she</em> had run away first.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7664\" data-end=\"7714\">It had been her fault—so why was Zion apologizing?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7716\" data-end=\"7794\">“I never loved you, but… you still deserve someone who takes responsibility….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7796\" data-end=\"7836\">“Then why… were you the one who… fell…?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7838\" data-end=\"7893\">“Make sure you live… and meet someone cooler than me….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7895\" data-end=\"7949\">“Stop talking! You’ll die for real if you keep going!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7951\" data-end=\"8022\">“If I’m going to die anyway… I want my last words… to mean something….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8024\" data-end=\"8087\">Zion did not look away from Hanette, though his vision blurred.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8089\" data-end=\"8167\">The inevitable fate of all humans—disappearing from the world—was approaching.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8169\" data-end=\"8263\">At the very least, he wondered if it was a comfort to accept that fate for his fiancée’s sake.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8265\" data-end=\"8307\">“It’s a promise… someone better than me….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8309\" data-end=\"8357\">Zion slowly closed his eyes and tilted his head.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8359\" data-end=\"8404\">His heart had stopped. His breath faded away.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8406\" data-end=\"8476\">Hanette bit her lip, and only then did she grasp the truth before her.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8478\" data-end=\"8515\">“I don’t need… something like that….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8517\" data-end=\"8548\">Flames wrapped around her body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8550\" data-end=\"8598\">Monsters charged in, and soldiers fled in panic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8600\" data-end=\"8650\">A few knights tried to resist but fell helplessly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8652\" data-end=\"8695\">Was there even anywhere left to retreat to?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8697\" data-end=\"8730\">“I can live just fine on my own.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8732\" data-end=\"8784\">Hanette swung her flames, scattering tiny fragments.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8786\" data-end=\"8864\">Hundreds of sparks struck the monsters, burning their filthy bodies instantly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8866\" data-end=\"8911\">He told her to survive—then she must survive.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8913\" data-end=\"8941\">“I didn’t love you either….”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8943\" data-end=\"8987\">Hanette turned away, conjuring flames again.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8989\" data-end=\"9043\">Two or three sparks drifted and fell upon Zion’s body.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9045\" data-end=\"9113\">Rather than letting the monsters take him, she cremated him herself.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9115\" data-end=\"9215\"><em data-start=\"9115\" data-end=\"9215\">‘Next time… let’s meet as friends. If we meet as friends, maybe we can greet each other properly.’</em></p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9217\" data-end=\"9222\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9224\" data-end=\"9280\">Lingvern Castle, western region of the Kingdom of Alain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9282\" data-end=\"9397\">It stood at the far west based on the capital, yet it had remained the final fortress through repeated withdrawals.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9399\" data-end=\"9460\">If this castle fell, the Kingdom of Alain would be destroyed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9462\" data-end=\"9553\">Enrithe entered the castle with the remnants of his army, though he knew there was no hope.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9555\" data-end=\"9607\"><em data-start=\"9555\" data-end=\"9607\">‘Even though I prepared… I couldn’t withstand it.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9609\" data-end=\"9719\">He had gathered demon swords and wielders for a long time and even subdued demonic beasts along the outskirts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9721\" data-end=\"9848\">But he couldn’t eliminate their enemies, and as a result, the Demon God revived, rampaging alongside the four great calamities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9850\" data-end=\"9936\">Among the magic-sword users, he alone survived. All other Setino Quasars had perished.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9938\" data-end=\"9967\"><em data-start=\"9938\" data-end=\"9967\">‘Should I use that method?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9969\" data-end=\"10022\">Enrithe listened to the voice coming from El Tesoicb.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10024\" data-end=\"10114\">If he gathered the power of all demon swords, he could return everything to the beginning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10116\" data-end=\"10187\">Enrithe understood the suggestion but wasn’t sure whether it was right.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10189\" data-end=\"10215\"><em data-start=\"10189\" data-end=\"10215\">‘Is there no other way?’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10217\" data-end=\"10258\">He gripped El Tesoicb and raised it high.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10260\" data-end=\"10357\">If the future could not be reached, he would return to the past and search for new possibilities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10359\" data-end=\"10494\">Of course, no living being—including himself—would remember this terrible reality, but he could prevent the world from being destroyed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10496\" data-end=\"10535\">A silver light emerged from El Tesoicb.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10537\" data-end=\"10618\">Demon swords scattered across the continent of Karon Belaz gathered in one place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10620\" data-end=\"10703\">Most had lost their power, but remnants remained—enough to forge a new demon sword.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10705\" data-end=\"10740\"><em data-start=\"10705\" data-end=\"10740\">‘All of them… I’ll restore them.’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10742\" data-end=\"10783\">The demon swords fused around El Tesoicb.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10785\" data-end=\"10878\">Though El Tesoicb had lost its unique power, it now shone with a more brilliant silver light.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10880\" data-end=\"10959\">Enrithe whispered the name of the reborn demon sword and drew in all its magic.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10961\" data-end=\"10998\"><em data-start=\"10961\" data-end=\"10998\">‘The Sword of Reversal… Mayna Un….’</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11000\" data-end=\"11046\">He trusted his own judgment and used Mayna Un.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11048\" data-end=\"11084\">Vivid colors spread along its blade.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11086\" data-end=\"11182\">Brilliant silver light engulfed Lingvern Castle, then the monsters, demons, and four calamities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11184\" data-end=\"11286\">Eventually, even the continent of Karon Belaz was swallowed, and even the sea was caught in its color.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"11288\" data-end=\"11332\"><em data-start=\"11288\" data-end=\"11332\">‘I’ll continue until I achieve my desire!’</em></p>\r\n</div>",
                    $"<div class=\"content\"><a href=\"https://bacalightnovel.co/i-became-the-fiance-of-a-crazy-heroine-raw-chapter-198/\">GPT translated</a>\r\n<hr data-start=\"90\" data-end=\"93\">\r\n<p data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"132\"><strong data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"130\">8. I’m Still Happy (Completely)</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"189\"><strong data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"187\">Reggiard Family Residence, Medicine Storage Room.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"282\">Enrithe frequently went back and forth to the medicine storage room to prepare medicines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"339\">This had to be ready in case treatments were delayed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"341\" data-end=\"492\">Besides, even if the medicine was the same, if the sexual method was mixed in, the effect would be slightly better, so it was just for entertainment.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"494\" data-end=\"553\">“What are you doing here? You could just buy it outside.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"594\">Lesia helped Enrithe while grumbling.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"596\" data-end=\"695\">As long as you stay quiet, you won’t be disturbed, but you have to pretend to be doing something.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"778\">Even if Zion and Harnette could watch over him, the staff would have questions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"880\">That’s why while patrolling inside and outside the mansion, she even helped Enrithe with his work.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"882\" data-end=\"931\">“It’s better to make it myself than to buy it.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"958\">“Because of the magic.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"990\">“Boring to just stay still.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1010\">“It’s better… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1012\" data-end=\"1070\">“And you should work to make the best use of your time.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1092\">“Can’t I do this?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1140\">Originally, Enrithe was only given one task:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1204\">To treat anyone injured in the mansion immediately, anytime.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1206\" data-end=\"1345\">It was a simple and easy task for Enrithe, who had trained her voice, and with so few injuries in the mansion, it wasn’t a huge workload.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1347\" data-end=\"1434\">Even so, Enrithe tried to find other work on her own, and Lesia reluctantly followed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1512\">“You eat a lot, but aren’t you paid? If I don’t do much, nothing is left.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1514\" data-end=\"1567\">“What? That’s exactly why I have to eat this much!”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1569\" data-end=\"1636\">“If you have a conscience, shouldn’t you look at yourself first?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1638\" data-end=\"1699\">Lesia frowned, thinking about the food she had eaten today.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1701\" data-end=\"1829\">For breakfast, she had tasted soup with soft bread and expensive seafood, and had neatly eaten the fruit that came as dessert.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1831\" data-end=\"1919\">In addition, there were no snacks left for tea, and she ended up finishing the teapot.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1921\" data-end=\"1953\">“Um… Are you eating too much?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1955\" data-end=\"2006\">“Are you saying this because you really feel it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2130\">“Still, do you work as much as you eat? That… I’m helping with what you’re doing too. Sometimes I even work at night… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2132\" data-end=\"2172\">“Oops… Are you taking this seriously?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2174\" data-end=\"2225\">Enrithe placed the medicine box down and laughed.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2227\" data-end=\"2278\">Lesia stared at her absentmindedly, then frowned.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2280\" data-end=\"2310\">“What? Did you try it once?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2312\" data-end=\"2333\">“Isn’t that wrong?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2335\" data-end=\"2450\">“I do everything I can. Eating more doesn’t cause a problem. Isn’t that better than leaving food to go to waste?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2452\" data-end=\"2517\">“That’s trash… Are you trying to say something convincing now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2519\" data-end=\"2572\">Enrithe was satisfied and looked at Lesia intently.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2574\" data-end=\"2677\">Living as a human, she surely realized what the world is made of and how it is organically connected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2679\" data-end=\"2803\">Of course, that was just a reason to rationalize her own actions, but it must be seen that she had made a lot of progress.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2805\" data-end=\"2873\">“Even black doesn’t say anything… Oh, did I make a mistake again?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2875\" data-end=\"2911\">Enrithe muttered with gloomy eyes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2913\" data-end=\"3003\">Since she lost the Cetinos Quasar position, she could no longer be called by skin color.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3005\" data-end=\"3076\">She had promised to use a different title, but it still felt awkward.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3078\" data-end=\"3128\">“Didn’t I tell you to call me by my first name?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3130\" data-end=\"3176\">“I know, but… it’s not easy to get used to.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3178\" data-end=\"3188\">“Hmm… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3190\" data-end=\"3233\">Lesia closed her mouth and looked around.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3235\" data-end=\"3316\">She didn’t know the details, but she often expressed mixed feelings about Zion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3318\" data-end=\"3379\">She felt she had to say something to change the atmosphere.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3381\" data-end=\"3419\">“Alright… Should I get married now?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3421\" data-end=\"3444\">“You mean? hehehe… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3446\" data-end=\"3511\">Enrithe suddenly laughed, and Lesia frowned, answering instead.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3513\" data-end=\"3602\">There must be a reason to laugh, but could she really react like that to just one word?</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3604\" data-end=\"3624\">“I can do it too.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3626\" data-end=\"3669\">“I can do that. But who would marry you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3671\" data-end=\"3754\">“Speaking of the Cetinos Quasar sibling, how many people would come to see them?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3756\" data-end=\"3802\">“Are you going to sell me off and marry me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3804\" data-end=\"3859\">“That’s something I can do because I’m your sibling.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3861\" data-end=\"3893\">“Then you need my permission.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3895\" data-end=\"3904\">“…Why?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3906\" data-end=\"4013\">“Because she’s your sibling. Since there are no parents, shouldn’t I take responsibility in their place?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4015\" data-end=\"4054\">“Ahh… Are you trying to be a parent?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4056\" data-end=\"4106\">“I have to. I can’t entrust you to just anyone.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4108\" data-end=\"4116\">“… …?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4118\" data-end=\"4163\">Lesia fell silent at the unexpected answer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4165\" data-end=\"4237\">Only then did Enrithe start moving the medicine boxes without smiling.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4239\" data-end=\"4433\">“You don’t fully understand what marriage is. The same goes for those who aren’t married to me. So if you really want to marry, think hundreds of times before deciding. Now, listen seriously.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4435\" data-end=\"4498\">Enrithe wanted to respect Lesia’s wishes as much as possible.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4500\" data-end=\"4631\">Even if she left me, she wouldn’t resist me, and if there was something she wanted to do, she would help me as much as she could.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4633\" data-end=\"4715\">Of course, because she had a forged sword, she had to discuss how to discard it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4717\" data-end=\"4772\">“Do you have to know each other well to get married?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4774\" data-end=\"4899\">“Just knowing isn’t enough. You must be dedicated and caring. Black… did you feel anything when you saw Zion and Harnette?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4901\" data-end=\"4942\">“They seem to fight pretty well too… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4944\" data-end=\"5043\">“Because they think differently. Conversely, if we don’t fight, we see that there’s no dialogue.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5045\" data-end=\"5097\">“Does lack of conversation mean things get worse?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5099\" data-end=\"5289\">“Similar. Think about the first time you and I met. It was hard to talk to them, and even when we did, it led to arguments. If we have a good relationship, we can find compromise quickly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5291\" data-end=\"5331\">Lesia was confused, but nodded slowly.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5333\" data-end=\"5413\">She wondered if it was difficult, even though strangely, it seemed acceptable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5415\" data-end=\"5532\">Meanwhile, I had learned the general concept with humans, but there were certainly many things I still didn’t know.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5534\" data-end=\"5570\">“Um… Anyway, I have to marry you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5572\" data-end=\"5602\">“That’s too much of a joke.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5604\" data-end=\"5765\">“No one knows me as well as you. I also know a lot about you. Many things I have dedicated myself to and taken care of for you all this time. Isn’t that fine?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5767\" data-end=\"5823\">“After… Have I been teaching you wrong all this time?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5825\" data-end=\"5869\">Enrithe sighed deeply and gave a sad look.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5871\" data-end=\"5922\">Lesia clearly understood the concept of marriage.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5924\" data-end=\"6005\">Even so, she maintained her consistent attitude, occasionally talking nonsense.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6007\" data-end=\"6106\">“What she said… ah! Love escape. Yes. Let’s do that. That way, you can escape from your concept.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6108\" data-end=\"6155\">“Tell me why you have to run away from here.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6157\" data-end=\"6196\">“Reason? I’ll tell you the reason… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6198\" data-end=\"6263\">Lesia seemed to purse her lips, but soon swallowed her silence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6307\">There was no reason to leave this house.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6309\" data-end=\"6392\">She was formally employed, paid regularly, and the tasks given weren’t difficult.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6394\" data-end=\"6512\">Most importantly, there was no better environment than this, since you could eat all the food and snacks you wanted.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6514\" data-end=\"6549\">“And why do I have to marry you?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6551\" data-end=\"6582\">“Yes… uh… Maybe you like me?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6584\" data-end=\"6641\">“Now I’m starting to hate you more, what do you think?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6643\" data-end=\"6676\">“That… shouldn’t we work hard?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6678\" data-end=\"6708\">“If you know, help quickly.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6710\" data-end=\"6791\">Lesia reluctantly lifted the medicine boxes, a helpless expression on her face.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6793\" data-end=\"6884\">Enrithe glared at Lesia for a moment and belatedly began checking the amount of medicine.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6886\" data-end=\"6936\">‘This is marriage… If you’re black, a little… …’</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6938\" data-end=\"6941\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6943\" data-end=\"7002\"><strong data-start=\"6943\" data-end=\"7000\">About the family residence, Zion and Harnette’s room.</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7004\" data-end=\"7095\">Zion hadn’t left the mansion even once since he was stripped of the Setinos Quasar title.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7097\" data-end=\"7239\">If there were visitors, they contacted him by letter and made appointments, and anyone who visited off-schedule was sent home without mercy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7241\" data-end=\"7344\">Meanwhile, he often strolled in the front and back yard and practiced swordsmanship in the gymnasium.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7346\" data-end=\"7454\">Reluctantly, he felt disturbed by this situation, but he could relax simply by enjoying a peaceful future.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7456\" data-end=\"7495\">“I still don’t know. Should I do it?”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7497\" data-end=\"7558\">Harnette looked out the window and slowly opened her mouth.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7560\" data-end=\"7597\">The orange sunset slowly descended.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7599\" data-end=\"7678\">The sky received its color, and in a short time even the mansion was colored.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7680\" data-end=\"7759\">After the sun set, it would rise again tomorrow, but that too seemed in vain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7761\" data-end=\"7827\">“I could be wrong. Maybe it would be fine if I just stay quiet.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7829\" data-end=\"7874\">Zion answered calmly and tilted his teacup.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7876\" data-end=\"7940\">Of course, he had consulted Harnette before using this method.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7942\" data-end=\"8055\">However, Harnette was pessimistic and only added that if he wanted to try it, he should do so only in a crisis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8057\" data-end=\"8121\">“Huh… Don’t give in to my compulsion. You’re right this time.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8123\" data-end=\"8152\">Harnette had faced reality.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8154\" data-end=\"8296\">The longer they delayed, the more misunderstandings would accumulate, and pressure would eventually be placed on them in one way or another.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8298\" data-end=\"8426\">If you choose the king, the future is uncertain; if you choose the three princesses, you will be scrutinized until succession.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8428\" data-end=\"8497\">Ultimately, you have to choose one, but either choice carries risk.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8499\" data-end=\"8559\">“It doesn’t sound too unreasonable. Maybe I’m in a hurry.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8561\" data-end=\"8620\">“NO. I’m not in a hurry. If it’s late, we’ll lose money.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8622\" data-end=\"8710\">Even though she knew Zion’s decision was correct, she couldn’t accept it in her heart.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8712\" data-end=\"8867\">From now on, you won’t be trapped in a power structure, and even if someone threatens you, the Duke of Adelaira or the Marquis of Reggiard will help you.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8869\" data-end=\"8977\">No matter the title or the Setinos Quasar fee, it still felt uncomfortable for Zion to become the villain.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8979\" data-end=\"9031\">“Sorry. I shouldn’t have been a Cetinos Quasar… …”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9033\" data-end=\"9083\">“Don’t regret it. You didn’t do anything wrong.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9085\" data-end=\"9142\">Harnette slowly extended her hand and took Zion’s hand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9144\" data-end=\"9188\">Zion accepted it and touched it carefully.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9190\" data-end=\"9269\">“Does the title matter? You can get money again. I can do anything with you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9271\" data-end=\"9344\">Wealth, position, honor, origin, family, connections, and achievements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9346\" data-end=\"9412\">They are means to live happily, but cannot be the ultimate goal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9414\" data-end=\"9496\">Zion worked tirelessly for perfect peace and ultimately achieved what he wanted.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9498\" data-end=\"9573\">He had suffered for a long time, so now he had to protect and cherish it.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9575\" data-end=\"9647\">“I love you. I will love you until I die. No, I can love you forever.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9649\" data-end=\"9699\">Harnette murmured softly, making her lips smile.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9701\" data-end=\"9766\">Her orange hair mixed with the sunset, spreading bright colors.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9768\" data-end=\"9847\">Her golden eyes were full of sorrow, holding only the image of her companion.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9849\" data-end=\"9919\">“I love you too. I don’t think I can live a single day without you.”</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9921\" data-end=\"9971\">Zion rose from his seat and approached Harnette.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9973\" data-end=\"10023\">Then, slowly lowering his back, he moved closer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10025\" data-end=\"10088\">Harnette placed her hands on Zion’s back and kissed his lips.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10090\" data-end=\"10153\">Twilight crept in at some point, but neither of them stopped.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10155\" data-end=\"10258\">On the contrary, their desire for each other grew stronger, and the bed drew closer little by little.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10260\" data-end=\"10326\">As darkness fell, only harsh breaths and strange sounds emerged.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"10328\" data-end=\"10335\">—End—</p>\r\n</div>",
                };

                const int chapterPerVolume = 100;

                int skip = 180;

                int volume = 1;
                int chapter = 1;
                for (int i = 0; i < urls.Length; ++i) {
                    var url = urls[i];

                    Console.WriteLine($"{url}");

                    if (i >= skip) {
                        await brightnovel.DownloadChapter(url, @"D:\Visual Novels\[Self-Sourced] I Became the Fiance of a Crazy Heroine\Raw\" + $"Volume {volume}", $"{chapter.ToString("D4")}.xhtml");
                    }

                    if ((++chapter) > chapterPerVolume) {
                        ++volume;
                        chapter = 1;
                    }

                    if (i >= skip) {
                        Thread.Sleep(5000); // Cloudflare rate limiting
                    }
                }

                Console.WriteLine("Done!");
            });

            Console.ReadLine();

            return 0;
        }
    }
}